{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:28:25.139Z","ordinal":461861,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a183fa-0fb6-7221-af24-4451e0ebcb37","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-65b0f9e0-023b-4baf-b89a-56abb0dffa2e","process_id":"55633","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 300 --json comments,files --jq '{comments:[.comments[-4:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body:(.body|.[0:600])}],files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 300 --json comments,files --jq '{comments:[.comments[-4:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body:(.body|.[0:600])}],files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"claude-code **correction** to my ACCEPT above: I wrote that CI run 40720824591 \\\"succeeded\\\". That's wrong. It's still **in progress**: Node 22 and Node 24 passed, but `linux-x86_64` was still running at 16:21Z. The readiness record's own wording, which says the source gates ran on this revision, should be checked against that run's final conclusion before merge. My ACCEPT of the document's other content stands, on the condition that 40720824591 completes with success.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T16:21:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"An independent read-only review of the current PR head (`2b6490f7cbdda0fad8864b4867aab42d8013cb75`) found a documentation accuracy issue that should be corrected before approval:\\n\\n- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` still opens with a section labeled “Current release checkpoint” reporting an older `main` revision, while the appended checkpoint reports newer state. The opening status therefore remains misleading even though a later entry exists.\\n- The appended checkpoint is also stale against this PR's current observation: it says main CI is running and PR #302 is at `934ed912`, while live state has a\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T18:50:08Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review of exact head `a285ebedc449e6a64687bb763b3ecfac38f2e675` against `8580c821f57119768db01614d31cd60e8766468b` returned **CHANGES_REQUIRED** (diff SHA-256 `fa2bb1f4a849239a675ba7a515dccd354354ec0af25eb360dc14ff630f9cab46`).\\n\\n- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9` says run `40564959805` failed on an npm-version mismatch. GitHub records that run as success; its compare job completed successfully and compared the six selected artifacts, including `sbom.cdx.json`, with the published RC. Correct the failure and `REQ-REL-114` claims. This remains RC10-only evidence and does not pro\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T19:11:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only re-review of exact head `64ffe5ec275d755b61f0bdcff45fe3ef0b2a4d9f` against `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` returned **CHANGES_REQUIRED** (diff SHA-256 `7822120387384f94503ea17ec06eb82b91518dfd18259422c23855aa68e1857f`).\\n\\nThe prior RC10 reproducibility statement is corrected, and the exact-RC/source-gate distinction is clear. One mismatch remains at `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7`: it says PR #305’s Entire Gates check failed for lack of approval. GitHub’s final check conclusion is **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”), and ruleset 25340146 does not require En\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T19:19:44Z\"}],\"files\":[\"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":668640503}},"started_at_ms":1793215704469,"completed_at_ms":1793215705138}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:28:26.689Z","ordinal":461862,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a183fc-3641-7133-b512-4abddfdf4482","call_id":"call_c80a8175eb80499982ad208f83ce9c0b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"claude-code **correction** to my ACCEPT above: I wrote that CI run 40720824591 \\\"succeeded\\\". That's wrong. It's still **in progress**: Node 22 and Node 24 passed, but `linux-x86_64` was still running at 16:21Z. The readiness record's own wording, which says the source gates ran on this revision, should be checked against that run's final conclusion before merge. My ACCEPT of the document's other content stands, on the condition that 40720824591 completes with success.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T16:21:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"An independent read-only review of the current PR head (`2b6490f7cbdda0fad8864b4867aab42d8013cb75`) found a documentation accuracy issue that should be corrected before approval:\\n\\n- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` still opens with a section labeled “Current release checkpoint” reporting an older `main` revision, while the appended checkpoint reports newer state. The opening status therefore remains misleading even though a later entry exists.\\n- The appended checkpoint is also stale against this PR's current observation: it says main CI is running and PR #302 is at `934ed912`, while live state has a\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T18:50:08Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review of exact head `a285ebedc449e6a64687bb763b3ecfac38f2e675` against `8580c821f57119768db01614d31cd60e8766468b` returned **CHANGES_REQUIRED** (diff SHA-256 `fa2bb1f4a849239a675ba7a515dccd354354ec0af25eb360dc14ff630f9cab46`).\\n\\n- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9` says run `40564959805` failed on an npm-version mismatch. GitHub records that run as success; its compare job completed successfully and compared the six selected artifacts, including `sbom.cdx.json`, with the published RC. Correct the failure and `REQ-REL-114` claims. This remains RC10-only evidence and does not pro\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T19:11:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only re-review of exact head `64ffe5ec275d755b61f0bdcff45fe3ef0b2a4d9f` against `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` returned **CHANGES_REQUIRED** (diff SHA-256 `7822120387384f94503ea17ec06eb82b91518dfd18259422c23855aa68e1857f`).\\n\\nThe prior RC10 reproducibility statement is corrected, and the exact-RC/source-gate distinction is clear. One mismatch remains at `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7`: it says PR #305’s Entire Gates check failed for lack of approval. GitHub’s final check conclusion is **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”), and ruleset 25340146 does not require En\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T19:19:44Z\"}],\"files\":[\"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\"]}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a183fa-0fb6-7221-af24-4451e0ebcb37","create_time":1793215706.6893167}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
