rt behavior and tests, not requirement rows; the current-main run must still finish before claiming its exact-source gates passed. Source-stage evidence does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307's head was `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`; its actual merge commit is `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent source-review checks passed. Its Entire Gates check failed only because the review trail lacked approval; that check is not required by protected-branch ruleset 25340146, consistent with the documented PR #307 disposition. PR #302 was closed unmerged; PR #308 supersedes it at `41a63b4cfbd8c2ec40f384de28db4bea0faee49a` on base `8580c821`. At this observation, PR #308 Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed; Linux and Entire Gates were still running. PR #309 is at `65b4e1d9e379b630dc33acc714b7cbfa4e17fc6b` on base `8580c821`; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. PR #300's prior head `a285ebedc449e6a64687bb763b3ecfac38f2e675` had Node 22/24 in progress and JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; this readiness correction merges current main and requires fresh exact-head checks. Source PR checks are separate from release qualification.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) completed successfully (all jobs passed) for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence artifact reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for the six compared outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The current requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; ledger disposition remains for its owner to reconcile. RC10 evidence applies only to RC10 and does not establish cross-runner qualification for a successor RC. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest custodian status request is unanswered as of 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC. Held-out custody acceptance and T2/T3/T4 qualification therefore remain unverified. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; no genuine operator cell results are recorded. Remaining standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, human terminal, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n    12\t\n    13\tThe checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence; their source revision, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this observation.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 16:25 UTC; superseded)\n64ffe5ec275d755b61f0bdcff45fe3ef0b2a4d9f\n13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":930670290}},"started_at_ms":1793216514298,"completed_at_ms":1793216515229}}
