{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:42:08.280Z","ordinal":462285,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18405-0795-7761-83bc-7e851bfd6fd4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d2b80326-a3f7-479e-84d4-8fda8695c4e4","process_id":"3965","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '7,11p' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '7,11p' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md","name":"READINESS.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307's head was `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`; its actual merge commit is `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent source-review checks passed. Its Entire Gates check failed only because the review trail lacked approval; that check is not required by protected-branch ruleset 25340146, consistent with the documented PR #307 disposition. PR #302 was closed unmerged; PR #308 supersedes it at `41a63b4cfbd8c2ec40f384de28db4bea0faee49a` on base `8580c821`. At this observation, PR #308 Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed; Linux and Entire Gates were still running. PR #309 is at `65b4e1d9e379b630dc33acc714b7cbfa4e17fc6b` on base `8580c821`; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. PR #300's prior head `a285ebedc449e6a64687bb763b3ecfac38f2e675` had Node 22/24 in progress and JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; this readiness correction merges current main and requires fresh exact-head checks. Source PR checks are separate from release qualification.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) completed successfully (all jobs passed) for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence artifact reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for the six compared outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The current requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; ledger disposition remains for its owner to reconcile. RC10 evidence applies only to RC10 and does not establish cross-runner qualification for a successor RC. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest custodian status request is unanswered as of 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC. Held-out custody acceptance and T2/T3/T4 qualification therefore remain unverified. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; no genuine operator cell results are recorded. Remaining standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, human terminal, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":911021925}},"started_at_ms":1793216527368,"completed_at_ms":1793216528280}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:42:09.741Z","ordinal":462286,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18408-c54c-7723-8b62-b822cc1bb028","call_id":"call_7ec1f0e683e84daf8192e0e63c4ae801","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307's head was `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`; its actual merge commit is `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent source-review checks passed. Its Entire Gates check failed only because the review trail lacked approval; that check is not required by protected-branch ruleset 25340146, consistent with the documented PR #307 disposition. PR #302 was closed unmerged; PR #308 supersedes it at `41a63b4cfbd8c2ec40f384de28db4bea0faee49a` on base `8580c821`. At this observation, PR #308 Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed; Linux and Entire Gates were still running. PR #309 is at `65b4e1d9e379b630dc33acc714b7cbfa4e17fc6b` on base `8580c821`; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. PR #300's prior head `a285ebedc449e6a64687bb763b3ecfac38f2e675` had Node 22/24 in progress and JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; this readiness correction merges current main and requires fresh exact-head checks. Source PR checks are separate from release qualification.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) completed successfully (all jobs passed) for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence artifact reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for the six compared outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The current requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; ledger disposition remains for its owner to reconcile. RC10 evidence applies only to RC10 and does not establish cross-runner qualification for a successor RC. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest custodian status request is unanswered as of 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC. Held-out custody acceptance and T2/T3/T4 qualification therefore remain unverified. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; no genuine operator cell results are recorded. Remaining standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, human terminal, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18405-0795-7761-83bc-7e851bfd6fd4","create_time":1793216529.7409837}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
