{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:45:13.295Z","ordinal":462376,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18405-0795-7761-83bc-7e851bfd6fd4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae250c85fdc81a0a8958524804c9319","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The fresh independent review found a real gap in the new regression: `git add file[ab].txt` treats brackets as a Git pathspec pattern, so it may not stage the literal bracketed filename the test intends. I confirmed the line in the rebased candidate. I’m correcting the test to stage that exact literal path; I’ll let the current full-suite runs finish before pushing the new head, to avoid starting overlapping suites. XERJ confirmed the repository’s test conventions, and I verified against the exact PR source because its index is older."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793216712431,"completed_at_ms":1793216713295}}
