{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:46:05.103Z","ordinal":462422,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1840c-5cae-7d82-99e6-f2ff83d7fe5c","call_id":"call_241151e6aea0493c952baba2e6f78868","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — PR #308 exact head `aa86c943f9f2326912c12f87b9a2bece65feb914` against base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. The unified patch SHA-256 is `9b8e1e2723b9168e5cfd7c34fce4cd05e7dbe84bf6c25e29c97e9b673d297ca1`, matching the requested hash.\\n\\nThe changed files are limited to `checkpoint.ts` and its two restore tests. The ignore check invokes Git with an argument array, `--no-index`, and a `./`-anchored escaped path; failures other than “not ignored” fail closed at the restore preflight ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:44), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:169)). Tests cover pathspec-looking filenames, ignored descendants, and preserving the index and workspace on rejected restores ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:151), [checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1931)).\\n\\nRestore validates write/removal targets before changing the index, limits index updates to a nested workspace when applicable, and checks nested-repository and ignored-path obstructions before mutation ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:200), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1271)). I reviewed source and tests without running them; hosted CI remains separate evidence. No actionable finding in this review. I kept the disposition tied to the exact revision and did not treat it as release qualification. citeMEMORY.md:777-779\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18405-0795-7761-83bc-7e851bfd6fd4","create_time":1793216765.1029694}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
