{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:56:02.282Z","ordinal":462773,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18413-b547-7920-8748-309358a4fc4e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e5d8fe5d-ea22-49c1-9eae-da892223c387","process_id":"91979","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"entire|Approvals|Unresolved findings\" .github AGENTS.md docs scripts package.json --hidden 2>/dev/null | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n \"entire|Approvals|Unresolved findings\" .github AGENTS.md docs scripts package.json --hidden 2>/dev/null | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"AGENTS.md:25:<!-- entire-agent:begin -->\nAGENTS.md:26:Read .entire/agent-guide.md for this repository's workflow, source inspection, and verification guidance.\nAGENTS.md:27:@.entire/agent-guide.md\nAGENTS.md:28:<!-- entire-agent:end -->\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:27:`FlightRecorder.appendEvent()` is the single event persistence boundary. It sanitizes the entire event payload before constructing and appending the JSON line. If classification/sanitization fails, it returns a safe `recordingSkipped` event result without writing that record or propagating classifier diagnostics; authorized local execution continues. Session metadata, prompts, thoughts, tool arguments, result snippets, errors, durable state, diffs, and arbitrary nested payload fields all pass through this boundary.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:33:**Verifier runs bypass the gate entirely (VER-01).** Before the first edit (change baseline, `agent.ts:1602-1617`) and at every `task_completed` (`agent.ts:3432-3436`), Nexus runs the repository's own test command (`make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest`, chosen by `tester.ts:113-136`) through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These calls skip `dispatchToolCall`, so even review mode never asks, and no workspace-trust check applies. Opening a hostile repo and approving one `edit_file` therefore runs that repo's arbitrary test script on the host. `/test` and `nexus eval` run `execSync` on the host, bypassing the sandbox and blocking the event loop (VER-14).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:21:Both results are on tuned tasks. The following are missing entirely:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:117:| Stop loading the project `.env` entirely | Breaks the documented per-project endpoint/model workflow (CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md). An allowlist keeps it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:70:| REQ-TUI-10 | B7/F1-F3 | Approvals cannot be decided by stray typing; approve-all deliberate | TOP_TIER B7; USER_MANUAL Approvals | **ACCEPTED WITH DEFECTS** (independent round 5, NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:165,259); 028ca90 follow-up implementer-verified only | Y (round 5), N (follow-up) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:58:| AGT-15 | S4 | Persistence cost | state.ts recordProgress/recordOperationStart/End (load+redact+fsync rewrite of entire task JSON incl. messages) | INFERENCE/MEASUREMENT gap. ≥3 full-state rewrites per tool call, each O(conversation) with redaction scan and fsync. | Latency on long conversations / slow disks. | Measure (see §6). |\ndocs/WP04_CORRECTION_VERIFICATION.md:88:- **Vulnerability:** Non-Git directory walking used `dirent.isFile()`, ignoring symlinks entirely. Non-standard filesystem objects were not explicitly rejected.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:52:  - Approvals cannot be decided by stray typing.\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:189:6. **Thin presentation and rehearsal:** run the entire flow several times from reset fixtures, capture failure/recovery behavior, prepare a 5–10 minute script/video and reproducible instructions. The recording must show actual service and repository activity, not playback dressed as live execution.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:19:2. **Subprocess Ambient Authority & Unmediated Network Egress (F-02):** While `DATA-001..009` govern data crossing configured boundaries at the model/API layer, they fail to constrain subprocess execution (`linux_command_execute`). Subprocesses (package managers, compilers, curl, build scripts) execute with ambient network access and read access to the entire host filesystem under the current sandbox (`--ro-bind / /`), providing an unmediated exfiltration path.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:101:|  |  - In-process Plugins (CRITICAL: Currently shares entire runtime domain)   |  |\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:270:  1. In `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (lines 133–146), `bwrap` mounts the entire host root filesystem read-only: `--ro-bind / / --remount-ro /`.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:299:  2. In `cli/src/security.ts` (lines 176–182), `restore` performs a global substring replacement across the entire string without verifying destination, caller, or context: `restored.replaceAll(placeholder, secret)`.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:425:- **Reviewer Recommendation:** Mandate that all subprocess execution utilize separate process groups (`setpgid`) and terminate the entire process group (`kill(-pgid, SIGKILL)`) on timeout, cancellation, or error.\ndocs/enhancement-opportunities.md:271:**Differentiation:** Extends AI coding from local development to the entire software delivery pipeline.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:954:All normative architecture and security contracts were settled during Phase 2. The implementation decomposition choices—including evaluating race-resistant containment mechanisms (`DEC-01`), evaluating candidate identity representations (`DEC-02`), and deferring Ratatui (`DEC-03`)—fall entirely within engineering authority under the accepted requirements. Neither `DEC-01` nor `DEC-02` constitutes an operator policy choice; both remain open engineering implementation hypotheses to be validated empirically during their respective increments.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:30:7. **Blanket Fail-Closed Grouping Paralyzing Autonomy (Finding IR-07, MATERIAL):** `FAIL-002` groups six diverse controls into a blanket \"MUST FAIL CLOSED (halt execution, deny invocation, or refuse merge)\", which would cause verifier timeouts or token rehydration misses to abort the entire agent process rather than localized containment and autonomous recovery.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:216:- **Exact Problematic Wording:** In `SUBP-004`: *\"On task cancellation or timeout, the system MUST terminate the entire process group or container, leaving zero detached background orphan processes.\"*\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:217:- **Why It Matters:** The underlying architectural invariant is that Nexus must own and track the lifecycle of task-spawned execution so that cancellation or timeout terminates all task-owned descendant execution. Dictating that it MUST use \"the entire process group or container\" prematurely prescribes Unix `setpgid`/`kill(-pgid)` or Linux container namespaces into the requirements contract. On other platforms (e.g., Windows Job Objects) or environments where process groups are restricted, other tracking mechanisms satisfy the lifecycle ownership invariant.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:234:- **Why It Matters:** `FAIL-002` bunches six fundamentally different controls into a single compound parenthetical `(halt execution, deny invocation, or refuse merge)`. Without explicit assignment, an implementer could interpret this as requiring the system to halt the entire agent execution if a single verifier times out, or if an invalid rehydration token is encountered. In an autonomous engineering system, a verifier failure MUST refuse merge and report failure back to the agent so it can replan and self-correct! Halting execution aborts the autonomous task loop.\ndocs/PHASE3_CORRECTIONS_VERIFICATION.md:221:| Standalone `\bRESOLVED\b` on DEC-01/02 | **NOT FOUND (CLEAN)** | Zero occurrences in entire document. |\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:109:**Approvals.** The sidecar blocks on `approval.request` until it receives `approve`, `deny`, or `cancel` for that `id`. Only one approval is outstanding at a time.\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:30:With WP-05 now fully implemented, independently falsified, and explicitly **OPERATOR ACCEPTED**, this assessment reconciles the entire original 122-requirement normative contract against the new accepted baseline.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:102:- **Approvals.** A panel sized to its content states what is proposed and on which target (`Proposed: create\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:117:  the terminal (Esc still denies), and timing starts again when it is drawn. Approvals that arrive while another panel\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:142:4. Two non-context faults (input loss, unpassable verifier) were sufficient to produce the entire failure pattern.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md:104:- In both cases the \"reconstruction\" is **replay of the entire stored transcript** into context. There is no way to rebuild a smaller working context from durable state. (OBSERVED.)\ndocs/WP02_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:200:  2. Forbid subshell execution and command substitution entirely under read-only mode, or parse commands into discrete argv tokens and validate each token against an explicit immutable utility allowlist without shell execution.\ndocs/cloudflare/AGENT_COLLABORATION_EXPERIMENT_3_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:38:5. **Historical and present authority must stay separate.** Retained state branch history includes earlier collaboration state and an older asynchronous store implementation. Its JSON points to E3's exact baseline and separate producer candidate; the integrated producer is correctly baseline-derived and README-only. Do not treat the state ref's entire source tree, prior experiment `main`, or prior accepted worker results as the E3 candidate. Likewise, a local remote-tracking ref is not fresh verification of today's live Artifact ref.\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_REVIEW_PACKAGE_2026-10-02.md:135:privilege. First inspect this entire document and the bundle. Use a fresh\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:30:- **Approvals and slash commands** are phase 3. The sidecar runs in `auto` mode, so approvals do not occur; if one arrives anyway the transcript says so and Esc cancels the turn.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2586:    (\"\", \"Approvals (review mode)\"),\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-sidecar-protocol.md:342:4. Delete the entire `function buildConfig(options: any): HarnessConfig { ... }` definition (currently lines 52–99). Leave every `buildConfig(options)` call site as is.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-sidecar-protocol.md:1063:### Task 5: Approvals, cancellation, slash, shutdown\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:301:## 14. Unresolved findings (not fixed here)\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:24:| 13 | Approvals | Modal leaves transcript text visible in its margins; file changes use the old plain diff colouring; decisions only in the border (10) | Full panel, target and kind stated, diffs rendered with the shared diff component, decision buttons with a visible focus; buffered keys and pastes cannot decide | PASS at `804c5df` — screen 10 (from `83e7405`); `approval_decisions_have_a_visible_focus…`, `input_queued_when_an_approval_opens…`; PTY `tui_approval_input_e2e`. At `83e7405` this row was **not** met: a delayed burst approved an action (see Approval input below) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:44:| O6 | Approvals: input typed before a panel appears | BY DESIGN, disclosed — text typed while the agent works, before any panel exists, is steering (shown in the transcript), even if the operator meant it as an answer. It never decides an approval. When the TUI is stalled, whether such input is read before or after the approval event depends on when the sidecar reader thread delivers the event. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc-2026-10-21/logs/t2-bugfix-csv-1/agent.stdout.json:187:    \"No test changes were made. The fix is entirely in csv.js.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc-2026-10-21/logs/t2-bugfix-csv-2/agent.stdout.json:187:    \"No test changes were made. The fix is entirely in csv.js.\",\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1467:All normative architectural requirements and data-security policies were authoritatively settled during Phase 2 and operator-accepted. The execution parameters established in this document—including the evaluation protocols for `DEC-01` and `DEC-02`, the 11 work-package boundaries, and the deferral of `DEC-03`—fall entirely within engineering implementation authority. No operator policy intervention is required to proceed with implementation.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:24:- Impact: an operator who chose review mode to stay in control can lose the entire repository, including uncommitted work and git history,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:67:  provider keys in the environment. Read-only mode and the bwrap sandbox (which only wrap `run_command`) are bypassed entirely.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_false_verified.test.ts:20:  // The suite tests something else entirely; nothing covers math.js.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":389837888}},"started_at_ms":1793217361891,"completed_at_ms":1793217362282}}
