: r1/vulnerability-scanning/SKILL.md)\n- walkthrough-video: Generate (file: r1/walkthrough-video/SKILL.md)\n- wcag-audit-patterns: Conduct  (file: r1/wcag-audit-patterns/SKILL.md)\n- web-artifacts-builder: Suite of (file: r1/web-artifacts-builder/SKILL.md)\n- web-performance-audit: Conduct  (file: r1/web-performance-audit/SKILL.md)\n- web-performance-optimization: Optimize w (file: r1/web-performance-optimization/SKILL.md)\n- webapp-testing: Toolkit fo (file: r1/webapp-testing/SKILL.md)\n- what-happened: Explain  (file: r1/what-happened/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create,  (file: r9/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, in (file: r9/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, (file: r9/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n- writing-plans: Use when (file: r1/writing-plans/SKILL.md)\n- writing-skills: Use when c (file: r1/writing-skills/SKILL.md)\n- youtube-transcript: Download Y (file: r1/youtube-transcript/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nIn Default mode, strongly prefer making reasonable assumptions and executing the user's request rather than stopping to ask questions.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ctools\u003e\nDeferred tool namespaces:\n- mcp__codex_apps__chatgpt_space: Read, search, create, and edit pages and spaces in ChatGPT Space, within your current account.\n- mcp__codex_apps__codex_document_control: Use Codex Document Control to find connected document sessions, inspect the tools supported by a selected session, and execute one supported tool against that session. Call `list_document_sessions` first to choose the intended connected session, c...\n- mcp__codex_apps__github: Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\n- mcp__codex_apps__google_drive: Search and work with files from Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides.\n- mcp__codex_apps__hotline: Look up local helpline information for the user based on country inferred from the conversation. You must use this tool before providing a suicide or self-harm helpline; do not use web search or guess.\n- mcp__codex_apps__pets: Create and manage the user's animated companion pets inside ChatGPT Work mode. Use only for ChatGPT Pets, not real-world animal advice, generic pet images, or pets in other apps.\n- mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management: Manage plugins, settings, permissions, and connections. Prefer available built-in tools or connected plugins when they fit the task. Proactively search for plugins when an external app, account, or service would materially help, even if the user d...\n- mcp__codex_apps__search_service: Tool for accessing the internet.\n- mcp__codex_apps__sites: Use Sites to build or modify websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals, trackers, hubs, and internal tools. Use Sites skills for local implementation, source preparation, and artifact packaging. Use this connector for site...\n- mcp__faultline\n- mcp__mcp_agent_mail: You are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format...\n- mcp__mcp_search\n- mcp__xerj: XERJ tools proxy to a running XERJ engine (ES-compatible). Use xerj_search for retrieval — pass `query` as a plain string for definition-first code search (ranks the defining file first, returns the matching passage instead of whole files, and add...\n\u003c/tools\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Codex Security (codex-security@openai-curated-remote)\n- Figma (figma@openai-curated-remote)\n- Gmail (gmail@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- Notion (notion@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Email (outlook-email@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n- Teams (teams@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a18428-01d0-7db3-9c29-7f08b9a4a9ef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","tools.deferred_namespaces","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a18422-99d5-74d1-8392-e2c348b8135f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"`.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a18428-01d0-7db3-9c29-7f18a5d6d4a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a18422-99d5-74d1-8392-e2c348b8135f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a18428-01d0-7db3-9c29-7f25eb01de1a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a18422-99d5-74d1-8392-e2c348b8135f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"# AGENTS.md instructions for /home/mike/nexus-code\n\n\u003cINSTRUCTIONS\u003e\n## XERJ (code search)\n\nThis project uses XERJ for reference coding. Before writing code that touches\nunfamiliar territory: `xerj def \"\u003csymbol\u003e\"` for go-to-definition, or\n`xerj search \"\u003cplain words\u003e\"` for ranked, definition-first passages.\nIndex each repo under its own prefix: `xerj autoindex \u003cfolder\u003e --prefix \u003cname\u003e`, then\npass the same `--prefix \u003cname\u003e` to `xerj search` and `xerj def` (without it they search\nthe default `ax` prefix). Cite file:line for anything you rely on.\nAfter using xerj, send the field report automatically with `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"YOUR_MODEL\" --used-for \"WHAT_YOU_DID\" --verdict \"WHAT_WORKED_AND_WHAT_DID_NOT\"` (or the MCP `xerj_field_report` tool); no need to ask the user. It opens a GitHub PR first and falls back to POST https://xerj.org/api/field-report only when GitHub is unavailable. `--disable-feedback` or `XERJ_DISABLE_FEEDBACK=true` opts out.\n\n## XERJ on this host\n\n- **Node:** `http://localhost:9200`, the default URL, so no `XERJ_URL` is needed. It runs as the systemd user service `xerj` (`systemctl --user status xerj`). Its data lives in `~/xerj-data`.\n- **Restarting:** use `systemctl --user restart xerj`. Never start a second node on 9200, and never `pkill xerj`.\n- **Prefixes.** Always pass one with `--prefix`:\n\n  | Prefix | Contents |\n  |---|---|\n  | `nexus-cli` | Nexus Code `cli/src` at `origin/main` |\n  | `nexus-core` | `core/src` |\n  | `nexus-test` | `cli/test` |\n  | `nexus-docs` | `docs` |\n  | `goose`, `opencode` | Peer agent harnesses: reference checkouts in `~/nexus-reference-20261025/`, indexed 2026-10-25 |\n\n- **Nexus freshness:** the `nexus-*` indices are rebuilt hourly from committed `origin/main` only, by the `xerj-refresh-nexus.timer` user timer. The indexed commit is in `~/xerj-sources/nexus-code/.origin-main-sha`. For a PR head or uncommitted work, use `git grep` / `git show \u003csha\u003e:\u003cpath\u003e` instead.\n- **Search is lexical (BM25).** Use the words that appear in the code. Dotted identifiers such as `core.hooksPath` match as one token.\n- **Never index:**\n  - `eval/`\n  - held-out tasks or payloads\n  - credentials, or `~/.nexus`, `~/.codex` or `~/.claude` state\n\n  Index only folders you are allowed to read, under a new prefix that doesn't start with an existing one.\n- **Never delete or replace indices you didn't create.**\n- **Field reports are allowed for public/open-source work.** Preview with `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `--submit`. Keep private data, paths of private repos and secrets out of them.\n- **Don't use `rerank`.** It sends document text to a third party.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n# Project Guidelines \u0026 Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n\n\u003c/INSTRUCTIONS\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/home/mike/nexus-code\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-28\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eEtc/UTC\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/home/mike/nexus-code\u003c/root\u003e\u003croot\u003e/home/mike/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/18/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"disabled\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"unrestricted\" /\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n  \u003csubagents\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/acceptance_stage_clarification\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/context_rc_gate_audit\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/pr207_independent_review\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/pr74_77_stalled_review_lane\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/pr9_reconciliation\" /\u003e\n  \u003c/subagents\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a18428-01d0-7db3-9c29-7f3dd7868344","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a18422-99d5-74d1-8392-e2c348b8135f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_6c91e4d7099e4fba93013cc2ffe1f665\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"Entire shows the logged-in identity as Mike Holownych (the PR author), so it cannot count as independent approval. How should we arrange the required distinct reviewer?\",\"answer\":\"It's a single user repo. There is no one else.\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a1832d-cafa-7081-9f07-6969653c4b5e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1793202178.810596,"turn_id":"01a1832d-46fa-7b02-b655-c652a6a9162d"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":false,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a14cb3-440f-7013-8eb9-a4ae5852b58f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a14cb3-41e5-7801-aa32-9255177a52a9"},"revision":"retained_01a14cb3-4410-7c10-9ca2-74ccb1b912dc"},"user_input_order":0},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":false,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a14cbb-b1ac-7340-a0b3-41ae35060e47","role":"user","turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14a-7783-b5cf-c72089b0073b"},"revision":"retained_01a14cbb-b1ad-7061-ad4d-aea548917e87"},"user_input_order":17},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14a-7783-b5cf-c72089b0073b","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"register_agent"},{"first_turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14a-7783-b5cf-c72089b0073b","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"send_message"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":false,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a14cd4-5a5f-7992-b8df-77fb86c018d6","role":"user","turn_id":"01a14cd4-59f8-7720-a95a-13c578c1cd28"},"revision":"retained_01a14cd4-5a5f-7992-b8df-7811e8b7492a"},"user_input_order":56},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14a-7783-b5cf-c72089b0073b","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"register_agent"},{"first_turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14a-7783-b5cf-c72089b0073b","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"send_message"},{"first_turn_id":"01a14cd4-59f8-7720-a95a-13c578c1cd28","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"request_contact"},{"first_turn_id":"01a14cd4-59f8-7720-a95a-13c578c1cd28","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_inbox"},{"first_turn_id":"01a14cd4-59f8-7720-a95a-13c578c1cd28","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"list_contacts"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":false,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a14e58-17ec-7203-bb0d-5bc55c23603e","role":"user","turn_id":"01a14e58-1753-7d33-ae87-c1f74cb2b16e"},"revision":"retained_01a14e58-17ed-7e30-9e04-c5695934eb7a"},"user_input_order":155},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a14cbb-b14