{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:16:27.017Z","ordinal":463340,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18428-2989-76d3-94c9-91709a5f4a2f","call_id":"call_5323e97ca9584481833a9c7baeb6e6fd","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\nRead this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is true. Params: list, includeClosed. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read(args: {\n  // Also show done and dropped items and closed lists\n  includeClosed?: boolean;\n  // Read only this list\n  list?: string;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```\nmcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\nYour canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call appends one entry to a list. To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...details}. State on the list itself: any other fields (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list). Returns what is still open in the list. Params: list (required), fields (required"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18422-99d5-74d1-8392-e2c348b8135f","create_time":1793218587.0177984}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
