{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:21:17.784Z","ordinal":463506,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1842c-9958-7e71-ac2b-19a65452d5c6","call_id":"call_682c964d3375483280ff470f0c170413","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"2fb069d455686d2b1d37497d44d9f0401e219231\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n**Owner decision, 2026-10-18:** the sealed T2 corpus keeps its legacy hidden tests (`hidden: {dir, command}`). They run **hardened, SWE-bench style**. The alternatives were re-authoring the tasks as blackbox-v1 or accepting the legacy tests as-is; both were rejected. The corpus and its `50895b84` seal are unchanged. See `eval/README.md`, \\\"Hardened legacy hidden tests\\\".\\n\\n- **Never in the agent's workspace.** In qualification, or with `hardenedChecks: true`, a legacy hidden check never runs where the agent worked. The task is staged again, using the same pin or fixture and the same setup, and the fresh tree is verified to equal the baseline tree. Only the agent's **source** changes are copied in.\\n- **Test infrastructure is discarded.** This covers test files and directories, `conftest.py`, pytest/tox/`setup.cfg`, `sitecustomize.py`/`.pth`, jest/vitest/mocha/karma/babel config, `_test.go` files (and therefore `TestMain`), `build.rs`, `.cargo/`, `.github/`, `Makefile` and `.env*`. Symlinks are discarded too.\\n- **Test-runner config changes refuse the checks.** A change to test-runner configuration inside `package.json`, `pyproject.toml` or `Cargo.toml` refuses both the hidden and the regression check.\\n- **Separate, read-only oracle.** The hidden command runs with the hidden directory **mounted read-only**. The regression command runs in a **separate** identical copy, so code executed by one check cannot prepare the other.\\n- **No disclosure.** In qualification, hidden-test output is reduced to status, byte count and sha256.\\n- **Corpus binding.** The custodian's heldout-v2 manifest schema is bound through `task_sha256` and `hidden_sha256`, using the custodian's exact algorithm, with an exact population check. Custody is a frozen `corpusCustody {custodian, approvedAt, reportSha256}` in the config. This resolves codex-lead's 11:11:30Z boundary request.\\n\\n**Residual risk, documented:** candidate source still executes inside the hidden test process, as in other SWE-bench-style evaluations.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `eval_hardened`, `eval_integrity`, `eval_harness` and `eval_t3` pass **45/45, 0 skipped** locally, with a CI-equivalent dedicated tmpfs mounted temporarily.\\n- End-to-end: a correct fix passes in a fresh workspace. A wrong fix that also rewrites `scripts.test` to `exit 0` and adds a `test/` file is **refused**: hidden and regression both fail, the test file is discarded and the change is recorded.\\n- The binding was checked against the real committed `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (`50895b84…`). It reaches the custody and population checks, so the hash scheme matches. The digest equals an independent `find | sort | sha256sum` pipeline.\\n- No held-out payload was read.\\n\\n## Needs\\n\\n- Independent review.\\n- Before T2 qualification: a frozen `corpusCustody` in `eval/configs/v1-t2-*.json`, plus the installed RC and the provisioned host.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/plan-10-pr-10m-hardened\",\"headRefOid\":\"0c161e88e177389f688734076437992610a9ccda\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNKNOWN\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-18T18:15:09Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39153235793/job/117751037367\",\"name\":\"cloudflare-contest-contract\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-18T18:14:22Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-18T18:15