{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:33:19.201Z","ordinal":463832,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18432-af9c-7882-80ce-70535521cb1b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0cbe8c15-76e0-40e9-b831-48fb8eebbfcf","process_id":"12955","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-code grep -n -E 'eval_hardened|validateTask|qualification' origin/main -- scripts eval | head -100; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code ls-tree --name-only origin/main | head -60"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-code grep -n -E 'eval_hardened|validateTask|qualification' origin/main -- scripts eval | head -100; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code ls-tree --name-only origin/main | head -60"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:eval/README.md:1:# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\norigin/main:eval/README.md:7:runner source for evaluator behavior added after that revision. Neither document represents completed M5 qualification.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:19:those commands execute against the candidate workspace after the agent exits and are **not safe for qualification**, because\norigin/main:eval/README.md:29:hashes when qualification is configured, executable version, budgets, host and Node version. Each result records the\norigin/main:eval/README.md:117:A config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\norigin/main:eval/README.md:129:  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\norigin/main:eval/README.md:148:- **Corpus binding is integrity evidence, not approval authentication.** The qualification config pins the exact\norigin/main:eval/README.md:156:  archived by the acceptance reviewer before any qualification run. The current candidate task package has not been\norigin/main:eval/README.md:163:binds. Black-box qualification keeps oracle expectations outside candidate namespaces. Legacy hidden commands share a\norigin/main:eval/README.md:164:process with candidate code and are rejected during qualification preflight. The hardened legacy path below is only for\norigin/main:eval/README.md:165:development and pilot scoring; it is not qualification evidence. Aggregate CPU, memory, process-count and\norigin/main:eval/README.md:172:code in the same process as the oracle. They do not meet the qualification boundary, even when hardened. Qualification\norigin/main:eval/README.md:173:preflight accepts only the isolated `blackbox-v1` protocol. Any legacy task in a qualification corpus must be replaced\norigin/main:eval/README.md:221:provide independent qualification. `qualification: true` rejects every legacy hidden command before any candidate\norigin/main:eval/README.md:222:starts. Do not relabel legacy evidence as qualification evidence.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:269:  these controls are unsupported for qualification; they must not fall back to process-only or best-effort limits.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:279:- Preflight runs a contained probe and refuses qualification unless this host applies and cleans up the contract. CI\norigin/main:eval/README.md:284:The frozen qualification config sets the limit values. They must be recorded before the first scored run and must not\norigin/main:eval/README.md:300:  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:3:This directory is the reviewable procedure for preparing the host that runs `eval/run.mjs` for v1 qualification\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:19:- `/usr/bin/bwrap` must report upstream version 0.12.0 or later (CVE-2026-87766). `validate.mjs` cannot detect distro backports, so it also rejects older vendor-patched builds. Ubuntu 24.04 `0.9.0-1ubuntu0.3` removed the fix. Install a release with the fix before qualification; `scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh` shows the pinned source build that CI uses. `provision.sh` does not replace the binary.\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:26:node eval/host/validate.mjs --heldout <sealed task store> --json docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ).json\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:71:  the run record before each qualification window. If that load grows, the box can reach swap.\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:82:   (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) before the first qualification run.\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:83:3. **After freeze.** Values never change in response to qualification outcomes. A change for any reason after the\norigin/main:eval/host/bubblewrap.mjs:1:// Minimum Bubblewrap for the qualification host. Releases before 0.12.0 are affected by CVE-2026-87766\norigin/main:eval/host/provision.sh:2:# Provision the qualification host (eval/host/README.md). Run as root on the qualification host only:\norigin/main:eval/host/provision.sh:145:Description=Nexus qualification workspace root (size-capped tmpfs)\norigin/main:eval/host/rollback.sh:69:echo \"rolled back qualification host provisioning\"\norigin/main:eval/host/validate.mjs:2:// Infrastructure-only validation of a provisioned qualification host (eval/host/README.md). Run as the operator:\norigin/main:eval/host/validate.mjs:123:await check(\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\", () => {\norigin/main:eval/host/validate.mjs:130:      qualification: true,\norigin/main:eval/host/validate.mjs:136:    }, HELD_OUT) ?? \"\"), \"qualification preflight must reject protected corpus paths under unconditional host mounts\");\norigin/main:eval/host/validate.mjs:137:    const base = { name: \"failclosed\", qualification: true, endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:9/v1\", model: \"m\", runAs: ACCOUNT, sandboxRuntimePaths: [], sandboxRuntimeRoots: [\"/opt/nexus-qual\"] };\norigin/main:eval/oracle.mjs:1:// Black-box qualification oracle: expected values stay in the evaluator process and are never mounted into candidate\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:13:import { asUserSpec, corpusManifestProblem, corpusTaskRows, fetchModelEntry, hiddenTestIsolationProblem, modelFingerprint, nexusContextLimitArgs, nexusLimitsProblem, qualificationBudgetProblem, runtimeCorpusOverlapProblem, taskTreeDigest, validateTask } from \"./validate.mjs\";\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:46:  const includeParent = config.qualification === true || fs.realpathSync(parent) !== fs.realpathSync(evalDir);\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:87:if (config.qualification === true && only) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:88:  console.error(\"eval/run.mjs: qualification task subsets are forbidden; use a frozen corpus run or an explicitly recorded infrastructure-pair rerun\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:91:if (config.qualification === true && config.proxy === false) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:92:  console.error(\"eval/run.mjs: qualification requires the authenticated per-run model proxy\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:103:// A run is valid only with well-formed tasks, hidden tests the agent cannot read, and (for qualification) a model\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:106:  return validateTask(task, dir, { qualification: config.qualification === true }).map((p) => `${id}: ${p}`);\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:111:if (config.resources !== undefined && config.qualification !== true) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:116:if (config.qualification === true) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:120:if (config.qualification === true && config.sampling?.temperature !== 0) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:121:  problems.push(\"qualification adapters require sampling.temperature=0 so the matched Nexus, Goose and OpenCode runs use the same deterministic setting\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:123:if (config.qualification === true) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:124:  const budgetProblem = qualificationBudgetProblem(config);\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:137:    if (config.qualification === true && (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\") {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:155:  qualificationCorpus: config.qualification === true ? { manifestSha256: config.corpusManifestSha256, tasks: frozenTaskRows } : null,\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:250:    // Legacy hidden tests share a process with candidate code. In qualification (or with hardenedChecks) they never\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:253:    const hardened = (config.qualification === true || config.hardenedChecks === true) && task.hidden?.protocol !== \"blackbox-v1\";\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:345:    if (config.qualification === true) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:347:        return { record: null, problem: \"qualification requires nexusExecutable to be the absolute path of the installed RC\" };\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:350:        return { record: null, problem: \"qualification requires expectedAgentVersion to pin the installed RC\" };\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:353:        return { record: null, problem: \"qualification requires nexusPackageSha256 from the installed RC release asset\" };\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:358:          return { record: null, problem: \"qualification must use the installed RC, not the checkout cli/dist/index.js\" };\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:371:  const required = config.qualification === true || config.expectedAgentVersion !== undefined;\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:440:      ...(agent === \"nexus\" && config.qualification === true ? { packageSha256: config.nexusPackageSha256 } : {}),\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:534:  if (task.tier !== \"T4\" || (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || config.qualification !== true || !config.resources) {\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:535:    throw new Error(\"sigterm_resume requires an installed Nexus qualification run with the kernel resource contract\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:571:  if (config.qualification === true && !config.runAs) throw new Error(\"qualification candidate execution requires the dedicated evaluator account\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:594:   