{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:33:30.720Z","ordinal":463845,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18432-af9c-7882-80ce-70535521cb1b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a18432-af9c-7882-80ce-70535521cb1b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae25c183e2081a09c8b63fe121b9132","usage":{"input_tokens":152073,"cached_input_tokens":150016,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":170,"reasoning_output_tokens":34,"total_tokens":152243},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3401978,"cached_input_tokens":3379072,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5149,"reasoning_output_tokens":2564,"total_tokens":3407127},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8568554961,"cached_input_tokens":8477222272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24372899,"reasoning_output_tokens":14048008,"total_tokens":8592927860}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:33:31.944Z","ordinal":463846,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18432-af9c-7882-80ce-70535521cb1b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bd83e742-ed7d-4311-8a4c-da9540fc45ee","process_id":"74060","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show origin/main:eval/README.md | sed -n '115,180p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | rg 'eval_.*\\.mjs|eval.*test|test.*eval' | head -80; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code grep -n 'eval_hardened' origin/main -- . | head"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show origin/main:eval/README.md | sed -n '115,180p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | rg 'eval_.*\\.mjs|eval.*test|test.*eval' | head -80; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code grep -n 'eval_hardened' origin/main -- . | head"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\n  verify the account and these existing operating-system permissions through the approved local setup procedure:\n  1. `sudo useradd --system --create-home nexus-eval`\n  2. A narrowly constrained sudoers rule permitting only the required Bubblewrap invocation as `nexus-eval`; do not\n     grant arbitrary `env` command execution.\n  3. Keep task stores unreadable to the evaluator account; the runner does not mount them into the candidate namespace.\n  4. A Nexus install, Node and the peer agents that `nexus-eval` can read and execute.\n\n  Development runs may omit `runAs`; Bubblewrap isolation still applies. Qualification is refused without a separate\n  evaluator account, `setfacl`, explicit `sandboxRuntimeRoots`, and read-only `sandboxRuntimePaths` contained by those\n  roots. Protected roots such as `/etc`, `/dev`, `/proc`, `/sys`, `/run`, `/var`, `/tmp`, and sensitive user-cache paths\n  are rejected. No setup procedure is applied by the runner.\n\n- **Repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned commit.** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages a repo task as a\n  fresh `git init` that fetches only the pinned commit and its ancestors from the local cache (`--no-tags`, no\n  FETCH_HEAD), then checks out that commit detached. There is no `--shared` clone, alternates link, remote, tag or\n  descendant object, so the upstream fix that follows a held-out baseline is not reachable from the workspace. Staging\n  verifies this and refuses the run otherwise.\n\n- **Corpus binding is integrity evidence, not approval authentication.** The qualification config pins the exact\n  corpus-manifest SHA-256, and the run manifest repeats the selected task hashes. The v1 manifest binds every task's\n  full task tree in row `sha256`. The heldout-v2 manifest binds each task's raw `task.json` and hidden-directory digest for\n  pinned-repository tasks; a local fixture additionally requires a full-tree `sha256` because those two v2 digests do\n  not cover fixture files. The frozen config carries `corpusCustody: { custodian, approvedAt, reportPath, reportSha256 }`\n  and may also name `storeRoot`, `validatorPath`, `referencePath`, and `authorLogPath`; the report path and optional\n  private paths are protected from runtime mounts. These values and the manifest's custody labels are claims, not\n  signatures. Independent custody acceptance, pre-RC commit timing, and configuration freeze must be verified and\n  archived by the acceptance reviewer before any qualification run. The current candidate task package has not been\n  independently accepted.\n\n### Isolation limits\n\nBubblewrap plus the current runner enforces separate mount/user/PID/network namespaces, a cleared task-command\nenvironment, a bounded wall clock, bounded captured output, per-run process-group teardown, and read-only runtime\nbinds. Black-box qualification keeps oracle expectations outside candidate namespaces. Legacy hidden commands share a\nprocess with candidate code and are rejected during qualification preflight. The hardened legacy path below is only for\ndevelopment and pilot scoring; it is not qualification evidence. Aggregate CPU, memory, process-count and\nwritable-storage limits come from the resource contract below, not from request/token ceilings. Appliance-specific\nBubblewrap enforcement is a separate, unverified condition.\n\n### Hardened legacy hidden tests (development and pilot only)\n\nLegacy tasks use `hidden: { dir, command }` (for example `pytest` or `go test` over copied test files) and run candidate\ncode in the same process as the oracle. They do not meet the qualification boundary, even when hardened. Qualification\npreflight accepts only the isolated `blackbox-v1` protocol. Any legacy task in a qualification corpus must be replaced\nor converted by the authorized custodian, with custody checks repeated and a new immutable manifest identity recorded.\nDevelopment configs may opt into the hardened diagnostic path with `\"hardenedChecks\": true`.\n\n1. The agent's workspace is never tested, and nothing runs git or any other program against it after the agent ran.\n   An agent-written `.git/config` or `.gitattributes` would otherwise run commands as the harness user. The baseline\n   tree hash is taken before the agent starts. The harness then stages the task again (the same pinned commit or\n   fixture, the same setup commands) into a fresh workspace, and checks that its tree equals that baseline.\ncli/test/eval_hardened.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_harness.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_host_bubblewrap.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_host_operator_home.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_score_diagnostics.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_t3.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts\ncli/test/evaluator.test.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md\neval/host/container-test/run.sh\neval/host/container-test/systemctl-shim\neval/tasks/selftest-add/hidden/math.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/selftest-add/repo/package.json\neval/tasks/selftest-add/repo/test/other.test.js\neval/tasks/selftest-add/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/hidden/csv.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/repo/test/csv.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/hidden/test_duration_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/repo/tests/test_durations.py\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/hidden/report.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/test/report.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/hidden/test_inventory_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/repo/tests/test_inventory.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/hidden/slugify.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/repo/test/slugify.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/hidden/test_tax_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/repo/tests/test_totals.py\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":146854269}},"started_at_ms":1793219611796,"completed_at_ms":1793219611943}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:33:32.994Z","ordinal":463847,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18437-d142-7452-8289-1c2c50769991","call_id":"call_35078a4aa1144f15a88aad8e8ac1ffcb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1732)\nTotal output lines: 94\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\n  verify the account and these existing operating-system permissions through the approved local setup procedure:\n  1. `sudo useradd --system --create-home nexus-eval`\n  2. A narrowly constrained sudoers rule permitting only the required Bubblewrap invocation as `nexus-eval`; do not\n     grant arbitrary `env` command execution.\n  3. Keep task stores unreadable to the evaluator account; the runner does not mount them into the candidate namespace.\n  4. A Nexus install, Node and the peer agents that `nexus-eval` can read and execute.\n\n  Development runs may omit `runAs`; Bubblewrap isolation still applies. Qualification is refused without a separate\n  evaluator account, `setfacl`, explicit `sandboxRuntimeRoots`, and read-only `sandboxRuntimePaths` contained by those\n  roots. Protected roots such as `/etc`, `/dev`, `/proc`, `/sys`, `/run`, `/var`, `/tmp`, and sensitive user-cache paths\n  are rejected. No setup procedure is applied by the runner.\n\n- **Repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned commit.** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages a repo task as a\n  fresh `git init` that fetches only the pinned commit and its ancestors from the local cache (`--no-tags`, no\n  FETCH_HEAD), then checks out that commit detached. There is no `--shared` clone, alternates link, remote, tag or\n  descendant object, so the upstream fix t…432 tokens truncated…is not qualification evidence. Aggregate CPU, memory, process-count and\nwritable-storage limits come from the resource contract below, not from request/token ceilings. Appliance-specific\nBubblewrap enforcement is a separate, unverified condition.\n\n### Hardened legacy hidden tests (development and pilot only)\n\nLegacy tasks use `hidden: { dir, command }` (for example `pytest` or `go test` over copied test files) and run candidate\ncode in the same process as the oracle. They do not meet the qualification boundary, even when hardened. Qualification\npreflight accepts only the isolated `blackbox-v1` protocol. Any legacy task in a qualification corpus must be replaced\nor converted by the authorized custodian, with custody checks repeated and a new immutable manifest identity recorded.\nDevelopment configs may opt into the hardened diagnostic path with `\"hardenedChecks\": true`.\n\n1. The agent's workspace is never tested, and nothing runs git or any other program against it after the agent ran.\n   An agent-written `.git/config` or `.gitattributes` would otherwise run commands as the harness user. The baseline\n   tree hash is taken before the agent starts. The harness then stages the task again (the same pinned commit or\n   fixture, the same setup commands) into a fresh workspace, and checks that its tree equals that baseline.\ncli/test/eval_hardened.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_harness.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_host_bubblewrap.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_host_operator_home.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_score_diagnostics.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_t3.test.ts\ncli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts\ncli/test/evaluator.test.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md\neval/host/container-test/run.sh\neval/host/container-test/systemctl-shim\neval/tasks/selftest-add/hidden/math.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/selftest-add/repo/package.json\neval/tasks/selftest-add/repo/test/other.test.js\neval/tasks/selftest-add/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/hidden/csv.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/repo/test/csv.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/hidden/test_duration_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/repo/tests/test_durations.py\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/hidden/report.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/test/report.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/hidden/test_inventory_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/repo/tests/test_inventory.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/hidden/slugify.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/repo/test/slugify.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/hidden/test_tax_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/repo/tests/test_totals.py\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18432-af9c-7882-80ce-70535521cb1b","create_time":1793219612.994299}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
