commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\n+**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`; PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`; PR #305 merged as `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. PR #302 was closed unmerged and superseded by PR #308. PR #308 is open at `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` on base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; exact-head run [40763991304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40763991304) has Node 22 passed and Node 24 still running; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, with Linux checks not yet complete. The follow-up applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts index membership. Its change has independent review ACCEPT; an earlier focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log. PR #309 merged at 20:36 UTC as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed; it adds the checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 is open at `c8df374334bc50ed6dc3a3904cb4c52cf27e7d93` on base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; exact-head run [40762803901](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40762803901) has Node 22/24 passed and Linux tests in progress, and JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. A review identified stale PR #300 head/status text in the prior checkpoint; this update corrects it. Source PR checks remain distinct from release qualification.\n \n-**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n+**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04. Its evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open, so its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor RC. PR #309's merged provider evidence also applies only to RC10. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 20:25 UTC); the latest request for a custodian checkpoint or handoff remains unanswered. No custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; screenshot artifacts were waived, but terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n \n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n \nc8df374334bc50ed6dc3a3904cb4c52cf27e7d93\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1843d-be16-7a30-8bd0-717d10d5833e","create_time":1793220586.868267}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
