{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:05:42.020Z","ordinal":464883,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18455-4084-7d20-a7a8-3e48614e872e","call_id":"call_07d02fe0f4bf4250bfe0d98222de6b64","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8626)\nTotal output lines: 108\n\nmerged\n  result 100644 fec69a3b85c190d9a5d7ebb1a4b589a6500e3bfd docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n  our    100644 0f467c8d2c9e25fa70c57908cf86bc229a7a03b4 docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,90 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 00:35 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:52 UTC)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af`, the PR #309 merge commit. Main CI run [40764779353](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40764779353) is running on this exact SHA; its `sync-version --check` and requirements-check steps passed, and Node 22/24 test matrices are in progress. CodeQL run [40764779313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40764779313) passed. An isolated-HOME `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` run on this exact SHA passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This is source-stage evidence only.\n+\n+**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`; PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`; PR #305 merged as `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. PR #302 was closed unmerged and superseded by PR #308. PR #308 is open at `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` on base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; exact-head run [40763991304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40763991304) has Node 22 and Node 24 passed; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Linux checks are in progress. The follow-up applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts index membership. Its change has independent review ACCEPT; an earlier focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log. PR #309 merged at 20:36 UTC as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed; it adds the checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 is open at `c8df374334bc50ed6dc3a3904cb4c52cf27e7d93` on base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; exact-head run [40762803901](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40762803901) has Node 22/24 passed and Linux tests in progress, and JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. A review identified stale PR #300 head/status text in the prior checkpoint; this update corrects it. Source PR checks remain distinct from release qualification.\n+\n+**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04. Its evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-1…7026 tokens truncated…to issues [#3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3) and [#5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/5). Publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance; no additional authorization is requested here.\n+\n+## Historical checkpoint after PR #306 (2026-10-28; observation time not recorded)\n+\n+- **Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `8580c821f57119768db01614d31cd60e8766468b`, the merge of PR #306 on top of `90837aa` (which contains PR #307). PR #306 adds operation context budgeting and durable conversation checkpoints. PR #307's build-identity change is present on this main revision.\n+- **Requirements and version checks:** On a clean detached worktree at exactly `8580c82`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows; tested 108, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7. The 12 listed rows remain deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`.\n+- **Exact-main hosted CI:** CodeQL run [40733687484](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40733687484) passed on `8580c82` at 17:17:25 UTC. CI run [40733687806](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40733687806) remained in progress on that exact SHA when checked; no main test-matrix conclusion is claimed until it finishes.\n+- **Checkpoint restore PR #302:** The remote PR head remains `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`; its exact run [40729450236](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40729450236) failed the Node 22 and Node 24 suites on the tracked-deletion/symlink-parent checkpoint creation case, with Linux skipped. A separate local candidate has been rebased onto `8580c82` at `87b560c7e581fa71cce270474ba40766f372fb04`; the cumulative change is limited to `checkpoint.ts` and its two restore tests. Independent full-diff review and the authorized full-suite owner’s safe-boundary release are pending. The candidate has not been pushed, and no test result is claimed for it.\n+- **Readiness change review:** PR #300 remains remotely at head `d38341f` against base `145d464`; it has not been refreshed on GitHub. Its previous exact-head checks passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL; its Entire status failed because no separate reviewer approved that trail. The local readiness branch at `51409f5` has merged current `origin/main` `8580c82` and contains the checkpoint update now under review. It requires exact-head required checks before integration. Earlier contents remain historical evidence and must not be read as current source status.\n+- **Qualification and release:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. The installed-RC evidence remains tied to RC10, not this source revision. Held-out custody and evaluator compatibility are unresolved; no protected payload was accessed or run. The manual real-terminal matrix remains 0/15, with two screenshots and human verdicts required per cell. Current exact-RC provider, standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1844c-0389-7191-bd33-ba7c92f2b1e0","create_time":1793221542.0204265}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
