{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:20:19.105Z","ordinal":465338,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1844c-0389-7191-bd33-ba7c92f2b1e0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-335263d1-02cd-4714-aa61-1442f927f1c6","process_id":"97231","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Nexus v1|independent reviewer|single user|readiness claim\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Nexus v1|independent reviewer|single user|readiness claim' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"Nexus v1|independent reviewer|single user|readiness claim","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"777:# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n778:scope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n789:- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n812:- The readiness claims were `FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json` and `PLAN-10_READINESS_T2/owner.json`; at handoff the owner PID was absent but the claim was younger than 24 hours. Resume after release or the documented stale-claim procedure, update against `2c70d39`, and rerun fresh branch CI. [Task 2]\n817:- Symptom: PR #9 readiness evidence is canceled/skipped or stale. Cause: it was based on the old integration head. Fix: acquire/release the readiness claim, refresh against current integration, then run fresh CI; never infer qualification from its prior checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":40791}},"started_at_ms":1793222419105,"completed_at_ms":1793222419105}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:20:21.464Z","ordinal":465339,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18462-abd8-7cb2-8cd5-e92c447997e0","call_id":"call_bba843477aad449896621362f9d1b9ba","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"777:# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n778:scope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n789:- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n812:- The readiness claims were `FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json` and `PLAN-10_READINESS_T2/owner.json`; at handoff the owner PID was absent but the claim was younger than 24 hours. Resume after release or the documented stale-claim procedure, update against `2c70d39`, and rerun fresh branch CI. [Task 2]\n817:- Symptom: PR #9 readiness evidence is canceled/skipped or stale. Cause: it was based on the old integration head. Fix: acquire/release the readiness claim, refresh against current integration, then run fresh CI; never infer qualification from its prior checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1844c-0389-7191-bd33-ba7c92f2b1e0","create_time":1793222421.4647658}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
