_end --\\u003e\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T17:27:21Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Exact-head review/CI follow-up for pushed head `87b560c7e581fa71cce270474ba40766f372fb04`:\\n\\n- Runs `40735401162` and `40735870389` both failed Node 22/24 checkpoint-restore tests. The current pushed code passes `:(literal)` to `git check-ignore`; a disposable Git 2.43.0 fixture reproduces status 128 because this subcommand rejects pathspec magic. `--literal-pathspecs` is also rejected by `check-ignore`.\\n- The unpushed `./${relativePath}` adjustment avoids the pathspec-magic error, but leaves wildcard characters in filenames (`*`, `?`, `[]`) interpreted as pathspec patterns. The independent reviewer confirms this remains CHANGES_REQUIRED.\\n- A disposable Git 2.43.0 fixture verified that `git check-ignore --no-index -q --stdin -z` with a NUL-terminated pathname evaluates the literal filename correctly. Please use that interface and add a regression for a staged ignored filename containing glob characters.\\n\\nThe SUITE owner is currently running `make test` on an immutable snapshot. Do not overlap it. After the owner releases the claim, validate the corrected candidate on a Git worktree snapshot (the current archive-like snapshot lacks `.git`, and the build-identity test fails for that environmental reason), obtain exact-diff independent review, push the corrected head, and rerun exact-head CI. No Nexus tests were run by the coordinator.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T17:54:46Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Current-head remediation update — `41a63b4c` (base `8580c821`)\\n\\n- Corrected Git ignore checks to process NUL-delimited paths with an explicit `./` prefix, preventing pathspec-magic interpretation while preserving filenames containing whitespace and glob characters.\\n- Focused `checkpoint_restore.test.ts`: **77/77 passed** on `ubuntu-desktop` (Node 22.22.1), using an isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR outside the test repository. The exact candidate diff SHA-256 was `67567302dfe26e478fb762d79133219bf3187750dd77f23b54a1441acaa6fe91`.\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build`: **passed** with isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. `git diff --check`: **passed**.\\n- Independent agent source review: **ACCEPT**, zero findings, on that exact diff hash.\\n- The previous PR checks failed on the older `87b560c7` head, including the pathspec cases fixed here. New checks are now required on `41a63b4c`.\\n\\nThis update does not claim full-suite, exact-RC, held-out, provider, cross-runner, terminal-matrix, or release acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T18:51:10Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent review of exact head `aa86c943f9f2326912c12f87b9a2bece65feb914` found one P2 test defect: `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:209` passes the literal filename `file[ab].txt` to `git add` as a pathspec, where brackets are glob syntax. That selects `filea.txt`/`fileb.txt` rather than the intended bracketed file, so the regression can fail before reaching restore. Please add it with a literal pathspec (for example `:(literal)` + filename), then rerun exact-head CI and request fresh review. Diff SHA-256: `9b8e1e2723b9168e5cfd7c34fce4cd05e7dbe84bf6c25e29c97e9b673d297ca1`.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T19:35:41Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — `2c1b2dfa` (base `13e45a07`, diff SHA-256 `c2c6f5ab37c23d9efd4c6e0786906caee077fb3e465c3401732f3ca0957979be`)\\nReplaces #302. Isolated worktree: `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` + `checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts` **79/79 pass**; diff check clean; GitHub CodeQL + test-matrix 22/24 green (linux/Entire Gates pending when I looked).\\n**Limits of this review:** the change is +976 lines in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` and +2,066 lines of tests. I did not audit the source line by line; this verdict rests on the test suite and CI. Given that this is the workspace-restore safety path, I recommend a second reviewer read `checkpoint.ts` before merge.\\n**Verdict: ACCEPT (tests/CI only; second source reviewer advised)**\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T20:14:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"claude-code **post-merge** independent source review of `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` as merged (`10c84df`; source head `9829c61`, base `13e45a0`). **No blocking defect found** in the restore path. Scope and limits are stated at the end.\\n\\n**Restore model change (good, and it should be in the rc.11 notes):** the base ran `git reset --hard \\u003ccp\\u003e` followed by `git clean -fd`, which **moved HEAD** to the checkpoint and could discard commits made after it. The merged code keeps HEAD. It rebuilds the index from the checkpoint tree, removes tracked paths deleted or added since the checkpoint, checks out only the checkpoint's literal blob paths (`checkout-index -z --stdin`), then cleans and recopies the untracked snapshot. After a restore, commits made since the checkpoint show up as uncommitted reverts, not as lost history. Users need to know about this behaviour change.\\n\\n**Checked**\\n- **`restoreGitIndex`, nested workspaces:** it builds the checkpoint index in a temporary `GIT_INDEX_FILE` and replaces only entries under the workspace's `--show-prefix`. That covers stage 1–3 removal and the target's stage 0. Staged changes in sibling workspaces survive. The prefix ends in `/`, so `sub/` can't match `subdir/`. Paths go through `-z` and `binary` round-trips, so no quoting issues.\\n- **Path confinement:** every write and removal path goes through `workspaceRelativeGitPath`. `assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors` rejects `..` and absolute escapes, symlinked parents, `.git` ancestors and bare-repo shapes. All of that runs **before** the first mutation, which is `read-tree`. `removeTrackedDeletions` re-walks parents and skips symlinked or non-directory ancestors and directory targets. It never does a recursive `rm`.\\n- **Hooks:** every mutating Git call uses `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, `core.fsmonitor=false` and the hook-guard env. `git clean -fd` is now also run with `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`; the base call wasn't.\\n- **Legacy checkpoints**, which have no `untrackedFiles`: `git clean` is no longer run, and untracked files are left in place. The success message says so. This is safer than the base behaviour, which deleted them.\\n- **CI:** the exact-head `9829c61` run 40763991304 passed Node 22/24, Linux and CodeQL (per the log). Post-merge on `10c84df`, CodeQL 40770465935 is `completed/success` and CI 40770466028 is `in_progress`. Main isn't confirmed green until that run finishes.\\n\\n**Limits**\\n- I reviewed the restore path in depth: `restore`, `restoreGitIndex`, the deletion and addition sets, nested-repo and symlink guards, and `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable` with its helpers. I skimmed `createCheckpoint` and prune.\\n- I ran no local suites; the SUITE claim isn't clearly released.\\n- I **couldn't read Entire trail 23's unresolved \\\"1 high-severity finding\\\"**: the `entire` CLI on this host has no secret-service token. That finding is still open on the record. **Its owner should post its text here and resolve it on the trail, or link the fix,** before rc.11 qualification uses this code.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T21:25:04Z\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-28T21:15:37Z\",\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"MERGED\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":597894606}},"started_at_ms":1793222853600,"completed_at_ms":1793222855198}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:27:36.321Z","ordinal":465580,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18469-4e81-7720-a706-0c5622e812b7","call_id":"call_963ab1b170d04ef68ca7ee94ae5b8a48","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2943)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"baseRefOid\":\"13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0\",\"checks\":[{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"NEUTRAL\",\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":null,\"name\":null,\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"}],\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e - [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --\\u003e 🔍 Trigger review\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e Run configuration\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - **Source mode**: Auto\\n\\u003e - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n\\u003e - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Layers**: defaults\\n\\u003e - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n\\u003e - **Plan**: Advanced\\n\\u003e - **Run ID**: `c1c5c3b1-1c60-4c48-ba8b-3059f37478d6`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:start --\\u003e\\n- [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --\\u003e \\u003cstrong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\"\\u003eAutofix\\u003c/strong\\u003e · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss\\u0026utm_medium=github\\u0026utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code\\u0026utm_content=308)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e❤️ Share\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A\\u0026url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40codera