e merges; this checkpoint corrects it.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CON…13042 tokens truncated…fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The required real-terminal matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence does not replace operator evidence. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no recorded custodian acceptance; no private payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, exact-current-RC provider/standalone and cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization is granted but gated. The distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\nThe 11:58 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, CI and acceptance state by this checkpoint.\n\n---\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 11:58 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `d2442b0e0aa143191ab5ae478bc243ecce97861e`, which integrates PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266). Post-merge CI [40461301453](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40461301453) and CodeQL [40461301693](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40461301693) both completed successfully. PR #266 exact-head CI, including Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests/package and reproducibility, and CodeQL passed before merge. The source and its local regressions are integrated; this does not qualify the already-published RC10 artifact.\n\n**Current release PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) is open at `97e3f72e4a5fe8676a0a30ea9f6e023147ad73a5` on current base `d2442b0`; CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed and exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) is still running. PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on the previous `303ea32` source. Its earlier CI and CodeQL passed on that older head. A local readiness candidate has been refreshed to `d2442b0`; requirement enforcement (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), RC10 version synchronization, and diff hygiene pass on the refreshed candidate. Independent review asked that the old 05:54 snapshot be clearly superseded; this checkpoint does so. The refreshed candidate still needs final-base review, owner push, and exact-head hosted checks.\n\n**Installed RC and qualification:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. No stable `v1.0.0` release appears among the current public releases. The human five-terminal, three-size matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence is partial and does not replace the operator matrix. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (2026-10-26); no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n\n**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains gated on all required qualification and independent acceptance. The 05:54 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source, PR #266 integration, current PR checks, and release-gate status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 05:54 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and pre-RC checks:** `origin/main` is `303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4` (PR #267 merged); `origin/v1/integration` remains `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. On a clean detached snapshot of `303ea32`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10` passed. This is source-gate evidence for `303ea32`, not exact-RC acceptance.\n\n**Verifier candidate:** PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266) was updated to exact head `965a0c6f02aa1e4917563b648f7f20089592ba61`, based on `303ea32`. Independent source review accepted this exact commit. Focused verifier tests passed 6/6. At this checkpoint CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed; Node 22 and Node 24 CI were still running ([run 40457644361](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40457644361)). Do not merge until all exact-head checks pass. A separate local full-suite attempt on an older snapshot exited nonzero while a duplicate suite overlapped; its outcomes are unqualified and are not represented as passing evidence.\n\n**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\n\n**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published; publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoint below (04:20 UTC) is retained as historical evidence and superseded for exact source, PR #266, installer provenance, and terminal-host preparation.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 04:20 UTC)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18468-7ef6-7763-98c2-d6bd3928c395","create_time":1793222862.6669054}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
