c `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n \n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n \n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18468-7ef6-7763-98c2-d6bd3928c395","create_time":1793222885.6920576}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
