ease checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 21:31 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 21:42 UTC)\n \n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Post-merge CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) remains in progress on this exact SHA; Node 22 and Node 24 are running `npm --prefix cli test`. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n \n **Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path, but reports Entire trail 23 still summarizes one unresolved high-severity finding. The reviewer could not access its text, so that finding has not been evaluated or resolved and must be surfaced by its owner before successor-RC qualification. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its checks are running. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation. This checkpoint distinguishes the neutral GitHub check from the separate unresolved Entire trail report.\n \n-**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n+**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n \n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":903316755}},"started_at_ms":1793223731130,"completed_at_ms":1793223732034}}
