the rendered busy frame\n| * 115a231f test(tui): wait for the busy indicator\n| * d67c5d9d fix(operation): roll back partial context restores\nb035e716 docs(release): honor terminal screenshot waiver\n docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md                                    | 4 ++--\n docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | 2 +-\n 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c\nAuthor:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nAuthorDate: Wed Oct 28 21:34:39 2026 +0000\nCommit:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nCommitDate: Wed Oct 28 21:34:39 2026 +0000\n\n    docs(release): honor terminal screenshot waiver\n\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 7874d3e9..e8e009fb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell has a per-cell verdict and recorded outcomes; the release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ For each terminal × size, check:\n 6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. NO_COLOR.\n \n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n+Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this waiver does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n \n **Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex b3fe0b3b..6a63095f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this does not waive manual behavior checks or their evidence records.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \nunknown flag: --stat\n\nView changes in a pull request.\n\nWithout an argument, the pull request that belongs to the current branch\nis selected.\n\nWith `--web` flag, open the pull request diff in a web browser instead.\n\nUse `--exclude` to filter out files matching a glob pattern. The pattern\nuses forward slashes as path separators on all platforms. You can repeat\nthe flag to exclude multiple patterns.\n\nBy default, terminal escape sequences in the diff are neutralized, since\nthey could manipulate your terminal. Pass `--allow-escape-sequences` to\nprint the diff verbatim, for example when piping a patch to another program.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh pr diff [<number> | <url> | <branch>] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n      --allow-escape-sequences   Allow printing terminal escape sequences\n      --color string             Use color in diff output: {always|never|auto} (default \"auto\")\n  -e, --exclude patterns         Exclude files matching glob patterns from the diff\n      --name-only                Display only names of changed files\n      --patch                    Display diff in patch format\n  -w, --web                      Open the pull request diff in the browser\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n      --help                     Show help for command\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # See diff for current branch\n  $ gh pr diff\n  \n  # See diff for a specific PR\n  $ gh pr diff 123\n  \n  # Exclude files from diff output\n  $ gh pr diff --exclude '*.yml' --exclude 'generated/*'\n  \n  # Exclude matching files by name\n  $ gh pr diff --name-only --exclude '*.generated.*'\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":293215156}},"started_at_ms":1793223764612,"completed_at_ms":1793223765906}}
