{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:43:25.578Z","ordinal":466080,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18477-ca8a-7b13-9190-a40416b766a6","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed the current diff against `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`; SHA-256 `3f5e1f97256360016663933f14b9e8cee3cfff4d818e96c4fc98cc8a24934f0a`.\n\nPR #273’s merge SHA and successful exact-head checks match the records. The ancestry supports the stated limit: `e94208d` is **not** an ancestor of RC10 source `16ee8ca`, so RC10 does not contain that fix; the current main source and runtime-identity regression test do. The RC8 dogfood observation is explicitly labeled pre-fix, and successor-RC confirmation remains required.\n\nThe cumulative diff also updates ACCEPTANCE and SPEC-10 for the screenshot waiver. Those edits preserve the interactive checks, per-cell outcomes, and evidence requirements; they do not claim the 0/15 matrix is complete. The current CI and custody/qualification blockers remain accurately stated. `git diff --check` passed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","create_time":1793223805.5787058}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22187}}
