ame":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a182df-d9e4-7be3-8ff1-b56ddd57a74a","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_def"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26a89250081a0a59b7f6fdffa4ed8","order":22177,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18470-29a1-72b0-8930-3c5cfa769921","text":"I’m checking whether PR #310 auto-merged and whether the long-running main test jobs have finished. I’ll then update the release record against the actual resulting commit and select the next unblocked qualification task.","turn_id":"01a18470-1917-7473-af4c-d5bdd349f090"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26abf1c1481a0bbd3cc42bf3139b9","order":22178,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a18470-feb3-7982-b3df-24fb012b83ab","text":"Main CI advanced on exact `10c84df8`: Node 22 and Node 24 passed; Linux packaging is installing prerequisites and still running. CodeQL passed.\n\nPR #310 remains open at `16f13ba0`, with auto-merge enabled. Its JS/TS and CodeQL checks passed; Node 22/24 and Entire Gates are still running. The corrected readiness diff received independent agent acceptance.\n\nHeld-out qualification remains unstarted: Issue #1 is open and unassigned. I’ve also requested the unavailable details for Entire trail 23’s reported high-severity finding. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.","turn_id":"01a18470-1917-7473-af4c-d5bdd349f090"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26aff8fdc81a081b138442e586455","order":22179,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18471-f81f-71f0-84ed-a51fded9a980","text":"I’m refreshing the running checks and PR merge state. If they’re still active, I’ll use the latest output to decide whether there’s a safe parallel release task rather than repeating a status-only wait.","turn_id":"01a18471-eb5e-7921-8747-1d40b62f9ba1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26b11396c81a09c75b8c3b1b95f0d","order":22180,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18472-3d13-75d2-b21f-59c6589469ff","text":"Main CI has advanced again: Node 22/24 passed, and Linux is now building the release binaries. The held-out owner still hasn’t responded. I’m checking whether the evaluator’s legacy-format compatibility gap can be addressed with public code and synthetic fixtures, without touching the protected corpus.","turn_id":"01a18471-eb5e-7921-8747-1d40b62f9ba1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26b433bbc81a0b77536c660936d78","order":22181,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a18473-0179-7870-b9e2-358cce52fb71","text":"Exact-main CI on `10c84df8` advanced: Node 22 and Node 24 passed, and Linux is building `harness-core` and `nexus-tui`. CodeQL passed.\n\nPR #310 remains open at `16f13ba0`; its auto-merge is waiting on checks. Issue #1 remains open and unassigned, with no custodian response. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no RC or release acceptance is claimed.","turn_id":"01a18471-eb5e-7921-8747-1d40b62f9ba1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26b83639881a09455a2feca1eb287","order":22182,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18473-face-7783-a52f-5a594cbc8bba","text":"I’m checking the latest CI conclusions and auto-merge state. I’ll update the readiness evidence and move to the next prerequisite as soon as the exact checks finish.","turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26c518e8c81a096b866418690a21c","order":22186,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18477-2066-7bc0-8226-50f82b1b8893","text":"I found an additional pre-existing commit in the readiness branch history while preparing the update. Before pushing, I’m checking its scope and the exact PR diff so I don’t accidentally add work that belongs to a separate claim.","turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26c82df1081a09607a0be76ab79fc","order":22188,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18477-e155-7d91-b67d-9312caf7be66","text":"The added material is now independently accepted as part of the cumulative PR diff, including the documented screenshot waiver and the RC8 identity-fix provenance. I’m pushing the reviewed commits together and updating PR #310’s description so its scope matches the contents.","turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":22189,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16013,"receiver_message_id":"fc