{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:44:29.439Z","ordinal":466128,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26cbad53481a092e158a8d18fa829","usage":{"input_tokens":86906,"cached_input_tokens":86272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":156,"reasoning_output_tokens":139,"total_tokens":87062},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4070641,"cached_input_tokens":4020608,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13926,"reasoning_output_tokens":7726,"total_tokens":4084567},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8611426628,"cached_input_tokens":8519741056,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24497281,"reasoning_output_tokens":14115344,"total_tokens":8635923909}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:44:31.185Z","ordinal":466129,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18478-cad1-7cf2-b028-1058e19f7cfb","call_id":"call_0510a7e57ac04aafb95fd545f5c79afa","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At `origin/main@13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` (merge #305, `2026-10-28T15:11:02-04:00`), the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still has 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and four languages.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open and unassigned. Its latest comment, #6479873007 (`2026-10-28 20:24 UTC`), is a coordinator request for ownership/status or a safe handoff. No custodian response or handoff is visible in the issue or claims. The October 18 T2 report records historical corpus custody acceptance, but explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance.\\n\\nPR #33 is merged, but its hardened legacy support does not satisfy the current qualification contract: `eval/validate.mjs:49` and `eval/run.mjs:718` still reject legacy hidden commands during qualification; the README directs custodian-led conversion or replacement with fresh custody checks and a new manifest identity.\\n\\nSafe evaluator work can continue with synthetic compatibility tests and reconciliation of PR #33’s historical decision against the current fail-closed policy. Whether conversion preserves T2 validator semantics still requires custodian input. No private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the current diff against `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`; SHA-256 `3f5e1f97256360016663933f14b9e8cee3cfff4d818e96c4fc98cc8a24934f0a`.\\n\\nPR #273’s merge SHA and successful exact-head checks match the records. The ancestry supports the stated limit: `e94208d` is **not** an ancestor of RC10 source `16ee8ca`, so RC10 does not contain that fix; the current main source and runtime-identity regression test do. The RC8 dogfood observation is explicitly labeled pre-fix, and successor-RC confirmation remains required.\\n\\nThe cumulative diff also updates ACCEPTANCE and SPEC-10 for the screenshot waiver. Those edits preserve the interactive checks, per-cell outcomes, and evidence requirements; they do not claim the 0/15 matrix is complete. The current CI and custody/qualification blockers remain accurately stated. `git diff --check` passed.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18473-ec48-7c83-b9e5-71dfb1a63e9b","create_time":1793223871.1857605}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
