eadRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/dotenv-18.0.8\",\"headRefOid\":\"bb8f56e4f6343ebee54ab79ba73975e4062ba46f\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":111,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump dotenv from 16.6.1 to 18.0.8 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:04:30Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/111\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/libc-0.2.191\",\"headRefOid\":\"d70302124870dae35a4e33bfa536f782bc174cde\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":110,\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump libc from 0.2.189 to 0.2.191 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:53Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/110\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/softprops/action-gh-release-3.0.3\",\"headRefOid\":\"6a3c3ba1da7f6f0735cc40cee277dc546f80a112\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":108,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump softprops/action-gh-release from 2.6.2 to 3.0.3\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:11:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/108\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/similar-3.2.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"be7416b6620a421332e6291754558d87576d892f\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":107,\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump similar from 2.7.0 to 3.2.0 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:52Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/107\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/checkout-7.0.1\",\"headRefOid\":\"7df9a695ce312c10ec5210ac6eaf23c8a85ca2f5\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":104,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/checkout from 4.4.0 to 7.0.1\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:50:08Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/104\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/REDACTED\",\"headRefOid\":\"25b39142f444a2586f4bf6be1c8c0e04036df863\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":103,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/attest-build-provenance from 92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc to ef244123eb79f2f7a7e75d99086184180e6d0018\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:06:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/103\"}]\n## v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028...origin/v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028 [ahead 1]\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 7874d3e9..e8e009fb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell has a per-cell verdict and recorded outcomes; the release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ For each terminal × size, check:\n 6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. NO_COLOR.\n \n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n+Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this waiver does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n \n **Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 657b3188..4ccdfa03 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,16 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 21:45 UTC)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Post-merge CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) remains in progress on this exact SHA: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; the `linux-x86_64` job is running `npm --prefix cli test`. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n+\n+**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path, but reports Entire trail 23 still summarizes one unresolved high-severity finding. The reviewer could not access its text, so that finding has not been evaluated or resolved and must be surfaced by its owner before successor-RC qualification. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its checks are running. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation. This checkpoint distinguishes the neutral GitHub check from the separate unresolved Entire trail report.\n+\n+**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n+\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n+\n+## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n \n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex b3fe0b3b..6a63095f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this does not waive manual behavior checks or their evidence records.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":521905235}},"started_at_ms":1793224014284,"completed_at_ms":1793224016807}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:46:58.069Z","ordinal":466189,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1847b-0895-7e83-92e2-518073037c0d","call_id":"call_31bcd1d2d86f40718691aef9b7d7f4aa","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 14448)\nTotal output lines: 60\n\n{\"assignees\":[],\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\n\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).\\n   - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table is sealed inside `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2/LICENSE-AUDIT-2026-10-18.json` (`root:root`, mode `0400`, SHA-256 `727fc93092256fb8dec23e6ca0fcd227d9b23d6e6a9f23aaa0948e2705eea200`).\\n2. **T3 Sealed `heldout-t3` Corpus (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json` SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`):**\\n   - All 8 T3 tasks are first-party clean-room fixtures authored specifically for Nexus v1.0.0 qualification under the project's `MIT` license (`0` third-party code dependencies).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6253067267\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNi7_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity from authoritative gateway deployment evidence (alias engineering/deep alone is insufficient); provide that metadata through the authorized runtime/custody boundary. No new private-store access is requested for implementation sessions. Peer runtime binaries are now rootowned/hash-pinned, but no RC or qualification claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6255328253\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOTZNQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference solutions, validator contents, answers or credentials. Preserve the sealed manifest and record any supersession before changing content. No T2/T3/T4 qualification has been started by this coordinator.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6256122165\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeAFf4w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**\\n\\nThe public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.\\n\\nThe latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version and supersession before qualification.\\n\\nPlease do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, hidden answers, validators, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and the evaluator-boundary gates are established.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6308323299\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeFr82g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.\\n\\nCustodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible immutable successor and repeat validation/custody checks, or whether an already-approved compatibility path exists; (3) expected completion/owner; and (4) whether T3 custody/identity remains unchanged. Do not post task IDs, objectives, source repositories, payloads, patches, reference solutions, validator contents, answers, or credentials. Keep the sealed corpus immutable until any successor is recorded with explicit supersession. Public metadata approval remains separate from private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6314196186\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeHMGgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexu…8448 tokens truncated…in\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/commander-15.0.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"aeea1da4ad2f87dda43c29f5964ce40d95acee56\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":114,\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump commander from 12.1.0 to 15.0.0 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T23:25:55Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/114\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/serde_json-1.0.154\",\"headRefOid\":\"b11ec547a7ae9f44f51f9699d0619426a603f89e\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":113,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump serde_json from 1.0.151 to 1.0.154 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:08:12Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/113\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-node-7.1.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"b3cb1d905266bc6387aa877f6755ff8761fabc59\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":112,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/setup-node from 4.4.0 to 7.1.0\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:11:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/112\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/dotenv-18.0.8\",\"headRefOid\":\"bb8f56e4f6343ebee54ab79ba73975e4062ba46f\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":111,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump dotenv from 16.6.1 to 18.0.8 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:04:30Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/111\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/libc-0.2.191\",\"headRefOid\":\"d70302124870dae35a4e33bfa536f782bc174cde\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":110,\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump libc from 0.2.189 to 0.2.191 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:53Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/110\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/softprops/action-gh-release-3.0.3\",\"headRefOid\":\"6a3c3ba1da7f6f0735cc40cee277dc546f80a112\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":108,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump softprops/action-gh-release from 2.6.2 to 3.0.3\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:11:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/108\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/similar-3.2.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"be7416b6620a421332e6291754558d87576d892f\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":107,\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump similar from 2.7.0 to 3.2.0 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:52Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/107\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/checkout-7.0.1\",\"headRefOid\":\"7df9a695ce312c10ec5210ac6eaf23c8a85ca2f5\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":104,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/checkout from 4.4.0 to 7.0.1\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:50:08Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/104\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/REDACTED\",\"headRefOid\":\"25b39142f444a2586f4bf6be1c8c0e04036df863\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":103,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/attest-build-provenance from 92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc to ef244123eb79f2f7a7e75d99086184180e6d0018\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:06:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/103\"}]\n## v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028...origin/v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028 [ahead 1]\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 7874d3e9..e8e009fb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell has a per-cell verdict and recorded outcomes; the release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ For each terminal × size, check:\n 6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. NO_COLOR.\n \n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n+Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this waiver does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n \n **Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 657b3188..4ccdfa03 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,16 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 21:45 UTC)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Post-merge CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) remains in progress on this exact SHA: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; the `linux-x86_64` job is running `npm --prefix cli test`. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n+\n+**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path, but reports Entire trail 23 still summarizes one unresolved high-severity finding. The reviewer could not access its text, so that finding has not been evaluated or resolved and must be surfaced by its owner before successor-RC qualification. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its checks are running. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation. This checkpoint distinguishes the neutral GitHub check from the separate unresolved Entire trail report.\n+\n+**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n+\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n+\n+## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n \n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex b3fe0b3b..6a63095f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this does not waive manual behavior checks or their evidence records.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224018.069118}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
