{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:51:01.710Z","ordinal":466354,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae26e40e5f881a0afc2c03961f91c3b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8ff535998eed4ceab7392103dedf3aae","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path, but reports Entire trail 23 still summarizes one unresolved high-severity finding. The reviewer could not access its text, so that finding has not been evaluated or resolved and must be surfaced by its owner before successor-RC qualification. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its checks are running. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation. This checkpoint distinguishes the neutral GitHub check from the separate unresolved Entire trail report.\\n+**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. This is distinct from the neutral GitHub Entire Gates check. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its Node 22/24 and Entire checks are running while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL have passed. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224256.9214032}}}
