{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:56:24.325Z","ordinal":466587,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8fbfff35-a696-4c3f-83ae-ae5c815ba146","process_id":"40999","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'Archive screenshots|screenshots are archived|screenshots.*gate|screenshot.*terminal' docs/v1.0.0 docs | head -40 && find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf '%f\\n' | rg 'DECISIONS|PLAN-10|READINESS|TERMINAL'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Archive screenshots|screenshots are archived|screenshots.*gate|screenshot.*terminal' docs/v1.0.0 docs","query":"Archive screenshots|screenshots are archived|screenshots.*gate|screenshot.*terminal","path":"v1.0.0"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf \"%f\\\\n\"","path":"nexus-claims"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg 'DECISIONS|PLAN-10|READINESS|TERMINAL'","query":"DECISIONS|PLAN-10|READINESS|TERMINAL","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qual