r each cell, perform all seven checks in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3: launch; exercise the approval panel with continuous typing and a three-line paste before a deliberate approval; use Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter for multiline input; resize while streaming; press Esc during `sleep 30` and confirm no survivor; press Ctrl-C twice and confirm clean terminal restoration; and verify `NO_COLOR`. Save the approval-panel and post-exit screenshots and record a PASS/FAIL verdict. A failure on approval input, cancellation cleanup, or terminal restoration fails the safety gate; every other failure needs a documented disposition. Keep failed attempts and retries distinct.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md:43:For each row, attach a genuine screenshot of the approval panel and a genuine screenshot of the restored post-exit terminal. Record exact observations, commands where applicable, and any failure disposition. Automated PTY evidence does not fill these manual rows.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md:26:A later installed-RC10 synthetic probe rendered all nine source `Overlay` variants across two synthetic runs at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14. The Detail capture is retained separately; its final idle predicate timed out after Esc visibly closed the panel. Follow-up attempts displayed the command approval panel but did not complete the synthetic approval sequence; they are classified as harness-incomplete, not product failures. Raw streams, screenshots, driver, mock gateway and attempts are archived under [overlay-expansion-20261027](overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md). This narrows the earlier overlay-coverage gap but does not change the overall `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED` disposition: other terminal configurations are uncovered, the intermittent cancellation timeouts remain, and human terminal acceptance remains pending.\nPLAN-10_HOST_PREFLIGHT_CURRENT_SOURCE\nDEFECT_AGENT_STREAM_TERMINAL_OUTPUT_20261025\nFILE