{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:56:43.014Z","ordinal":466603,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2f4f583a-9f71-4cc8-b98e-3293a7f163da","process_id":"33596","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md && sed -n '1,70p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md && rg -n '^#|screenshot|REQ-QUAL-108|terminal' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | head -60 && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_ACCEPTANCE.md/owner.json && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","name":"TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,70p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^#|screenshot|REQ-QUAL-108|terminal' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md","query":"^#|screenshot|REQ-QUAL-108|terminal","path":"DECISIONS.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_ACCEPTANCE.md/owner.json","name":"owner.json","path":"/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_ACCEPTANCE.md/owner.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md/owner.json","name":"owner.json","path":"/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an unfilled recording template; it contains no test results and does not qualify an RC.\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n\n§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, screenshots, and evidence\nreferences are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\nfailure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\ncheck (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\nor a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n\nACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\nrequired screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\ncell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\nfailed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n| Task authoring | 40 T2 tasks at 1–2 hours each, plus 8 T3 tasks at 3–4 hours each: roughly 10–14 days of author time | Author availability (X2) |\n| Run wall time (historical estimate; see below) | (40×5 + 8×5 + 40) runs per agent × 3 agents ≈ 840 runs. At a median 6 min/run serial on one inference host, about 84 hours, roughly 4 days of continuous inference. T3 runs are longer. | Inference-host availability and thermal behaviour (see the `experiments/thermal-soak` history). This is the critical-path risk for M5. |\n\nThe original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\n1:# Decisions: Nexus Code v1.0.0\n29:## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n50:## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\n54:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\n60:## DEC-03: Team and operation scope in v1\n72:## DEC-04: Issue #12 open normative blockers\n81:## DEC-05: v1 evaluation protocol and thresholds\n116:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n126:## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n132:## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n138:## DEC-09: Release provenance mechanism\n144:## DEC-10: Tracking of `cli/dist`\n150:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\n157:## DEC-12: Platform scope\n163:## DEC-13: Contest track disposition\n178:## DEC-14: Free text on the command line\n182:## DEC-15: Knowledge auto-extraction\n188:## DEC-16: Standalone qualification under a gateway-only environment\n220:## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n241:## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028\",\n  \"base\": \"10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-28T21:40:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Apply user-authorized waiver of manual terminal screenshot artifacts while preserving all terminal behavior and per-cell verdict requirements\",\n  \"status\": \"Local commit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c aligns ACC-TUI-MANUAL with the user-authorized screenshot-artifact waiver; all interactive checks and per-cell outcomes remain required. Awaiting owner push and exact review/checks. Independent read-only review ACCEPT exact patch SHA256 2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e; no tests run (documentation-only). Local commit remains unpushed; owner push and exact-head CI/integration pending.\",\n  \"head\": \"bf3965543431061d4c119940edab29ab4ee9d473\",\n  \"independent_review\": {\n    \"disposition\": \"ACCEPT\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"/root/rc5_candidate_review\",\n    \"commit\": \"b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c\",\n    \"patch_sha256\": \"2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e\",\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"tests_run\": false,\n    \"confirmed_at\": \"2026-10-28T21:37:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028\",\n  \"base\": \"10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-28T21:42:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Align v1 qualification spec with owner-authorized terminal screenshot-artifact waiver while preserving interactive checks\",\n  \"status\": \"Local commit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c records screenshot-artifact waiver for v1.0.0 while preserving behavior checks/evidence. Awaiting owner push and exact review/checks. Independent read-only review ACCEPT exact patch SHA256 2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e; no tests run (documentation-only). Local commit remains unpushed; owner push and exact-head CI/integration pending.\",\n  \"head\": \"bf3965543431061d4c119940edab29ab4ee9d473\",\n  \"independent_review\": {\n    \"disposition\": \"ACCEPT\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"/root/rc5_candidate_review\",\n    \"commit\": \"b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c\",\n    \"patch_sha256\": \"2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e\",\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"tests_run\": false,\n    \"confirmed_at\": \"2026-10-28T21:37:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":779177156}},"started_at_ms":1793224602234,"completed_at_ms":1793224603014}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:56:44.069Z","ordinal":466604,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18483-f9a5-77d2-9ff6-5e5ae0ba7b42","call_id":"call_ad2b70f2ee184a7cb99a801fa61036dc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3644)\nTotal output lines: 222\n\n# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an unfilled recording template; it contains no test results and does not qualify an RC.\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n\n§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, screenshots, and evidence\nreferences are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\nfailure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\ncheck (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\nor a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n\nACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\nrequired screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\ncell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\nfailed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | S…644 tokens truncated… 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n| Task authoring | 40 T2 tasks at 1–2 hours each, plus 8 T3 tasks at 3–4 hours each: roughly 10–14 days of author time | Author availability (X2) |\n| Run wall time (historical estimate; see below) | (40×5 + 8×5 + 40) runs per agent × 3 agents ≈ 840 runs. At a median 6 min/run serial on one inference host, about 84 hours, roughly 4 days of continuous inference. T3 runs are longer. | Inference-host availability and thermal behaviour (see the `experiments/thermal-soak` history). This is the critical-path risk for M5. |\n\nThe original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\n1:# Decisions: Nexus Code v1.0.0\n29:## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n50:## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\n54:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\n60:## DEC-03: Team and operation scope in v1\n72:## DEC-04: Issue #12 open normative blockers\n81:## DEC-05: v1 evaluation protocol and thresholds\n116:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n126:## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n132:## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n138:## DEC-09: Release provenance mechanism\n144:## DEC-10: Tracking of `cli/dist`\n150:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\n157:## DEC-12: Platform scope\n163:## DEC-13: Contest track disposition\n178:## DEC-14: Free text on the command line\n182:## DEC-15: Knowledge auto-extraction\n188:## DEC-16: Standalone qualification under a gateway-only environment\n220:## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n241:## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028\",\n  \"base\": \"10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-28T21:40:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Apply user-authorized waiver of manual terminal screenshot artifacts while preserving all terminal behavior and per-cell verdict requirements\",\n  \"status\": \"Local commit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c aligns ACC-TUI-MANUAL with the user-authorized screenshot-artifact waiver; all interactive checks and per-cell outcomes remain required. Awaiting owner push and exact review/checks. Independent read-only review ACCEPT exact patch SHA256 2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e; no tests run (documentation-only). Local commit remains unpushed; owner push and exact-head CI/integration pending.\",\n  \"head\": \"bf3965543431061d4c119940edab29ab4ee9d473\",\n  \"independent_review\": {\n    \"disposition\": \"ACCEPT\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"/root/rc5_candidate_review\",\n    \"commit\": \"b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c\",\n    \"patch_sha256\": \"2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e\",\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"tests_run\": false,\n    \"confirmed_at\": \"2026-10-28T21:37:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028\",\n  \"base\": \"10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-28T21:42:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Align v1 qualification spec with owner-authorized terminal screenshot-artifact waiver while preserving interactive checks\",\n  \"status\": \"Local commit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c records screenshot-artifact waiver for v1.0.0 while preserving behavior checks/evidence. Awaiting owner push and exact review/checks. Independent read-only review ACCEPT exact patch SHA256 2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e; no tests run (documentation-only). Local commit remains unpushed; owner push and exact-head CI/integration pending.\",\n  \"head\": \"bf3965543431061d4c119940edab29ab4ee9d473\",\n  \"independent_review\": {\n    \"disposition\": \"ACCEPT\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"/root/rc5_candidate_review\",\n    \"commit\": \"b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c\",\n    \"patch_sha256\": \"2ae9a0d6d0ccd661fbb74378ed5ad1297fd26b6c44f927167c19e142eba1e87e\",\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"tests_run\": false,\n    \"confirmed_at\": \"2026-10-28T21:37:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224604.0697799}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
