{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:57:53.982Z","ordinal":466638,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-94d2a8d8-2dba-48f4-9be9-616d106d9b0d","process_id":"6033","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '210,255p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md && sed -n '1,110p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md && sed -n '32,40p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '210,255p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md","name":"DECISIONS.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,110p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","name":"TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '32,40p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\n\n**Release statement:**\n- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n- LM Studio stays \"compatible, not live-qualified\" unless a user-run report is added.\n\n**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-PRV-106, REQ-QUAL-107; SPEC-05; SPEC-10; PLAN-05 task 7; PLAN-10; ACCEPTANCE §4.2. Owner action X3 (separate host) is withdrawn.\n\n## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n\n**Question.** REQ-AGT-118 (SPEC-11 §2.7) requires the token estimator to be conservative for non-Latin scripts: **≥ 1 token per CJK, Hangul or kana character**. ACC-VER-07 requires the estimator to be **within 1.5× of a pinned tokenizer's count** for the CJK, digit, base64, emoji and prose corpora. For a tokenizer that merges common characters into multi-character tokens these two are mutually unsatisfiable.\n\n**Evidence (pinned worker `b0-live-llama-worker1`, limits_version `a3c2fcbc2f2b977c`; fixture `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json`).**\n\n| Corpus | Characters | Estimator (floor) | Tokenizer reference | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CJK common-word sentences × 50 | 400 | 400 | 200 | **2.00×** |\n| Hangul syllables × 200 | 200 | 200 | 120 | **1.67×** |\n\nThe floor forces 400 and 200 tokens; the band caps at 1.5 × 200 = 300 and 1.5 × 120 = 180. No estimator can satisfy both. This is a genuine, arithmetic inconsistency, not a measurement defect: the reference counts were re-measured on the pinned worker and the estimator was reproduced exactly.\n\n**Decision (chosen).** REQ-AGT-118's `≥ 1 token/char` floor is an **admission-safety** requirement, not an accuracy requirement: it guarantees the estimator never *under-admits* tokens for a non-Latin context, because an under-estimate silently overflows the context window (the failure class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent). ACC-VER-07's `≤ 1.5×` band is an **accuracy** target. The two are distinct properties, and where a merging tokenizer makes them collide the admission-safety floor takes precedence. ACC-VER-07 is therefore scoped to the corpora the floor does not dominate; for a merging tokenizer the floor-driven over-estimate is admitted as a **bounded admission-safety bias**. The `≤ 1.5×` accuracy threshold itself is **unchanged**.\n\nThis amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the measured estimator is floor-bound — currently exactly the two in the table above — and it **does not silently exempt any other corpus**: any corpus whose estimator lands between the floor and the band must be examined and recorded (`tokens.test.ts` pins the floor-bound set to these two names and the full 14-corpus set, so neither an added exemption nor a silent corpus deletion can pass the test). The original accuracy failures are **preserved** — in the table above, in the fixture's `floorBound` entries, and in the base ledger wording (git history at `e1759ca`; the live row now records the amendment and stays `partial` until the changed tests pass and the amendment is independently accepted) — as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. They are not deleted or rewritten into passes.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n\n## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n\n| # | Action | Why | When |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\n| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14 (T2) and 2026-10-18 (T3):** agent authorship authorized and completed for both T2 (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, sha256 `50895b84…`, 40 tasks) and T3 (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, sha256 `85fb9caf…`, 8 tasks), each sealed under root-owned `0700` custody. | DEC-05 | Done |\n| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\n| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\n| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\n| X6 | Provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106; judging is over, so the historical erratum check is no longer applicable | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\n| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\n| X8 | Decide whether to clean the 52k test-polluted records in the real `~/.nexus/tasks` (PER-03). Safe to remove: `task-*.json` whose `workspacePath` starts with `/tmp/nexus-app-test-`. | Hygiene | Any time |\n# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an unfilled recording template; it contains no test results and does not qualify an RC.\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n\n§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, screenshots, and evidence\nreferences are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\nfailure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\ncheck (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\nor a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n\nACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\nrequired screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\ncell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\nfailed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":861203454}},"started_at_ms":1793224673120,"completed_at_ms":1793224673982}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:57:55.005Z","ordinal":466639,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18485-0ebd-7833-97d7-43c60b823f23","call_id":"call_9cd1c483cc814da087d5b03ad849c5b0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3268)\nTotal output lines: 144\n\n- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\n\n**Release statement:**\n- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n- LM Studio stays \"compatible, not live-qualified\" unless a user-run report is added.\n\n**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-PRV-106, REQ-QUAL-107; SPEC-05; SPEC-10; PLAN-05 task 7; PLAN-10; ACCEPTANCE §4.2. Owner action X3 (separate host) is withdrawn.\n\n## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n\n**Question.** REQ-AGT-118 (SPEC-11 §2.7) requires the token estimator to be conservative for non-Latin scripts: **≥ 1 token per CJK, Hangul or kana character**. ACC-VER-07 requires the estimator to be **within 1.5× of a pinned tokenizer's count** for the CJK, digit, base64, emoji and prose corpora. For a tokenizer that merges common characters into multi-character tokens these two are mutually unsatisfiable.\n\n**Evidence (pinned worker `b0-live-llama-worker1`, limits_version `a3c2fcbc2f2b977c`; fixture `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json`).**\n\n| Corpus | Characters | Estimator (floor) | Tokenizer reference | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CJK common-word sentences × 50 | 400 | 400 | 200 | **2.00×** |\n| Hangul syllables × 200 | 200 | 200 | 120 | **1.67×** |\n\nThe floor forces 400 and 200 tokens; the band caps at 1.5 × 200 = 300 and 1.5 × 120 = 180. No estimator can satisfy both. This is a genuine, arithmetic inconsistency, not a measurement defect: the reference counts were re-measured on the pinned worker and the estimator was reproduced exactly.\n\n**Decision (chosen).** REQ-AGT-118's `≥ 1 token/char` floor is an **admission-safety** requirement, not an accuracy requirement: it guarantees the estimator never *under-admits* tokens for a non-Latin context, because an under-estimate silently overflows the context window (the failure class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent). ACC-VER-07's `≤ 1.5×` band is an **accuracy** target. The two are distinct properties, and where a merging tokenizer makes them collide the admission-safety floor takes precedence. ACC-VER-07 is therefore scoped to the corpora the floor does not dominate; for a merging tokenizer the floor-driven over-estimate is admitted as a **bounded admission-safety bias**. The `≤ 1.5×` accuracy threshold itself is **unchanged**.\n\nThis amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the measured estimator is floor-bound — currently exactly the two in the table above — and it **does not silently exempt any other corpus**: any corpus whose estimator lands between the floor and the band must be examined and recorded (`tokens.test.ts` pins the floor-bound set to these two names and the full 14-corpus set, so neither an added exemption nor a silent corpus deletion can pass the test). The original accuracy failures are **preserved** — in the table above, in the fixture's `floorBound` entries, and in the base ledger wording (git history at `e1759ca`; the live row now records the amendment and stays `partial` until the changed tests pass and the amendment is independently accepted) — as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. They are not deleted or rewritten into passes.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n\n## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n\n| # | Action | Why | When |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\n| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14 (T2) and 2026-10-18 (T3):** agent authorship authorized and completed for both T2 (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, sha256 `50895b84…`, 40 tasks) and T3 (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, sha256 `85fb9caf…`, 8 tasks), each sealed under root-owned `0700` custody. | DEC-05 | Done |\n| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping …768 tokens truncated…erences for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n\n§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, screenshots, and evidence\nreferences are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\nfailure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\ncheck (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\nor a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n\nACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\nrequired screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\ncell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\nfailed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224675.0053327}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
