{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:59:12.027Z","ordinal":466682,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c8b3699c-0a08-4c00-bea1-bf915922118a","process_id":"51631","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md')\ns=p.read_text()\nold='The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run.'\nnew='Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run.'\nassert s.count(old)==1, s.count(old)\np.write_text(s.replace(old,new))\nPY\nrg -n 'DEC-18|screenshot artifact|Archive screenshots|both required screenshots|approval-panel screenshot' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -30\ngit diff --check && git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-correction-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md')\ns=p.read_text()\nold='The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run.'\nnew='Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run.'\nassert s.count(old)==1, s.count(old)\np.write_text(s.replace(old,new))\nPY\nrg -n 'DEC-18|screenshot artifact|Archive screenshots|both required screenshots|approval-panel screenshot' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -30\ngit diff --check && git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); manual behavior checks and their evidence records remain mandatory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:36:| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-18. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell has a per-cell verdict and recorded outcomes; the release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:41:Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v10-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:84:per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\n M docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":910065943}},"started_at_ms":1793224751117,"completed_at_ms":1793224752027}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:59:13.488Z","ordinal":466683,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18486-4150-7142-aca4-9a4f316db86a","call_id":"call_72f0f68862454db3b9e29221e6750145","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); manual behavior checks and their evidence records remain mandatory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:36:| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-18. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell has a per-cell verdict and recorded outcomes; the release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:41:Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v10-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:84:per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\n M docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224753.4882228}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
