details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: cli/src/agent.ts:232 injects explicit Nexus Code host identity and prohibits inferring host from provider/model; cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts covers it. Exact-main CI 40751988282 passed Node22, Node24 and Linux. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify sensitive-checkpoint failure offers operator choices (details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: REPL offers read-only, continue without rollback checkpoint, create checkpoint despite sensitive persistence risk, cancel, or re-enter; sidecar reports same options. Tests cover REPL and sidecar; exact-main CI 40751988282 passed all jobs. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify upgrade accepts signed GitHub release asset redirect (details=The RC7 failure URL host is now explicitly allowlisted in current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 only for the expected release-asset path (cli/src/upgrade.ts:665-671). cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts:159 covers a synthetic signed GitHub release URL and unsafe cases remain rejected. Exact-main CI run 40751988282 passed all three jobs. This source check does not replace running `nexus upgrade` on the successor exact RC/package or validate backup-time UX.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [doing] Reconcile doctor D1-D3 report against current main (details=Entire recall plus exact committed origin/main source/test inspection at 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0. D1 appears source-remediated: async opendir/lstat in batches of 128, bounded newest-record parsing, 30s default integrity deadline; committed tests assert event-loop responsiveness, bounded concurrency and deadline. D2 appears source-remediated: index.json is excluded, schema-v2 requires messageLog and rejects messages; schema-v1 keeps messages. D3 has intended distinction: absent /models entry is advisory WARN; --deep performs one inference and upgrades model.available only on success; committed tests cover that exact case. These are committed-source/test evidence, not rerun tests or live reproduction. Next: inspect exact current commit CI/test coverage if needed and reproduce on mike-dev state without altering user data; acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify RC7 download redirect rejection against current main (details=Verified main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 source/test and tag ancestry. Fix commit 64c22d3e6fc20c36432946abc8e237017d4b91be (2026-10-26 03:17 UTC) accepts the signed GitHub release-assets redirect only on /github-production-release-asset/. Regression coverage added in 1cce2f48. Fix is absent from v1.0.0-rc.7 history, present in rc.8, rc.9, and rc.10. So the reported RC7 rejection is explained by an older artifact; current source already has the fix. No current-main code change needed. XERJ field report submitted; HTTP 200.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [dropped] Refresh PR #300 readiness facts and obtain exact-diff independent review (details=Superseded by current PR #300 head c8df374 and exact-head CI monitor task; old branch/head status no longer current.), updated about 1 hour ago\n  - [dropped] Refresh readiness checkpoint PR #300 (details=Duplicate created in prior work-state update; tracked under existing task Refresh readiness checkpoint and reconcile RC10 cross-runner evidence.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [done] Reconcile reported missing local AI setup option (details=Verified exact public RC10 source/tag `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` includes Appliance in the provider connect list and endpoint/key setup (`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:300-347`); its TUI regression test explicitly asserts the connect menu shows Appliance and opens the local endpoint prompt (`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3117-3