us Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The exact-main source CI status is recorded separately above.\\n \\n-**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. The user expressly waived screenshot artifacts for this matrix; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\\n+**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\\n \\n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\\n \\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\\nindex 25cde4ed..c1b99f46 100644\\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\\n@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ Fill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not cop\\n - `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\\n - Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\\n - Host OS and version: __________________________________\\n-- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\\n+- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\\n \\n Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\\n \\n@@ -38,41 +38,41 @@ Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by\\n 6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\\n 7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\\n \\n-For each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\\n+Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\\n \\n ## Terminal × size results\\n \\n-Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\\n-\\n-| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\\n-|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\\n-| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n-| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\\n+Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\\n+\\n+| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\\n+|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\\n+| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n+| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\\n \\n ## Acceptance gate\\n \\n - Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\\n - Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\\n-- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\\n+- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence references: [ ] yes  [ ] no\\n - All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\\n - Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\\n \\n §5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\\n \\n-Mark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, screenshots, and evidence\\n+Mark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence\\n references are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\\n failure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\\n check (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\\n@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ or a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\\n ACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\\n \\n Mark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\\n-required screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\\n+per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\\n cell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\\n failed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\\n §5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\nindex 2d161b82..7e4ff63c 100644\\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\n@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ Implements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harne\\n | 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\\n | 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\\n | 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\\n-| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\\n+| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\\n \\n ## PR slices\\n \\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\nindex 6a63095f..ecf81ef1 100644\\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. The release owner has waived screenshot artifacts for v1.0.0; this does not waive manual behavior checks or their evidence records.\\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Record per-cell verdicts and observed outcomes against the exact installed RC artifact. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); manual behavior checks and their evidence records remain mandatory.\\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\\n \\n\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224800.746952}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
