igh-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. This is distinct from the neutral GitHub Entire Gates check. The merged commit remains subject to current-main CI, which is still running. PR #310 is the open documentation-only readiness refresh against this exact main revision; its Node 22/24 and Entire checks are running while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL have passed. PR #131 is post-v1 documentation.\n+**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be