very documented (PR293); runtime diagnostic handling fixed/tested (PR296). Current files are ~10 KB capabilities, ~16 KB operation model, ~24 KB scheduler, ~22 KB runner. Generated DAG invariant tests explore 100 fixed seeds; real-agent lifecycle integration tests exist. No remaining empty catch blocks in the operation runner modules. These are source-level observations; current main CI/full-suite results still pending.), updated about 3 hours ago\\n  - [doing] Close evaluation coverage gate with independent held-out qualification (details=Fresh Issue #1 check at 2026-10-28 20:24 UTC still OPEN/unassigned; no response to prior metadata-only request at 14:23. Sent a concise follow-up asking whether the independent author/custodian is active, for the next checkpoint, or for the authorized custody handoff path. Comment 6479873007; no payloads/answers/private digests requested. Public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance; compatibility blocker remains legacy hidden command format vs blackbox-v1 evaluator. Qualification remains unstarted and protected.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Refresh authoritative release state after Entire review (details=Current authoritative state refreshed 2026-10-28 20:06 UTC. origin/main=13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0; its CI run 40751988282 passed all required jobs. PR300 head f3957a67 and PR309 head aace981b are based on current main with Node22/24 still in progress at last check. PR308 head 2c1b2dfa remains on current base, Node24 succeeded, Node22 still running in run 40757432379. Main rules require Node22, Node24, Linux only and zero approving reviews; Entire Gates (including approval/finding signal) is not a required status check and must not be treated as a human reviewer blocker. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Verify Nexus host identity is independent of provider/model (details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: cli/src/agent.ts:232 injects explicit Nexus Code host identity and prohibits inferring host from provider/model; cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts covers it. Exact-main CI 40751988282 passed Node22, Node24 and Linux. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Verify sensitive-checkpoint failure offers operator choices (details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: REPL offers read-only, continue without rollback checkpoint, create checkpoint despite sensitive persistence risk, cancel, or re-enter; sidecar reports same options. Tests cover REPL and sidecar; exact-main CI 40751988282 passed all jobs. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Verify upgrade accepts signed GitHub release asset redirect (details=The RC7 failure URL host is now explicitly allowlisted in current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 only for the expected release-asset path (cli/src/upgrade.ts:665-671). cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts:159 covers a synthetic signed GitHub release URL and unsafe cases remain rejected. Exact-main CI run 40751988282 passed all three jobs. This source check does not replace running `nexus upgrade` on the successor exact RC/package or validate backup-time UX.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [doing] Reconcile doctor D1-D3 report against current main (details=Entire recall plus exact committed origin/main source/test inspection at 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0. D1 appears source-remediated: async opendir/lstat in batches of 128, bounded newest-record parsing, 30s default integrity deadline; committed tests assert event-loop responsiveness, bounded concurrency and deadline. D2 appears source-remediated: index.json is excluded, schema-v2 requires messageLog and rejects messages; schema-v1 keeps messages. D3 has intended distinction: absent /models entry is advisory WARN; --deep performs one inference and upgrades model.available only on success; committed tests cover that exact case. These are committed-source/test evidence, not rerun tests or live reproduction. Next: inspect exact current commit CI/test coverage if needed and reproduce on mike-dev state without altering user data; acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Verify RC7 download redirect rejection against current main (details=Verified main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 source/test and tag ancestry. Fix commit 64c22d3e6fc20c36432946abc8e237017d4b91be (2026-10-26 03:17 UTC) accepts the signed GitHub release-assets redirect only on /github-production-release-asset/. Regression coverage added in 1cce2f48. Fix is absent from v1.0.0-rc.7 history, present in rc.8, rc.9, and rc.10. So the reported RC7 rejection is explained by an older artifact; current source already has the fix. No current-main code change needed. XERJ field report submitted; HTTP 200.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [dropped] Refresh PR #300 readiness facts and obtain exact-diff independent review (details=Superseded by current PR #300 head c8df374 and exact-head CI monitor task; old branch/head status no longer current.), updated about 1 hour ago\\n  - [dropped] Refresh readiness checkpoint PR #300 (details=Duplicate created in prior work-state update; tracked under existing task Refresh readiness checkpoint and reconcile RC10 cross-runner evidence.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Reconcile reported missing local AI setup option (details=Verified exact public RC10 source/tag `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` includes Appliance in the provider connect list and endpoint/key setup (`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:300-347`); its TUI regression test explicitly asserts the connect menu shows Appliance and opens the local endpoint prompt (`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3117-3129`). Exact RC10 tag CI 40419408166 completed SUCCESS. Current main retains the implementation and exact-main CI 40751988282 passed. Thus this is fixed no later than RC10, but the earlier screenshot itself remains valid evidence against the installed older release; no new code change is needed.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] Monitor PR #308 exact-head CI and integrate reviewed checkpoint fixture fix (details=PR #308 merged after exact-head Node22, Node24, Linux packaging/tests, CodeQL and JS/TS passed; independent review ACCEPT. Merge commit 10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496.), updated 41 minutes ago\\n  - [done] Monitor PR #300 exact-head readiness correction checks (details=PR #300 merged through protected merge path at 2026-10-28T21:07:46Z as 79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da after exact-head Node22/24/Linux, JS/TS, CodeQL checks passed; independent review ACCEPT. Entire Gates remained pending but is not required by ruleset. The 20:18 checkpoint is timestamped and remains historical; refresh the same readiness file after PR #308 integration.), updated 52 minutes ago\\n  - [done] Monitor PR #309 exact-head RC10 ChatGPT provider evidence checks (details=Superseded by verified integration: PR #309 merged as b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af after required Node22/24, Linux package/reproducibility, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed. Exact evidence remains RC10-only.), updated about 1 hour ago\\n  - [doing] Verify PR #309 integration and main CI (details=PR #309 merged at 2026-10-28T20:36:21Z as b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af after independent ACCEPT and exact-head required checks (Node22, Node24, Linux package/reproducibility) passed. New main CI 40764779353 and CodeQL 40764779313 are both still in progress. No exact-RC acceptance claim.), updated about 1 hour ago\\n  - [done] Reconfirm successor RC needed before exact-RC/manual qualification (details=GitHub compare shows origin/main b3dea1a is 246 commits ahead of v1.0.0-rc.10 and changes 40 cli/src or core/src paths. RC10 cannot serve as exact candidate for current source. Ubuntu desktop was freshly reachable at 10.0.8.3; xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal and RC10 are installed. Do not count terminal cells until a candidate built from the final source revision is installed.), updated about 1 hour ago\\n  - [done] Monitor post-PR-308 main CI and refresh release readiness (details=Exact main SHA 10c84df run 40770466028 completed SUCCESS, including Node 22/24 tests, Rust and CLI tests, security gates, reproducible package, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL 40770465935 passed. See recovery CI log event at 22:00 UTC.), updated 1 minute ago\\n  - [doing] Post-308 readiness checkpoint PR (details=Remote PR #310 exact head 5afbae0e93de7a87a63cb69c2042315ea4d8bb43/base 10c84df is independent ACCEPT; reviewer /root/rc1_docs_review exact patch SHA256 e26884593defa7f97c96e34f4895636ce2de6496c923adb90b43cb7181cb16bf. It preserves the Entire trail23 finding as unresolved/unverified; the authenticated ubuntu-desktop query itself remains owner-reported, not independently reproduced. PR exact CI remains in progress, auto-merge enabled. Main run 40770466028 on 10c84df: Node22/24 and Linux npm test passed; Linux package build in progress, CodeQL pass. No tests run for docs.), updated 5 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] Respect screenshot-artifact waiver; continue terminal behavior qualification (details=User explicitly waived terminal screenshot artifacts for release. This waives screenshots only; live terminal behavior checks and evidence recording remain required. User reported render behavior across tested sizes, with tmux inside GNOME Terminal at 43x13 as the known exception; evaluate whether that human report can satisfy any matrix cells, and do remaining cells on exact successor RC. Current successor RC not built/installed; do not count RC10.), updated 28 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] Align acceptance documentation with terminal screenshot-artifact waiver (details=Local commit b035e716657e467c71a2b1a3ef7981068dea0f0c