`b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The exact-main source CI status is recorded separately above.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819