{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:01:24.915Z","ordinal":466807,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e186b93d-907a-4b30-9bf5-66d1f264b9e9","process_id":"94788","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '25,40p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '25,40p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    25\t## User preferences\n    26\t\n    27\t- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n    28\t- the user required evidence-supported claims and separate ready/blocked dispositions -> local fixtures, structural checks, synthetic broker tests, and public video must not be presented as Cloudflare-backed acceptance; do not automate application entry. [Task 1]\n    29\t- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n    30\t- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n    31\t\n    32\t## Reusable knowledge\n    33\t\n    34\t- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n    35\t- Cloudflare contest rules require a 5–10 minute video, public source, run instructions, Workers and Artifacts usage, and an MIT/Apache/BSD license; automated application entry is prohibited. [Task 1]\n    36\t- Installed-runtime resolution needs `NEXUS_HOME`; source-oriented paths under `core/target` and repository-relative CLI paths are not sufficient after installation. [Task 2]\n    37\t- The stated support envelope is Linux x86-64/glibc with Node.js 20+; do not claim portability beyond it. The rollout records prerelease `v0.1.0-alpha.1`, release workflow `38459471967`, checksum `39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8`, and fresh-home installer verification. [Task 2]\n    38\t\n    39\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    40\t\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28520}},"started_at_ms":1793224884914,"completed_at_ms":1793224884915}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:01:26.048Z","ordinal":466808,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18488-4720-7fc1-90c8-da96a464a398","call_id":"call_7091a2f79bd348f29564d2c637a1af8d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    25\t## User preferences\n    26\t\n    27\t- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n    28\t- the user required evidence-supported claims and separate ready/blocked dispositions -> local fixtures, structural checks, synthetic broker tests, and public video must not be presented as Cloudflare-backed acceptance; do not automate application entry. [Task 1]\n    29\t- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n    30\t- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n    31\t\n    32\t## Reusable knowledge\n    33\t\n    34\t- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n    35\t- Cloudflare contest rules require a 5–10 minute video, public source, run instructions, Workers and Artifacts usage, and an MIT/Apache/BSD license; automated application entry is prohibited. [Task 1]\n    36\t- Installed-runtime resolution needs `NEXUS_HOME`; source-oriented paths under `core/target` and repository-relative CLI paths are not sufficient after installation. [Task 2]\n    37\t- The stated support envelope is Linux x86-64/glibc with Node.js 20+; do not claim portability beyond it. The rollout records prerelease `v0.1.0-alpha.1`, release workflow `38459471967`, checksum `39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8`, and fresh-home installer verification. [Task 2]\n    38\t\n    39\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    40\t\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793224886.0486648}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
