{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:17:45.889Z","ordinal":467473,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18497-3aa1-7212-8e4e-a52c89e25128","call_id":"call_6ca64002c4e74526a8c4047cd6543eb7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 11.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 17745)\nTotal output lines: 179\n\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/tasks/lessons.md:33:  request after a load-induced timeout). Rule: one test run at a time per machine; take the `SUITE` claim\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/tasks/lessons.md:38:- 2026-10-16: I ran targeted tests and live calls while another agent's `SUITE` claim was held, because I checked\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/CONTRIBUTING.md:24:The complete suite needs Linux isolation facilities and security tools configured by the CI workflow. Do not disable isolation to obtain a pass. Report environmental blockers and exact commands/results. Tests and probes must use disposable user state; never point them at your normal `~/.nexus`. On a shared development host, acquire the documented `SUITE` claim before running any tests and use a committed snapshot for full suites.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_safe_fs.ts/owner.json:9:  \"status\": \"Refreshed PR207 candidate; no content change from independently accepted 3a5fc8e diff. Exact diff-check PASS; independent re-review pending. Tests/push wait for active SUITE and post-merge full CI.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`; its latest follow-up scopes checkout to the nested workspace and extends the regression to preserve both staged and unstaged sibling state. The prior nested-index delta at `662d084` was independently ACCEPTed (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`), and the checkout-scope delta was independently ACCEPTed by `review_pr302` (SHA-256 `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`, tests not run). PR #302 CodeQL and JS/TS checks pass; Node 22/24 CI and Entire are running. TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed on the prior delta; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:47:**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:597:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_repl.ts/owner.json:10:  \"scope\": \"Resolve REPL pending prompt on stdin EOF using existing exit signal; add EOF regression in operator_config_startup.test.ts. No tests while SUITE claim is held; no merge without exact CI and independent review.\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_DEFECT_UPGRADE_REGULAR_LAUNCHER_RECOVERY_20261027/owner.json:10:  \"status\": \"Ready for owner PR and exact-head CI; not integrated. SUITE and hot-file claims released\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:102:  \"terminal_matrix\": \"0/15; user cannot run the xterm 80x24 cell now. No manual checks started. Idle SUITE/GATEWAY claims released and logged; worksheet/procedure remains ready.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_OPERATION_RUNNER_REBASE_20261028/owner.json:8:  \"status\": \"review_correction_committed_and_pushed; npm_build_and_diff_check_pass; focused_test_waits_for_SUITE_claim; fresh_exact_CI_and_review_pending\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/POST_CONTEST_DEP_UPDATE_PR126/owner.json:11:  \"safe_boundary\": \"clean local merge commit; diff-check and JSON parse passed; worktree preserved; no tests, push, or PR merge; acquire SUITE and complete exact-head checks before any remote update\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_DEFECT_LOCAL_CHAT_MODEL_FILTER/owner.json:10:  \"status\": \"Ready for owner PR after cache-origin parent a52d7f31; exact-head CI pending. SUITE, GATEWAY and file claims released\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_operator_config_startup.test.ts/owner.json:11:  \"status\": \"takeover: diagnose/fix package smoke EOF exit 13; no tests while SUITE claimed; no merge until exact CI and independent review\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/SEC_CODEQL_EVAL_TEST_SCRIPT_ARGS_20261026/owner.json:6:  \"scope\": \"replace dynamic node -e interpolation in cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts with fixture script files and argv; address CodeQL alerts 48/49; no test run until existing SUITE claim releases\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_doctor.test.ts/owner.json:11:  \"status\": \"Refreshed PR207 candidate; no content change from independently accepted 3a5fc8e diff. Exact diff-check PASS; independent re-revie…12745 tokens truncated… test.** Extend the operationRig (`durable_continuity.test.ts:152-178`): small `contextLimit` with a gateway returning large tool outputs so the **auto** path (`agent.ts:3051`, `trigger: \"auto\"`) commits compaction mid-turn on the depth-1 `durable: true` work-unit agent; kill the agent process (crash-child pattern as in `compaction_continuity.test.ts:536-541`) at the commit boundary; resume via a fresh executor + `recoverFromTaskState`; assert `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the auto compaction id, `read_archive` returns the originals, and no action is replayed (cf. the no-replay assertion `compaction_continuity.test.ts:566`). This requires running the suite (SUITE claim) → **deferred to execution; the test specification itself is statically closable now.**\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md:157:| M3 | confirmed | ACC-CONT-03 (SPEC-04:146) | Test spec now; execution deferred (SUITE) |\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md:15:Focused validation: `node --import tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 test/{session_state_v2,task_state_v2,task_message_log,state,state_migration,file_guard,retention,retention_state_v2,persistence_protection,egress_persistence_equivalence,upgrade_transaction_recovery}.test.ts`: **143/143 pass**, zero failures/skips. `tsc --noEmit`: exit0. All HOME/XDG/TMPDIR roots isolated under /var/tmp; local SUITE claimed. No inference or held-out data accessed.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:38:Separation: the implementation agents (codex app-server sessions and `kiro-cli` on the Nexus repository) authored nothing. The custodian authored nothing and edited task files never; it edited store bookkeeping (`ASSIGNMENT-*.md`, `AUTHOR-TRANSFER-2026-10-18.md`, `AGENTS.md`) and ran the validator. Authors never ran `bin/validate.py` and never held the `SUITE` claim.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:42:Every task was validated by the custodian in a bounded, atomically claimed `SUITE` window (claim log lines `CLAIM SUITE opencode v7/v8/v9/v10/v11`, each released with `RELEASE SUITE`). Rounds: batches 1–7 one round each (windows v7, v8); batches 8–9 and the repaired task two rounds each (v9–v11). Per-task logs: `reference/<id>.validation.log` in the store. Claim-log evidence: one `VALIDATED <id> rounds=N (<window>)` line per task; latest line governs.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:89:`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log`, 2026-10-18: `TRANSFER HELDOUT authorship` 02:25:21Z; `BROKEN CLAIM HELDOUT_AUTHORING_B8` 02:33:14Z; `ABORT … author-b8r` 02:35Z; `REJECT HELDOUT batch 9` 02:37Z; `CLAIM/RELEASE SUITE opencode v9` 02:4xZ–02:54:09Z, `v10` 02:5xZ–03:01:22Z, `v11` 03:0xZ–03:05Z; `CUSTODY NOTE v9`, `CUSTODY HOLD` 02:54:09Z; `VALIDATED` lines per task; `BOUNDARY REQUEST (QUALIFICATION BLOCKER)` 03:05:08Z.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_COMPONENT_COHERENCE/README.md:5:Focused validation: 15/15 tests passed on mike-dev with atomic SUITE ownership and throwaway HOME/XDG state. Tests cover coherent stable/prerelease/build versions and each component mismatching by version, prerelease, or build; they exercise updater eligibility, archive binding and the standalone publisher validator. Existing read-only tsx executable from p10g-validation supplied the runner; no dependency files were changed. Full integration checks and independent review remain required. This does not close transaction recovery, legacy fallback, installed-RC qualification, or release acceptance.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:87:- **v2 batch 1 authored + custodian-verified.** `ho2-py-bugfix-01` (more-itertools @ `1ea82a7`) and `ho2-go-refactor-01` (google/uuid @ `6e10cd1`): schema OK for both; **all four manifest hashes re-derived exactly** by the custodian; reference patches + validation logs present. Live `bin/validate.py` runs are **deferred** (SUITE held) — recorded in each validation log; custodian to run 2 rounds per task when SUITE frees.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:90:- **Corpus progress (store v2):** batches 1–3 authored → **11 tasks**; custodian re-derived **all 11 manifest hash pairs exactly** (5/5 batch 3 re-verified separately after the author's self-check) and `check_schema.mjs` reports OK × 11. Live `bin/validate.py` runs for all 11 remain **deferred pending a SUITE window** (pending notes + author-side dry-run sequences recorded per task). Remaining: ~29 tasks to the 40 target, custodian validation, then sealing.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:7:| Claim protocol | `SUITE` taken atomically (`mkdir`), **ownership recheck before every phase** (owner.json agent+pid must match the watcher's own), released **only if still owned** at exit (claim log 18:56:33Z CLAIM → 19:24:21Z RELEASE; codex re-took at 19:24:39Z — no overlap) |\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:43:Watcher v3 aborted fail-closed immediately after taking the claim (20:38:51Z) and left its own dead-pid claim in place: its `owns_claim` pid pattern was corrupted by a quoted heredoc (`\\$` escaped the dollar → the pattern never matched). The stale claim was logged and released by the owner-of-record at 20:51:47Z; v4/v5 use a `printf`-built fixed-string pattern. codex's 20:44:48Z \"REQUEST SUITE release … codex will wait\" was honoured. No suites overlapped at any point.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/publication-gating.md:15:- REQ-AGT-118: changed tests executed (SUITE window) + independent acceptance of DEC-17 (review is approve-with-issues; acceptance pending).\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:13:| focused `tokens.test.ts` | **3/3 PASS** (watcher v6, 23:16:36Z, SUITE window) | **3/3 PASS** by independent coordinator `codex-lead` (record below) |\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:29:- **31 authored** (batches 1–7), **30 custodian-validated** via `bin/validate.py` in bounded SUITE windows (v7: 25/26 in 12 min; v8: 5/5), all 31 manifest hash pairs re-derived exactly; schema OK × 31.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:32:- Validation incident (diagnostic): the first validation window (v6) self-deadlocked — `validate.py` waits on the SUITE claim that the custodian's own window holds — so its 420 s \"timeouts\" were deadlock waits, not task failures. Fixed with a documented kill-switch `HELDOUT_CLAIMWAIT=0` in the store's `claimwait.py`; evidence of the invalid window preserved.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:37:SUITE windows rotated codex ↔ opencode (v4, v5, v6, v7, v8) with zero overlaps; every opencode window took the claim atomically, rechecked ownership before executing, and released only its own claim. One protocol incident (v3 quoting bug, fail-closed) is documented in `test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md`.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:67:REQUIREMENTS.md:153 keeps REQ-AGT-118 `partial` with \"Changed-test execution and independent review are **pending**\". Reality matches: docs + test/fixture changed; the SUITE claim is held by codex (verified: `nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json`, pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z); verification.md:29,32 explicitly defers execution, states a ledger pass \"is not behavioural acceptance\", and lists the re-run steps. This reviewer likewise did not run the suite. REQ-QUAL-105 staying `tested` is defensible: the injector/smoke tests (EVL-001) are unchanged and the 8→9 correction is docs-only. ✓\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:96:- Ledger status promoted to `tested` before the changed test executes on a free SUITE (not present — `partial` is correct).\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:45:- Batch 1 authored (`ho2-py-bugfix-01`, `ho2-go-refactor-01`); custodian re-derived all four manifest hashes exactly; live validation deferred to a SUITE window. See `custody-report-2026-10-17.md` §5.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/verification.md:29:- `HOME=<tmp> node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` → **exit 0**; `requirements: 121 rows; tested 106, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7`. **This establishes ledger integrity only.** REQ-AGT-118 remains `partial`: the changed test has not been executed (SUITE held), and the DEC-17 amendment review is approve-with-issues (below). A ledger pass is **not** behavioural acceptance.\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/verification.md:38:- **Test execution deferred:** the `SUITE` claim is held by `codex` (pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z), so no suite or targeted test was run on this machine. RE-RUN when `SUITE` is free:\n/tmp/nexus-pr176-review.YEHLNr/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/README.md:11:Validation: retention.test.ts plus retention_state_v2.test.ts:20/20 passed, no failures/skips. tsc --noEmit:exit0. Negative controls:3 expected failures,8 filtered tests, not acceptance passes. HOME/XDG/TMPDIR were isolated under /var/tmp with the local SUITE claim.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","create_time":1793225865.8894892}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
