/tokens_probe.ts\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS-62-a2354cc98b5a4ca354e7e77e61c9cba2901aa19a4c263ac544a4b850ceb1ef83  evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS-63-d569652b3b153a3d90a3f8a1de092f60942734226408dec8eb1db951bca339ea  evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS-64-2884a72e89b6a024382dc029df0540dff04f0ed09201daeca5bf2b74f5595bc9  evidence/probes/e_run.sh\n--\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-3-Source base d7e79139028813eaee11437db91bb80c00e8cdb1. Addresses issue49 finding6254719484. The version probe already applies CPU, memory and process limits but creates its writable sandbox workspace under os.tmpdir(), bypassing the dedicated capped filesystem. It now allocates under resources.workspaceRoot when resources are configured. Existing fail-closed resource validation runs before resolveAgentIdentity; no-resources development behavior keeps its original temporary-directory fallback.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-4-\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-5-A separate production-path regression invokes the real eval/run.mjs with an empty synthetic task set and a synthetic Goose executable. The executable checks its actual working filesystem device and size against the configured capped mount, writes a file and returns its version. The test requires successful identity discovery, manifest recording and workspace cleanup. Its local HTTP server returns only synthetic model metadata; no model inference, private tasks, gateway or credentials are used. Its child process group and pipes have bounded cleanup.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-6-\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md:7:Validation: runner syntax check passed. Local WSL attempted the regression with isolated HOME/XDG and failed at its explicit precondition because that host lacks the dedicated capped/cgroup CI fixture; local-precondition.tap preserves this result. This is not a functional pass. CI and release workflows already provide NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and user-cgroup fixtures. Required exact-head hosted checks and independent review are pending. No mike-dev test started: two older foreign evaluator test processes remain live in p10i, untouched by this slice.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-8-\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md-9-Independent source/design review of the initial502b4aa identified two fixture-only contract mistakes: expectedAgentVersion must contain SemVer alone, and the selected temporary executable must use the existing exact allowedFiles path rather than a forbidden /tmp runtime-root allowlist. Both were corrected without weakening production validation; the test title now describes the workspace scope. Corrected local attempt remains blocked at the same missing-fixture precondition, preserved separately in corrected-local-precondition.tap. Original local-precondition.tap is historical draft evidence, not a claim of functional validation at the corrected commit. Hosted results remain required.\n--\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/corrected-local-precondition.tap-4-  ---\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/corrected-local-precondition.tap-5-  duration_ms: 2.246404\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLA