{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:06.504Z","ordinal":467589,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2758d7f1881a09bd79ffc6a13c095","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7a91c7f550f84f19be9b3f17e613b2ea","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,140p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; rg -n \\\"PACKAGE_QUALIFICATION|reproducib|package-linux|builder\\\" docs/v1.0.0 scripts .github/workflows -g '*.md' -g '*.yml' -g '*.sh' | head -120; ls -la .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW/owner.json 2>/dev/null\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:5000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","create_time":1793226125.4997947}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:06.598Z","ordinal":467590,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae27584cc0881a093b0fc6ca71da94c","usage":{"input_tokens":118513,"cached_input_tokens":117376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1153,"reasoning_output_tokens":965,"total_tokens":119666},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":352697,"cached_input_tokens":348800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1961,"reasoning_output_tokens":1392,"total_tokens":354658},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8638311670,"cached_input_tokens":8546167808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24588597,"reasoning_output_tokens":14166277,"total_tokens":8662900267}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:09.936Z","ordinal":467591,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a5d105a4-b451-4bd3-bf55-c4371ee33a9f","process_id":"37017","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,140p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; rg -n \"PACKAGE_QUALIFICATION|reproducib|package-linux|builder\" docs/v1.0.0 scripts .github/workflows -g '*.md' -g '*.yml' -g '*.sh' | head -120; ls -la .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW/owner.json 2>/dev/null"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,140p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; rg -n \"PACKAGE_QUALIFICATION|reproducib|package-linux|builder\" docs/v1.0.0 scripts .github/workflows -g '*.md' -g '*.yml' -g '*.sh' | head -120; ls -la .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW/owner.json 2>/dev/null"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:159:**Chosen:** Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22 for v1.0.0. The owner selected Node 22 as the minimum on 2026-10-22 because Node 20 reached end of life on 2026-04-30; v1.0.0 must not require or build on an end-of-life Node runtime. Validate Node 22 and 24 in the source CI matrix, with release and reproducibility builds on Node 22. The docs keep the conservative glibc \"≥ 2.35\" claim; the binaries reference glibc symbols ≤ 2.34. macOS, arm64 and musl are post-v1 roadmap items.\nscripts/package-linux.sh:16:VERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:17:OUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:22:    echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder (set NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1 only for local development)\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:26:  echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:183:# path remains host-built and must not be used as reproducibility evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:50:| REQ-REL-06..09 | REL-001..004 | Lockfile provenance; SHA-256 + commit-bound release identity; SBOM hooks; patch obligations for supported public lines, EOL marking | P2 §23 | DEMONSTRATED (generate_sbom.sh; make verify-reproducibility) | P | Maturity review 10-12 P1: SBOM from direct deps only, not CycloneDX-validated; top-tier D4 no signing/provenance. Since 10-13: deterministic archive + CI reproducibility (87360e6, fa0959f), SHA256SUMS in releases. REL-004 now live obligation (repo PUBLIC, releases published) with no SECURITY.md process (D4) |\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:20:# 1. Generate Rust SBOM for the exact platform shipped by package-linux.sh.\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:168:# 4. Normalize metadata for reproducible builds if SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH or git commit is available\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:133:- **The docs are honest about the block:** CONTEST.md:15,65,89 and VIDEO_ASSET.md:19 do not claim reproducibility. Offline modes are labelled. In real-agent mode the demo labels the control/treatment contrast as historical (nexus-demo.mjs:313-314).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:167:| CON-R4 | One independent clean-account Cloudflare-backed end-to-end run, with a committed redacted run record | failure / evidence | BLOCKER (contest claim of reproducibility). Otherwise submit with an explicit \"operator-host only\" statement. | G1 procedure |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:36:- Launcher: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js` (scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30); no code path in\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:15:- `scripts/package-linux.sh` (deterministic packaging of compatibility metadata with reproducible timestamps)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:40:This records artifact identity, published checksums, provenance verification results, and an installed-package version/self-test. It does not establish provider behavior, upgrade behavior from RC6, held-out results, standalone engineering correctness, T3/T4 results, cross-runner reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, or independent RC acceptance. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:29:| scripts/package-linux.sh | targeted (packaged bin/nexus) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:43:- Entry points: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js \"$@\"` (package-linux.sh:25-30); no args -> `repl`\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:60:| TUI-04 | S2 | Install -> first run | scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30; index.ts:747; live.rs:126-131; tui.ts:59-90 | SOURCE+RUNTIME: packaged `nexus` = REPL; no command reaches the live TUI; packaged `lib/core/nexus-tui --live` fails \"sidecar not found at <pkg>/cli/dist/sidecar.js\" (checkout-layout assumption `ancestors().nth(4)`). ISSUE12 UI-004 (\"TUI MUST serve as the default interactive human surface\" — Satisfied) is false for the shipped package | Release users get the weaker REPL (TUI-02/03/08 apply) and never the hardened TUI | Make `nexus` launch `nexus-tui --live` on a TTY with packaged sidecar path; resolve packaged layout |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:19:- `harness.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh` (CA export)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:37:| 12 | Custom CA: document `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` in config.env; the launcher (node entry re-exec, or `bin/nexus` sh) exports it before node starts; doctor validates that the file exists and parses. | `scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30` launcher; `harness.sh`; `doctor.ts` | PLAN-06 task 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:12:- `scripts/package-linux.sh`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:14:| scripts/package-linux.sh, smoke-package.sh, installer-smoke.sh, package-smoke-*.{py,mjs}, security_gates.sh, audit_rust_deps.py, generate_sbom.sh, token_accounting.py | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:32:- **Release pipeline.** A tag `v*.*.*` triggers `release.yml`. The workflow checks that the tag commit is an ancestor of origin/main and that the tag matches `package.json` version. It then runs `npm ci`, the cli build, `cargo test --locked`, the release build, `npm test`, and security_gates. Next it runs `package-linux.sh` twice and `cmp`s the outputs (a reproducibility check), then `smoke-package.sh` and `installer-smoke.sh`. Finally `softprops/action-gh-release` uploads `nexus-linux-x86_64-<tag>.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS`, setting prerelease when the tag contains `-`. Release notes come from `generate_release_notes`; `docs/releases/*.md` is not used.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:59:| REL-01 | S2 | install → first run | scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30; cli/src/index.ts:747-749; harness.sh:21-38 | RUNTIME. Installed `nexus` (no args) opens the readline REPL. `nexus --live` → `error: unknown option '--live'`. The packaged launcher has no route to the live TUI (`nexus-tui --live --sidecar`), although nexus-tui and sidecar.js are shipped and doctor reports `PASS tui.build: The live TUI ... built`. | Release users never get the primary UI that the developer uses and that the PTY tests cover. The shipped product is a different product from the tested daily driver. The doctor's PASS is misleading. | Make the packaged launcher equal to harness.sh: same routing, and live TUI when there are no args and a TTY. Add a smoke test that the package launches `--live` in a PTY. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:63:| REL-05 | S2 | compliance | scripts/package-linux.sh:22; release assets | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates are statically linked (Cargo.lock: 152 packages, MIT/Apache-2.0 etc.), and there is no third-party notice for them. Node deps ship their own LICENSE files (20 found). No SBOM is published. | MIT/Apache attribution obligations are not met for redistributed binaries. Enterprise intake (SBOM) is blocked. | Generate THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (cargo-about / cargo-deny licenses + npm license list) and a real lockfile-based SBOM, and attach both to releases. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:74:| MNT-03 | S4 | maintainability | Makefile:36-45 | SOURCE. `verify-reproducibility` writes fixed `/tmp/nexus-repro-{1,2}` and covers only cli/dist, not the release tarball. The real check lives in the workflows (`cmp` of two package builds, same machine and same toolchain). | Weak local repro check. Cross-machine reproducibility is not proven. | Point the target at `package-linux.sh` twice + `cmp`, using mktemp. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:127:  - Two package builds are `cmp`-compared for byte reproducibility.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:137:- **Cross-machine reproducibility is unproven.** The CI repro check runs on the same runner with the same toolchain. To qualify: build the tag on two different machines or runner images with a pinned toolchain, then `cmp` the tarballs and the published SHA256SUMS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:10:- `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`, `scripts/security_gates.sh`, `scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:26:| 2 | Third-party notices: install cargo-about and the npm license checker in CI. Use `about.toml` with an allowlist (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, MPL-2.0 only if reviewed). Have `package-linux.sh` write `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and upload it as an asset. | `package-linux.sh:22`; `release.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:30:| 6 | Add a CI matrix for Node 22/24 (tests). Packaging, release and reproducibility builds use Node 22. Pin the cargo-audit version. | `ci.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:32:| 8 | Delete `.gitlab-ci.yml`. Remove tracked `*.pyc` and ignore them. Point `make verify-reproducibility` at `package-linux.sh` run twice with mktemp and cmp. | `.gitlab-ci.yml`; `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/harness/__pycache__`; `Makefile:36-45` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:34:| 10 | Cross-runner reproducibility: a workflow_dispatch job builds on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 with the pinned toolchain and compares the outputs. Run it once for the RC. | new `.github/workflows/repro.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:14:| C6 | Clean-account run (owner action X6): fresh VM and Cloudflare account. Follow the G1 procedure in `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` §6 and commit a redacted run record. | — | Required for a reproducibility claim |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:16:**Two launchers.** The developer launcher is `harness.sh` (on this host, `/usr/local/bin/nexus`). With no arguments on a TTY it starts the Ratatui live TUI. The packaged launcher `bin/nexus` (`scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30`) is `node lib/cli/dist/index.js \"$@\"`. With no arguments it starts the readline REPL (`cli/src/index.ts:747-749`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Build entry points | `make build` (cargo release + `tsc`), `make test` (cargo test + `npm --prefix cli test` + `scripts/security_gates.sh`), `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/smoke-package.sh`, `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`. CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (contest contract job + `linux-x86_64`), `release.yml` (tag-triggered). A dead `.gitlab-ci.yml` also exists. | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:265:| REL-01 | S2 | B | Install → first run | `package-linux.sh:24-30`; `index.ts:747` | RT | The installed product lacks the TUI | REQ-REL-101 (SPEC-06) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:360:  - Same-runner byte-reproducible packages.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:374:- No cross-runner reproducibility check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:33:The deadline recorded in the contest docs is 2026-10-14. The owner confirmed the submission is complete; operator work state records submission id `e05006b6-…` at revision `ce7e58b9`. Contest submission readiness is therefore **closed as submitted**. The findings below describe the state of the submitted tree: reproducibility of the submission is limited to the operator host (CON-002, CON-005). They are a hardening backlog, not a submission gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:133:| ACC-UPG-13 | Public-Release Upgrade Acceptance | Tests reproducible end-to-end upgrade from prior public release (`v0.1.0-alpha.2`) with preserved state, doctor, CLI, TUI, and restart verification. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:17:| REL-05 | The release archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates (MIT/Apache-2.0 and others) are statically linked into `harness-core` and `nexus-tui`, with no attribution. No SBOM is published. | RUNTIME + SOURCE (`scripts/package-linux.sh:22`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:24:| MNT-03 | `make verify-reproducibility` writes fixed `/tmp` paths and covers dist only. | SOURCE |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:47:8. **REQ-REL-114.** Cross-machine reproducibility is demonstrated once for the RC: two different runner images with the pinned toolchain produce identical tarballs. This is RELEASE-REQUIRED evidence, not a code change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:54:  - `package-linux.sh` concatenates both into the archive root.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:58:- **CI.** `strategy.matrix.node: [22, 24]` for the test job. Packaging, release and reproducibility builds run on Node 22. Add `cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version <pin>`. Add a step `git diff --exit-code -- cli/dist` after the build.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:68:| ACC-SUP-05 | The CI matrix is green on Node 22 and 24, release and reproducibility packaging use Node 22, and the dist-freshness step is present. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:71:| ACC-SUP-08 | Cross-runner reproducibility: tarballs built on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 runners with the pinned toolchain are byte-identical, or the differences are documented and accepted as a DEC-10 follow-up. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:77:| REQ-REL-002 | release.yml | Release is gated on main ancestry, a version match, the full suite, a same-runner byte-reproducible package, and package and installer smoke tests. | `.github/workflows/release.yml` | RT (CI log 905/905) | tested | N | Cross-runner reproducibility unproven | ACC-SUP-08 | K | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:186:| REQ-REL-101 | UI-004 (carried) | The packaged `nexus` opens the live TUI on a TTY. One launcher grammar. | primary workflow | `index.ts:747`; `package-linux.sh:24-30`; `live.rs:126-131` | TEST (ACC-PKG-01; test:cli/test/harness_entry.test.ts) | tested | ACC-PKG-01 | **B** | REL-01, TUI-04, DX-05 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:196:| REQ-REL-107 | License obligations | Third-party notices for all redistributed dependencies. | legal / compliance | `package-linux.sh` | TEST (ACC-SUP-01; test:scripts/check_notices.mjs, scripts/smoke-package.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-01 | **B** | REL-05 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:200:| REQ-REL-111 | Audit; DEC-12 | CI matrix for Node 22/24; release, reproducibility and evaluator builds use Node 22; pinned toolchain and MSRV, engines field, dist freshness (untracked). | compatibility | `ci.yml`, `release.yml`, `repro.yml` | At exact candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9`, PR #150 CI run `39866110578` passed both required matrix jobs (Node 22 job `120128589470`; Node 24 job `120128589221`). The same revision declares Node `>=22` in both package manifests, uses pinned Rust/MSRV, sets release and reproducibility packaging to Node 22, and runs the `cli/dist` freshness check in the matrix and package workflows. Exact-candidate Linux packaging remains a separate active source gate; this row covers ACC-SUP-05 only. | tested | ACC-SUP-05 | RR | REL-13, MNT-01 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:17:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`. Exact-head CI run [40720824591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824591) passed the Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices; the Linux packaging/reproducibility job was still running at observation time. CodeQL run [40720824319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824319) passed. The CI jobs completed `sync-version --check` and the requirements checker successfully on this source. These results qualify the source revision only; they do not qualify an installed release candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:25:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:53:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC quali