{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:30.646Z","ordinal":467606,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2759eec2481a0ba35553163227bcd","usage":{"input_tokens":130049,"cached_input_tokens":124928,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":784,"reasoning_output_tokens":767,"total_tokens":130833},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":607739,"cached_input_tokens":592128,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3284,"reasoning_output_tokens":2519,"total_tokens":611023},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8638566712,"cached_input_tokens":8546411136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24589920,"reasoning_output_tokens":14167404,"total_tokens":8663156632}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:31.943Z","ordinal":467607,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1849b-9807-7652-949a-59145debad03","call_id":"call_a0398ae02f85430fbccdda632a2dc956","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At `origin/main@13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0` (merge #305, `2026-10-28T15:11:02-04:00`), the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still has 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and four languages.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open and unassigned. Its latest comment, #6479873007 (`2026-10-28 20:24 UTC`), is a coordinator request for ownership/status or a safe handoff. No custodian response or handoff is visible in the issue or claims. The October 18 T2 report records historical corpus custody acceptance, but explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance.\\n\\nPR #33 is merged, but its hardened legacy support does not satisfy the current qualification contract: `eval/validate.mjs:49` and `eval/run.mjs:718` still reject legacy hidden commands during qualification; the README directs custodian-led conversion or replacement with fresh custody checks and a new manifest identity.\\n\\nSafe evaluator work can continue with synthetic compatibility tests and reconciliation of PR #33’s historical decision against the current fail-closed policy. Whether conversion preserves T2 validator semantics still requires custodian input. No private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact commit `4c4df05a32889dae251750780880b6d4d61401eb` atop `b84c542de6a4c8de918bd6441b08c0bf1c0affd9`; diff SHA-256 `9becc0ae105bd658fd8ca73e57d3a18380f134babf37980d751984f4e3e7d9d9`.\\n\\n`read_all_lines` collects into a `Result`, so a mid-stream read error discards accumulated lines. `batch_read` then emits a failed entry with empty content and zero lines. The deterministic fixture injects an error after yielding a line and exercises that same collector used by `batch_read`.\\n\\nI did not run tests; the focused test pass is implementer-reported.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","create_time":1793226151.9437747}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
