{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:51.408Z","ordinal":467622,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae275ba021481a08b60cc260477abfb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dc0c921028c84c319d0efe10efd795b5","name":"exec","input":"const res=await Promise.all([\n tools.mcp__xerj__xerj_search({prefix:\"nexus-docs\",query:\"legacy hidden commands qualification validator migration custodian\",size:5,max_tokens:1800}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git grep -n -i -E 'legacy|hidden command|qualification' -- eval/validate.mjs eval/run.mjs docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -130; git grep -n 'eval/validate.mjs\\\\|eval/run.mjs' -- docs/v1.0.0 scripts | head -80\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4000})\n]);\ntext(\"XERJ:\\n\"+JSON.stringify(res[0]).slice(0,8000));\ntext(\"REPO:\\n\"+res[1].output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","create_time":1793226170.0105646}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:51.539Z","ordinal":467623,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae275b561a881a0a4db20b9daf483f4","usage":{"input_tokens":133303,"cached_input_tokens":131328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":676,"reasoning_output_tokens":448,"total_tokens":133979},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":872407,"cached_input_tokens":853376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4699,"reasoning_output_tokens":3415,"total_tokens":877106},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8638831380,"cached_input_tokens":8546672384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24591335,"reasoning_output_tokens":14168300,"total_tokens":8663422715}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:22:54.080Z","ordinal":467624,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-00f0a094-896a-4bf6-9a21-01c485975b78","process_id":"46905","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'legacy|hidden command|qualification' -- eval/validate.mjs eval/run.mjs docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -130; git grep -n 'eval/validate.mjs\\|eval/run.mjs' -- docs/v1.0.0 scripts | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'legacy|hidden command|qualification' -- eval/validate.mjs eval/run.mjs docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md","query":"legacy|hidden command|qualification","path":"validate.mjs"},{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -n \"eval/validate.mjs\\\\|eval/run.mjs\" -- docs/v1.0.0 scripts","query":"eval/validate.mjs\\|eval/run.mjs","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:36:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:53:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:55:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:60:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:67:4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:208:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:338:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:340:  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:346:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:24:| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:62:**Options.** (A) Fully supported. **(B, chosen)** Shipped and labelled **experimental** in help and docs. Excluded from the qualification task-quality claims. But the following are still fixed for v1:\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:110:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:128:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:171:- During that historical freeze, one exception was considered: if contest rules permitted errata, an erratum could state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and reproduction is operator-host only. That restriction ended with judging; it does not limit current maintenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:174:**Tradeoff:** judges who follow the documented deploy may deploy the legacy Worker. That Worker deploys into their own account, so the exposure is confined to their own test deployment.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:188:## DEC-16: Standalone qualification under a gateway-only environment\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:237:**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7:**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:The checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence; their source revision, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this observation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:25:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:27:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source CI is mostly complete on `145d464`; PR #302's latest delta awaits independent review and exact Node 22/24 completion, while #307 has independent source review but exact PR checks remain pending. RC10 has passing, bounded provider and cross-runner evidence, but no accepted RC exists and mandatory qualification remains open. Publication authorization remains granted and gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:33:**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:41:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:45:**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:53:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:57:The 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:61:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:71:The 03:50 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:83:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease, built from immutable source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and was last updated 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC; no custodian acceptance or compatible sealed held-out corpus is recorded, and no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts**, with no screenshots. The operator reports successful rendering at tested sizes but a 43×13 lower limit for tmux inside GNOME Terminal; this is partial observation, not completion of the prescribed matrix. The available `mike-dev` shell is headless, and its configured `ubuntu-desktop` host name does not resolve, so I could not produce real-terminal screenshots or verdicts from this session. Stable publication remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:91:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:97:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:103:**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:113:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:119:**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on pa\n... command output truncated for persistence .