nce.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:383:**RC7 qualification evidence:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` remains the latest published candidate, resolving to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; its Linux archive digest remains `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. Cross-runner reproducibility passed for RC7 only (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)); ChatGPT provider verification passed 3/3 on the installed RC7 using `gpt-6-luna`. A fresh provider-status check on the Ubuntu desktop at 01:54 UTC found ChatGPT connected and OpenRouter disconnected. RC7 evidence does not qualify a later candidate or establish acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:385:**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:393:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest,