d installer checks passed. At this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source gates do not constitute installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:409:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:411:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:415:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:421:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:423:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:425:**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:429:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:433:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:435:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:437:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:443:**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:445:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:447:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:449:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Next source action is to finish exact post-merge CI on `1b9791f`; after it passes, proceed through the accepted RC3 workflow and exact-artifact qualification. Held-out qualification remains dependent on the independent custodian and cannot start before custody and runner compatibility are accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:453:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:455:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in the isolated readiness worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only; it does not qualify an installed RC or change any acceptance threshold.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:457:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:463:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:465:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:471:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:473:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `fa16045`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a clean detached Git worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. Retained stdout is in the [exact-main enforcement record](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/requirements-enforce-main-fa16045.txt). It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only. It does not qualify an installed RC or change any requirement's acceptance threshold.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:479:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:483:The authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:489:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:497:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, PR #140's merge commit. Exact-main CI [39747222866](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222866) passed all four jobs on that exact SHA: Node 20, 22, 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging, including the CLI suite and package smoke check. Exact-main CodeQL [39747222840](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222840) passed. PR #140's host report is synthetic-only: 10/10 infrastructure checks passed and independent review accepted it; it does not establish held-out qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:225:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:226:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:227:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:175:| REQ-PRV-106 | Standalone commitment; HIST-08; DEC-16 | Standalone qualification: (a) live runs through the gateway-stripping proxy, in plain and emulated-server profiles; (b) server-kind conformance fixtures. | standalone (product principle) | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | TEST (test:cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts); eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs; **RT 2026-10-17 @a2abdf7:** live dry run through the gateway, llama.cpp profile, 1 development task VERIFIED with hidden and regression tests passing (`evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/`). Gap: `eval/run.mjs` always passes `--context-limit`, so the discovered context is never the source in profile runs (boundary request logged). Product-qualified needs the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 matrix on the RC. | tested | ACC-INF-10, ACCEPTANCE §4.2 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05, PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:36:| eval/run.mjs, score.mjs, infra.mjs, README.md, configs/*.json | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:94:| EVL-003 | S3 | Contamination control | eval/run.mjs:57-59,178; score.mjs:80-84 | SOURCE. Agents run as the operator's user with the task dir (including hidden tests) readable. Detection catches only (a) a changed task dir or (b) the task path appearing in agent stdout or stderr. Peers rarely echo tool output. Contaminated runs are counted but **still included** in the pooled pass rate. | Hidden-test leakage might go undetected and would be scored. | Stage hidden tests outside the readable tree (another uid, or copy in after the run from a root-only dir). Exclude contaminated runs from the pooled rate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:95:| EVL-004 | S3 | Matched-condition identity | eval/run.mjs:31,50,114,118; configs/pilot-*.json | SOURCE. The manifest records the model *alias* (`engineering/lead`) but not the weights digest, server build or sampling parameters. No temperature or seed is set for Nexus or peers (each uses its own defaults). The full operator `process.env` is inherited (:114), so ambient env can differ per agent. Concurrent agents share one gateway, which the pilot notes inflated wall times. | \"Same model, same budget\" is asserted, not recorded. Speed comparisons are confounded. | Record a gateway model fingerprint (GGUF sha, llama.cpp build, sampling) per run. Use a minimal allow-listed env. Run serially, or report queueing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md:16:**Gap found.** Nexus reported `context 65536 (operator)`, because `eval/run.mjs` always passes `--context-limit` (from\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md:19:`eval/run.mjs`. `discovery supported` confirms that the `/props` probe itself answered.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:31:- `eval/run.mjs`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:47:| 8 | Update the eval runner to pass `--yes`. The contest has concluded and no contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment). Keep the demo aligned with the CLI approval contract; update test fixtures that assumed auto by checking `new InteractiveRepl(`, `SidecarServer(` and `mode:` in `cli/test`. | `eval/run.mjs`, `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs`, `cli/test/**` | 4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:11:- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:147:- `nexus run` in CI and eval contexts (`eval/run.mjs`) must pass `--yes` explicitly. Update the eval adapters in the same PR.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":131232366}},"started_at_ms":1793226172948,"completed_at_ms":1793226174080}}
