{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:23:00.852Z","ordinal":467626,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1849c-08f3-7481-ab15-bacbc162c51b","call_id":"call_dc0c921028c84c319d0efe10efd795b5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 9.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"XERJ:\n{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"took\\\":2272,\\\"timed_out\\\":false,\\\"_shards\\\":{\\\"total\\\":11,\\\"successful\\\":11,\\\"skipped\\\":0,\\\"failed\\\":0},\\\"hits\\\":{\\\"total\\\":{\\\"value\\\":1504,\\\"relation\\\":\\\"eq\\\"},\\\"max_score\\\":4.0,\\\"hits\\\":[{\\\"_index\\\":\\\"nexus-docs-reviews-evidence-5\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"33bf9ef738abb216c4693d2d1a34a38a\\\",\\\"_score\\\":4.0,\\\"_source\\\":{\\\"ax_path\\\":\\\"reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-ceabfcc-20261027/validate-ceabfcc-20261027T165220Z.json\\\",\\\"ax_file\\\":\\\"axf2-6e6fdb033eca5ed05dd984540f028aaa-1102\\\",\\\"ax_locator\\\":\\\"results:e8\\\"},\\\"fields\\\":{\\\"_passage\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"name\\\",\\\"ordinal\\\":0,\\\"start_offset\\\":0,\\\"end_offset\\\":57,\\\"text\\\":\\\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\\\"}]}},{\\\"_index\\\":\\\"nexus-docs-reviews-evidence-5\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"adf5a370f4db912fb565b5b483e82efd\\\",\\\"_score\\\":4.0,\\\"_source\\\":{\\\"ax_path\\\":\\\"reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-setup-failure.json\\\",\\\"ax_file\\\":\\\"axf2-bc165f998e042f17a9f83081fa9a0106-1183\\\",\\\"ax_locator\\\":\\\"results:e8\\\"},\\\"fields\\\":{\\\"_passage\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"name\\\",\\\"ordinal\\\":0,\\\"start_offset\\\":0,\\\"end_offset\\\":57,\\\"text\\\":\\\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\\\"}]}},{\\\"_index\\\":\\\"nexus-docs-reviews-evidence-5\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"f1f0621fa29599fc43e20e0222d3a158\\\",\\\"_score\\\":4.0,\\\"_source\\\":{\\\"ax_path\\\":\\\"reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.json\\\",\\\"ax_file\\\":\\\"axf2-d23e4570890eafd9c2827c53a165b521-1103\\\",\\\"ax_locator\\\":\\\"results:e8\\\"},\\\"fields\\\":{\\\"_passage\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"name\\\",\\\"ordinal\\\":0,\\\"start_offset\\\":0,\\\"end_offset\\\":57,\\\"text\\\":\\\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\\\"}]}},{\\\"_index\\\":\\\"nexus-docs-reviews-evidence-5\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"609ded4bb35d16b9746fc4037b074029\\\",\\\"_score\\\":4.0,\\\"_source\\\":{\\\"ax_path\\\":\\\"reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-a12-20261023T162028Z.json\\\",\\\"ax_file\\\":\\\"axf2-55ef0bff6210b141908cff2b810a5f94-1102\\\",\\\"ax_locator\\\":\\\"results:e8\\\"},\\\"fields\\\":{\\\"_passage\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"name\\\",\\\"ordinal\\\":0,\\\"start_offset\\\":0,\\\"end_offset\\\":57,\\\"text\\\":\\\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\\\"}]}},{\\\"_index\\\":\\\"nexus-docs-reviews-evidence-5\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"d09c1917b5ad98af53a63d4bbbd30f5b\\\",\\\"_score\\\":4.0,\\\"_source\\\":{\\\"ax_path\\\":\\\"reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261021T0443Z-synthetic.json\\\",\\\"ax_file\\\":\\\"axf2-23fa5859e026e44fd6a6b21a175430ee-1101\\\",\\\"ax_locator\\\":\\\"results:e8\\\"},\\\"fields\\\":{\\\"_passage\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"name\\\",\\\"ordinal\\\":0,\\\"start_offset\\\":0,\\\"end_offset\\\":57,\\\"text\\\":\\\"qualification preflight fails closed without the controls\\\"}]}}]}}\"}],\"isError\":false}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"REPO:\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 23199)\nTotal output lines: 147\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:36:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:53:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:55:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:60:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:67:4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:208:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep ve…19199 tokens truncated… `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:483:The authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:489:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:497:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, PR #140's merge commit. Exact-main CI [39747222866](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222866) passed all four jobs on that exact SHA: Node 20, 22, 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging, including the CLI suite and package smoke check. Exact-main CodeQL [39747222840](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222840) passed. PR #140's host report is synthetic-only: 10/10 infrastructure checks passed and independent review accepted it; it does not establish held-out qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:225:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:226:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:227:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:175:| REQ-PRV-106 | Standalone commitment; HIST-08; DEC-16 | Standalone qualification: (a) live runs through the gateway-stripping proxy, in plain and emulated-server profiles; (b) server-kind conformance fixtures. | standalone (product principle) | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | TEST (test:cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts); eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs; **RT 2026-10-17 @a2abdf7:** live dry run through the gateway, llama.cpp profile, 1 development task VERIFIED with hidden and regression tests passing (`evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/`). Gap: `eval/run.mjs` always passes `--context-limit`, so the discovered context is never the source in profile runs (boundary request logged). Product-qualified needs the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 matrix on the RC. | tested | ACC-INF-10, ACCEPTANCE §4.2 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05, PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:36:| eval/run.mjs, score.mjs, infra.mjs, README.md, configs/*.json | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:94:| EVL-003 | S3 | Contamination control | eval/run.mjs:57-59,178; score.mjs:80-84 | SOURCE. Agents run as the operator's user with the task dir (including hidden tests) readable. Detection catches only (a) a changed task dir or (b) the task path appearing in agent stdout or stderr. Peers rarely echo tool output. Contaminated runs are counted but **still included** in the pooled pass rate. | Hidden-test leakage might go undetected and would be scored. | Stage hidden tests outside the readable tree (another uid, or copy in after the run from a root-only dir). Exclude contaminated runs from the pooled rate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:95:| EVL-004 | S3 | Matched-condition identity | eval/run.mjs:31,50,114,118; configs/pilot-*.json | SOURCE. The manifest records the model *alias* (`engineering/lead`) but not the weights digest, server build or sampling parameters. No temperature or seed is set for Nexus or peers (each uses its own defaults). The full operator `process.env` is inherited (:114), so ambient env can differ per agent. Concurrent agents share one gateway, which the pilot notes inflated wall times. | \"Same model, same budget\" is asserted, not recorded. Speed comparisons are confounded. | Record a gateway model fingerprint (GGUF sha, llama.cpp build, sampling) per run. Use a minimal allow-listed env. Run serially, or report queueing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md:16:**Gap found.** Nexus reported `context 65536 (operator)`, because `eval/run.mjs` always passes `--context-limit` (from\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md:19:`eval/run.mjs`. `discovery supported` confirms that the `/props` probe itself answered.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:31:- `eval/run.mjs`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:47:| 8 | Update the eval runner to pass `--yes`. The contest has concluded and no contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment). Keep the demo aligned with the CLI approval contract; update test fixtures that assumed auto by checking `new InteractiveRepl(`, `SidecarServer(` and `mode:` in `cli/test`. | `eval/run.mjs`, `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs`, `cli/test/**` | 4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:11:- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:147:- `nexus run` in CI and eval contexts (`eval/run.mjs`) must pass `--yes` explicitly. Update the eval adapters in the same PR.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1849a-b358-70f3-86ea-b2ec73ad98ca","create_time":1793226180.8518195}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
