{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:29:17.384Z","ordinal":467787,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1849f-b0c5-7071-a08e-b7d54e0e0579","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2773bb3fc81a08ff34683918b489e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The authoritative integration revision remains `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`.\n\nPR #310’s Node 22 and Node 24 checks passed. Its Linux job has passed evaluator containment setup, Rust tests/build, and CLI build; the full CLI suite is still running. I’m holding candidate CI until that suite finishes.\n\nThe held-out issue remains unanswered. I recorded that the qualification runner correctly requires isolated `blackbox-v1` validators and asked the custodian for a conversion or replacement checkpoint. I did not access protected corpus material.\n\nThe candidate at `4c4df05` passes its focused regression, independent source review, enforced requirements check, and version-sync check. It is still source work at `rc.10` metadata—not a release candidate artifact.\n\n**Campaign: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no RC is accepted and no stable release is claimed.**"}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793226555728,"completed_at_ms":1793226557384}}
