{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:32:50.853Z","ordinal":467910,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1847a-3716-77f0-9e7d-01ae06afc407","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-825dab3f-3f98-4835-815d-68c5dc3871c2","process_id":"92808","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"capped_fixture|SUITE|QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9|4c4df05\" /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9 /tmp --glob '!*.jsonl' --glob '!*.log' --glob '!node_modules/**' --glob '!target/**' --max-count 4"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'capped_fixture|SUITE|QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9|4c4df05' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9 /tmp --glob '!*.jsonl' --glob '!*.log' --glob '!node_modules/**' --glob '!target/**' --max-count 4","query":"capped_fixture|SUITE|QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9|4c4df05","path":"nexus-claims"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/tasks/lessons.md:33:  request after a load-induced timeout). Rule: one test run at a time per machine; take the `SUITE` claim\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/tasks/lessons.md:38:- 2026-10-16: I ran targeted tests and live calls while another agent's `SUITE` claim was held, because I checked\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/CONTRIBUTING.md:24:The complete suite needs Linux isolation facilities and security tools configured by the CI workflow. Do not disable isolation to obtain a pass. Report environmental blockers and exact commands/results. Tests and probes must use disposable user state; never point them at your normal `~/.nexus`. On a shared development host, acquire the documented `SUITE` claim before running any tests and use a committed snapshot for full suites.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_safe_fs.ts/owner.json:9:  \"status\": \"Refreshed PR207 candidate; no content change from independently accepted 3a5fc8e diff. Exact diff-check PASS; independent re-review pending. Tests/push wait for active SUITE and post-merge full CI.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`; its latest follow-up scopes checkout to the nested workspace and extends the regression to preserve both staged and unstaged sibling state. The prior nested-index delta at `662d084` was independently ACCEPTed (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`), and the checkout-scope delta was independently ACCEPTed by `review_pr302` (SHA-256 `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`, tests not run). PR #302 CodeQL and JS/TS checks pass; Node 22/24 CI and Entire are running. TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed on the prior delta; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:47:**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:597:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_repl.ts/owner.json:10:  \"scope\": \"Resolve REPL pending prompt on stdin EOF using existing exit signal; add EOF regression in operator_config_startup.test.ts. No tests while SUITE claim is held; no merge without exact CI and independent review.\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_DEFECT_UPGRADE_REGULAR_LAUNCHER_RECOVERY_20261027/owner.json:10:  \"status\": \"Ready for owner PR and exact-head CI; not integrated. SUITE and hot-file claims released\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:102:  \"terminal_matrix\": \"0/15; user cannot run the xterm 80x24 cell now. No manual checks started. Idle SUITE/GATEWAY claims released and logged; worksheet/procedure remains ready.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_OPERATION_RUNNER_REBASE_20261028/owner.json:8:  \"status\": \"review_correction_committed_and_pushed; npm_build_and_diff_check_pass; focused_test_waits_for_SUITE_claim; fresh_exact_CI_and_review_pending\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/POST_CONTEST_DEP_UPDATE_PR126/owner.json:11:  \"safe_boundary\": \"clean local merge commit; diff-check and JSON parse passed; worktree pre