ence/v1/DEFECT-WORKTREE-RECORD-MIGRATION-20261027/README.md:38:- `tsc --noEmit`, `git diff --check`: clean; isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` under the SUITE claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md:15:Focused validation: `node --import tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 test/{session_state_v2,task_state_v2,task_message_log,state,state_migration,file_guard,retention,retention_state_v2,persistence_protection,egress_persistence_equivalence,upgrade_transaction_recovery}.test.ts`: **143/143 pass**, zero failures/skips. `tsc --noEmit`: exit0. All HOME/XDG/TMPDIR roots isolated under /var/tmp; local SUITE claimed. No inference or held-out data accessed.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DISCOVERED-VERIFIER-BASELINE-20261026/README.md:33:The first isolated attempt was incomplete because the Rust core had not yet been built. The final passing run above includes the built core and was executed under the shared `SUITE` claim. Earlier fixture iterations were corrected: the fixture now declares `./math.js` as its package entry, clears inherited `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` for its nested Node test command, and explicitly declares `math.js` as the deliverable.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DISCOVERED-VERIFIER-BASELINE-20261026/node22-focused-run.md:8:- Shared `SUITE` claim was held for the run and released after exit 0.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPDATE-PLAN-WORKSPACE-EFFECT-20261026/README.md:29:- `tsc --noEmit`, `git diff --check`: clean; isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` under the SUITE claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md:17:All runs use isolated HOME/XDG and SSD-backed `/var/tmp`; no external inference or held-out payloads. Focused tests ran under the local SUITE claim. Exact-head equipped-host CI and independent review are required before integration. No RC, human acceptance, or release readiness is established here.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_COMPONENT_COHERENCE/README.md:5:Focused validation: 15/15 tests passed on mike-dev with atomic SUITE ownership and throwaway HOME/XDG state. Tests cover coherent stable/prerelease/build versions and each component mismatching by version, prerelease, or build; they exercise updater eligibility, archive binding and the standalone publisher validator. Existing read-only tsx executable from p10g-validation supplied the runner; no dependency files were changed. Full integration checks and independent review remain required. This does not close transaction recovery, legacy fallback, installed-RC qualification, or release acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/README.md:11:Validation: retention.test.ts plus retention_state_v2.test.ts:20/20 passed, no failures/skips. tsc --noEmit:exit0. Negative controls:3 expected failures,8 filtered tests, not acceptance passes. HOME/XDG/TMPDIR were isolated under /var/tmp with the local SUITE claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:38:Separation: the implementation agents (codex app-server sessions and `kiro-cli` on the Nexus repository) authored nothing. The custodian authored nothing and edited task files never; it edited store bookkeeping (`ASSIGNMENT-*.md`, `AUTHOR-TRANSFER-2026-10-18.md`, `AGENTS.md`) and ran the validator. Authors never ran `bin/validate.py` and never held the `SUITE` claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:42:Every task was validated by the custodian in a bounded, atomically claimed `SUITE` window (claim log lines `CLAIM SUITE opencode v7/v8/v9/v10/v11`, each released with `RELEASE SUITE`). Rounds: batches 1–7 one round each (windows v7, v8); batches 8–9 and the repaired task two rounds each (v9–v11). Per-task logs: `reference/<id>.validation.log` in the store. Claim-log evidence: one `VALIDATED <id> rounds=N (<window>)` line per task; latest line governs.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:89:`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log`, 2026-10-18: `TRANSFER HELDOUT authorship` 02:25:21Z; `BROKEN CLAIM HELDOUT_AUTHORING_B8` 02:33:14Z; `ABORT … author-b8r` 02:35Z; `REJECT HELDOUT batch 9` 02:37Z; `CLAIM/RELEASE SUITE opencode v9` 02:4xZ–02:54:09Z, `v10` 02:5xZ–03:01:22Z, `v11` 03:0xZ–03:05Z; `CUSTODY NOTE v9`, `CUSTODY HOLD` 02:54:09Z; `VALIDATED` lines per task; `BOUNDARY REQUEST (QUALIFICATION BLOCKER)` 03:05:08Z.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:87:- **v2 batch 1 authored + custodian-verified.** `ho2-py-bugfix-01` (more-itertools @ `1ea82a7`) and `ho2-go-refactor-01` (google/uuid @ `6e10cd1`): schema OK for both; **all four manifest hashes re-derived exactly** by the custodian; reference patches + validation logs present. Live `bin/validate.py` runs are **deferred** (SUITE held) — recorded in each validation log; custodian to run 2 rounds per task when SUITE frees.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:90:- **Corpus progress (store v2):** batches 1–3 authored → **11 tasks**; custodian re-derived **all 11 manifest hash pairs exactly** (5/5 batch 3 re-verified separately after the author's self-check) and `check_schema.mjs` reports OK × 11. Live `bin/validate.py` runs for all 11 remain **deferred pending a SUITE window** (pending notes + author-side dry-run sequences recorded per task). Remaining: ~29 tasks to the 40 target, custodian validation, then sealing.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CODEQL-BAD-CODE-SANITIZATION-20261026/README.md:53:- Focused execution under the `SUITE` claim (isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`):\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:7:| Claim protocol | `SUITE` taken atomically (`mkdir`), **ownership recheck before every phase** (owner.json agent+pid must match the watcher's own), released **only if still owned** at exit (claim log 18:56:33Z CLAIM → 19:24:21Z RELEASE; codex re-took at 19:24:39Z — no overlap) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:43:Watcher v3 aborted fail-closed immediately after taking the claim (20:38:51Z) and left its own dead-pid claim in place: its `owns_claim` pid pattern was corrupted by a quoted heredoc (`\\$` escaped the dollar → the pattern never matched). The stale claim was logged and released by the owner-of-record at 20:51:47Z; v4/v5 use a `printf`-built fixed-string pattern. codex's 20:44:48Z \"REQUEST SUITE release … codex will wait\" was honoured. No suites overlapped at any point.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/verification.md:29:- `HOME=<tmp> node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` → **exit 0**; `requirements: 121 rows; tested 106, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7`. **This establishes ledger integrity only.** REQ-AGT-118 remains `partial`: the changed test has not been executed (SUITE held), and the DEC-17 amendment review is approve-with-issues (below). A ledger pass is **not** behavioural acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/verification.md:38:- **Test execution deferred:** the `SUITE` claim is held by `codex` (pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z), so no suite or targeted test was run on this machine. RE-RUN when `SUITE` is free:\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/publication-gating.md:15:- REQ-AGT-118: changed tests executed (SUITE window) + independent acceptance of DEC-17 (review is approve-with-issues; acceptance pending).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:13:| focused `tokens.test.ts` | **3/3 PASS** (watcher v6, 23:16:36Z, SUITE window) | **3/3 PASS** by independent coordinator `codex-lead` (record below) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:29:- **31 authored** (batches 1–7), **30 custodian-validated** via `bin/validate.py` in bounded SUITE windows (v7: 25/26 in 12 min; v8: 5/5), all 31 manifest hash pairs re-derived exactly; schema OK × 31.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:32:- Validation incident (diagnostic): the first validation window (v6) self-deadlocked — `validate.py` waits on the SUITE claim that the custodian's own window holds — so its 420 s \"timeouts\" were deadlock waits, not task failures. Fixed with a documented kill-switch `HELDOUT_CLAIMWAIT=0` in the store's `claimwait.py`; evidence of the invalid window preserved.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:37:SUITE windows rotated codex ↔ opencode (v4, v5, v6, v7, v8) with zero overlaps; every opencode window took the claim atomically, rechecked ownership before executing, and released only its own claim. One protocol incident (v3 quoting bug, fail-closed) is documented in `test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RECOVER-WORKTREE-CONVERSATION-20261026/README.md:63:- `tsc --noEmit`, `git diff --check`: clean; isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n... command output truncated for persistenc