0.12.1/src/mips32r6/netlink.rs:747:pub const NL80211_MAX_NR_AKM_SUITES: u32 = 2;\n/tmp/nexus-home.Fzx5ei/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/linux-raw-sys-0.12.1/src/mips32r6/netlink.rs:1143:pub const IFLA_MACSEC_CIPHER_SUITE: _bindgen_ty_15 = _bindgen_ty_15::IFLA_MACSEC_CIPHER_SUITE;\n/tmp/nexus-home.Fzx5ei/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/linux-raw-sys-0.12.1/src/mips32r6/netlink.rs:2028:NL80211_ATTR_CIPHER_SUITES = 57,\n/tmp/nexus-home.Fzx5ei/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/linux-raw-sys-0.12.1/src/mips32r6/if_arp.rs:1285:pub const IFLA_MACSEC_CIPHER_SUITE: _bindgen_ty_17 = _bindgen_ty_17::IFLA_MACSEC_CIPHER_SUITE;\n/tmp/nexus-home.Fzx5ei/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/linux-raw-sys-0.12.1/src/mips32r6/if_arp.rs:2072:IFLA_MACSEC_CIPHER_SUITE = 4,\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:187:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker/credential-broker-test.mjs:26:\tconsole.log(\"=== RUNNING FAIL-CLOSED CREDENTIAL BROKER SECURITY TEST SUITE ===\\n\");\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/CONTRIBUTING.md:24:The complete suite needs Linux isolation facilities and security tools configured by the CI workflow. Do not disable isolation to obtain a pass. Report environmental blockers and exact commands/results. Tests and probes must use disposable user state; never point them at your normal `~/.nexus`. On a shared development host, acquire the documented `SUITE` claim before running any tests and use a committed snapshot for full suites.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md:17:All runs use isolated HOME/XDG and SSD-backed `/var/tmp`; no external inference or held-out payloads. Focused tests ran under the local SUITE claim. Exact-head equipped-host CI and independent review are required before integration. No RC, human acceptance, or release readiness is established here.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:38:Separation: the implementation agents (codex app-server sessions and `kiro-cli` on the Nexus repository) authored nothing. The custodian authored nothing and edited task files never; it edited store bookkeeping (`ASSIGNMENT-*.md`, `AUTHOR-TRANSFER-2026-10-18.md`, `AGENTS.md`) and ran the validator. Authors never ran `bin/validate.py` and never held the `SUITE` claim.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:42:Every task was validated by the custodian in a bounded, atomically claimed `SUITE` window (claim log lines `CLAIM SUITE opencode v7/v8/v9/v10/v11`, each released with `RELEASE SUITE`). Rounds: batches 1–7 one round each (windows v7, v8); batches 8–9 and the repaired task two rounds each (v9–v11). Per-task logs: `reference/<id>.validation.log` in the store. Claim-log evidence: one `VALIDATED <id> rounds=N (<window>)` line per task; latest line governs.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:89:`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log`, 2026-10-18: `TRANSFER HELDOUT authorship` 02:25:21Z; `BROKEN CLAIM HELDOUT_AUTHORING_B8` 02:33:14Z; `ABORT … author-b8r` 02:35Z; `REJECT HELDOUT batch 9` 02:37Z; `CLAIM/RELEASE SUITE opencode v9` 02:4xZ–02:54:09Z, `v10` 02:5xZ–03:01:22Z, `v11` 03:0xZ–03:05Z; `CUSTODY NOTE v9`, `CUSTODY HOLD` 02:54:09Z; `VALIDATED` lines per task; `BOUNDARY REQUEST (QUALIFICATION BLOCKER)` 03:05:08Z.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/REPOSITORY-QUALITY-REVIEW/independent-review.md:19:Isolated HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME; atomic SUITE claim acquired for these short offline checks and released afterward. No production state, credentials, inference, or GitHub setting mutations were used.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_COMPONENT_COHERENCE/README.md:5:Focused validation: 15/15 tests passed on mike-dev with atomic SUITE ownership and throwaway HOME/XDG state. Tests cover coherent stable/prerelease/build versions and each component mismatching by version, prerelease, or build; they exercise updater eligibility, archive binding and the standalone publisher validator. Existing read-only tsx executable from p10g-validation supplied the runner; no dependency files were changed. Full integration checks and independent review remain required. This does not close transaction recovery, legacy fallback, installed-RC qualification, or release acceptance.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_BASELINE/README.md:7:This is source performance evidence, not installed-RC qualification, durability/crash acceptance or a broad product-readiness pass. Raw logs, source/benchmark hashes, Node/kernel identity and exact command are retained. No inference or held-out data were used, and no load was applied to mike-dev. The local SUITE claim was held and released. Final implementation and exact-source measurement, migration/continuity regression coverage and independent acceptance remain outstanding.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:87:- **v2 batch 1 authored + custodian-verified.** `ho2-py-bugfix-01` (more-itertools @ `1ea82a7`) and `ho2-go-refactor-01` (google/uuid @ `6e10cd1`): schema OK for both; **all four manifest hashes re-derived exactly** by the custodian; reference patches + validation logs present. Live `bin/validate.py` runs are **deferred** (SUITE held) — recorded in each validation log; custodian to run 2 rounds per task when SUITE frees.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:90:- **Corpus progress (store v2):** batches 1–3 authored → **11 tasks**; custodian re-derived **all 11 manifest hash pairs exactly** (5/5 batch 3 re-verified separately after the author's self-check) and `check_schema.mjs` reports OK × 11. Live `bin/validate.py` runs for all 11 remain **deferred pending a SUITE window** (pending notes + author-side dry-run sequences recorded per task). Remaining: ~29 tasks to the 40 target, custodian validation, then sealing.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:7:| Claim protocol | `SUITE` taken atomically (`mkdir`), **ownership recheck before every phase** (owner.json agent+pid must match the watcher's own), released **only if still owned** at exit (claim log 18:56:33Z CLAIM → 19:24:21Z RELEASE; codex re-took at 19:24:39Z — no overlap) |\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:43:Watcher v3 aborted fail-closed immediately after taking the claim (20:38:51Z) and left its own dead-pid claim in place: its `owns_claim` pid pattern was corrupted by a quoted heredoc (`\\$` escaped the dollar → the pattern never matched). The stale claim was logged and released by the owner-of-record at 20:51:47Z; v4/v5 use a `printf`-built fixed-string pattern. codex's 20:44:48Z \"REQUEST SUITE release … codex will wait\" was honoured. No suites overlapped at any point.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/publication-gating.md:15:- REQ-AGT-118: changed tests executed (SUITE window) + independent acceptance of DEC-17 (review is approve-with-issues; acceptance pending).\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:13:| focused `tokens.test.ts` | **3/3 PASS** (watcher v6, 23:16:36Z, SUITE window) | **3/3 PASS** by independent coordinator `codex-lead` (record below) |\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:29:- **31 authored** (batches 1–7), **30 custodian-validated** via `bin/validate.py` in bounded SUITE windows (v7: 25/26 in 12 min; v8: 5/5), all 31 manifest hash pairs re-derived exactly; schema OK × 31.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:32:- Validation incident (diagnostic): the first validation window (v6) self-deadlocked — `validate.py` waits on the SUITE claim that the custodian's own window holds — so its 420 s \"timeouts\" were deadlock waits, not task failures. Fixed with a documented kill-switch `HELDOUT_CLAIMWAIT=0` in the store's `claimwait.py`; evidence of the invalid window preserved.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:37:SUITE windows rotated codex ↔ opencode (v4, v5, v6, v7, v8) with zero overlaps; every opencode window took the claim atomically, rechecked ownership before executing, and released only its own claim. One protocol incident (v3 quoting bug, fail-closed) is documented in `test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md`.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:67:REQUIREMENTS.md:153 keeps REQ-AGT-118 `partial` with \"Changed-test execution and independent review are **pending**\". Reality matches: docs + test/fixture changed; the SUITE claim is held by codex (verified: `nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json`, pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z); verification.md:29,32 explicitly defers execution, states a ledger pass \"is not behavioural acceptance\", and lists the re-run steps. This reviewer likewise did not run the suite. REQ-QUAL-105 staying `tested` is defensible: the injector/smoke tests (EVL-001) are unchanged and the 8→9 correction is docs-only. ✓\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:96:- Ledger status promoted to `tested` before the changed test executes on a free SUITE (not present — `partial` is correct).\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:45:- Batch 1 authored (`ho2-py-bugfix-01`, `ho2-go-refactor-01`); custodian re-derived all four manifest hashes exactly; live validation deferred to a SUITE window. See `custody-report-2026-10-17.md` §5.\n/tmp/nexus-rc5-prepare/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/verification.md:29:- `HOME=<tmp> node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` → **exit 0**; `requirements: 121 rows; tested 106, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7`. **This establishes ledger integrity only.** REQ-AGT-118 remains `partial`: the changed test has not