{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:56:44.920Z","ordinal":468590,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8088eee0-7df9-4aa9-9f80-c19e89db40a6","process_id":"94690","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Nexus|v1\\.0\\.0|acceptance|review\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -35"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"Nexus|v1\\\\.0\\\\.0|acceptance|review\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"Nexus|v1\\.0\\.0|acceptance|review","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: Nexus Code client release and Cloudflare contest publication\n2:scope: Package the installed Nexus Code Linux client and prepare the distinct Nexus Workers/Artifacts contest submission in `/home/mike/nexus-code`; retain separate readiness dispositions and do not treat CI or offline fixtures as a clean-account proof.\n15:## Task 2: Package Nexus Code as a complete Linux client with installer and CI, partial\n27:- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n28:- the user required evidence-supported claims and separate ready/blocked dispositions -> local fixtures, structural checks, synthetic broker tests, and public video must not be presented as Cloudflare-backed acceptance; do not automate application entry. [Task 1]\n34:- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n45:# Task Group: Nexus agent effectiveness: unbounded continuation and evidence-bounded diagnosis\n46:scope: Review failed Nexus agent exports and maintain prompt/regression safeguards for progressing continuation loops, direct diagnostic questions, and timeout claims in `/home/mike/nexus-code`.\n57:- Nexus, nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, 54582+8192+4096>65536, make test, timeout, truncated output, direct status question, evidence-bounded diagnosis\n108:- Flash-Next Q-TOOLS passed 7/7 synthetic categories and 20/20 Nexus replay points. Q-LONGCTX passed probes from 16K through 59,913 tokens; a 67,335-token input was rejected with HTTP 400 in 0.14s. Both selected models passed production qualification after reboot and rollback restoration. [Task 1]\n146:# Task Group: Nexus dogfood-blockers independent candidate review and compaction evidence integrity\n147:scope: Review-only, isolated validation of `fix/dogfood-blockers` candidates against Nexus baseline; use before selecting an I1/objective-supervisor base or relying on context admission, unseen-result, or modified-file evidence.\n150:## Task 1: Independently review dogfood-blockers candidate `6b34f5f`, rejected as an I1 base\n154:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/06/rollout-2026-10-06T06-05-16-01a10fd0-fc8c-7bd1-ab0e-9fcdba8f7116.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-06T06:25:20+00:00, thread_id=01a10fd0-fc8c-7bd1-ab0e-9fcdba8f7116, `BASE_6B34F5F: NOT_ACCEPTABLE_FOR_I1_SPIKE`)\n158:- Nexus, fix/dogfood-blockers, 6b34f5f, 2860228, 6f71043, 6845415, unseen tool results, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, compaction, modified files, repeated tool-call IDs, editedPaths, editChangedFile, EALLOWSCRIPTS\n160:## Task 2: Independently review dogfood-blockers candidate `1b71e27`, suitable with explicit limitations\n164:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/05/rollout-2026-10-05T09-30-36-01a10b66-9c46-7200-a985-407131043586.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T20:40:25+00:00, thread_id=01a10b66-9c46-7200-a985-407131043586, review target=/home/mike/nexus-blockers; `SUITABLE_WITH_EXPLICIT_LIMITATIONS`)\n168:- Nexus, fix/dogfood-blockers, 1b71e27, 2860228, MAX_READ_LINES, StreamRedactor, tester.ts, verifier baseline, BASELINE_FAILURES_ONLY, EALLOWSCRIPTS, native Git metadata\n172:- for review-only candidate work, the user required: “Do not modify Nexus source”, “use a scratch copy”, “If something is wrong, REPORT IT”, and preserve the operator’s dirty tree -> isolate builds/tests, preserve negative results, and report rather than remediate. [Task 1]\n183:- Related skill: skills/reviewing-nexus-candidates/SKILL.md. [Task 1][Task 2]\n192:# Task Group: Nexus architecture reconnaissance and context-engineering baseline\n193:scope: Strictly read-only mapping of Nexus information/context flow, durable state, admission, and validation; use when the requested deliverable is an architecture investigation rather than remediation or design work.\n196:## Task 1: Capture baseline for the intended A-I Nexus architecture reconnaissance, incomplete\n200:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/05/rollout-2026-10-05T09-30-36-01a10b66-9c46-7200-a985-407131043586.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T20:40:25+00:00, thread_id=01a10b66-9c46-7200-a985-407131043586, original A-I report not delivered)\n204:- Nexus, read-only, architecture reconnaissance, context-engineering, CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md, 2860228, linear transcript resend, context admission, deterministic compaction, durable session state, no context router\n208:- for Nexus reconnaissance, the user required “read-only” and “do not modify source, tests, configuration, documentation, dependencies, Git state” -> preserve scope, record exact snapshot SHA plus concurrent-change risk, and do not implement optimization or prove a preferred theory. [Task 1]\n218:- The requested A-I report was not delivered because the rollout pivoted to `/home/mike/nexus-blockers` remediation review. Do not change repository/task scope without explicit authorization; stop or ask before a new investigation replaces the requested deliverable. [Task 1]\n220:# Task Group: Nexus live Ratatui TUI review and redaction/observer isolation\n221:scope: Read-only review of the landed live Ratatui TUI on `/home/mike/nexus-code` `main`; use when reviewing the live sidecar/TUI protocol, evidence and receipt panels, streaming redaction, or observer isolation, not as qualification that the implementation's tests passed.\n222:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (rollout metadata recorded cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost); reuse_rule=inspect the current HEAD and preserve any dirty working tree before reviewing; re-run TypeScript, Rust, and PTY coverage before treating this code-review result as release qualification.\n228:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-03T23-20-44-plr4-review_landed_ratatui_tui_main_2860228.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; target=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T23-20-44-01a10411-e678-7183-9233-5c0bc13de1ca.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T05:44:28+00:00, thread_id=01a10411-e678-7183-9233-5c0bc13de1ca, read-only review; no tests run)\n236:- when the user asks to “review the changes” already landed on `main`, inspect the current HEAD rather than rely on stale findings, preserve dirty working-tree changes, and report actionable findings with file/line references. [Task 1]\n240:- At reviewed HEAD `2860228`, Nexus had moved from a snapshot viewer to a live Ratatui client: multiline composer, approval overlays, slash commands, cancellation, tool-detail/evidence panels, receipt panels, and default TUI launch in a terminal. `--repl` remains the readline fallback. [Task 1]\n249:- Stop rule: this was code review only; no TypeScript, Rust, or PTY suites ran. Treat qualification as pending until those relevant suites pass. [Task 1]\n251:# Task Group: Nexus CRED-003 FlightRecorder and audit-log credential sanitization\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41857}},"started_at_ms":1793228204920,"completed_at_ms":1793228204920}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:56:46.057Z","ordinal":468591,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a184ba-efe8-7d23-a3ad-ba648956e063","call_id":"call_2793ab36cc4440569a229ad6c1df60bb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- v1.0.0 release: entire_local=Entire enabled on main; five sessions shown active/idle. Search failed at auth token refresh because org.freedesktop.secrets is unavailable; checkpoint listing confirms local unpushed checkpoints and checkpoint pushing disabled. No restart attempted., integration_head=origin/main remains 10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496 as observed at 2026-10-28 ~21:44 UTC; no new main merge during this poll., entire_search=Owner-recorded authenticated read-only query on ubuntu-desktop at 21:48 found trail23 open while Nexus Code change marked merged; finding/approvals commands returned no open change, historical finding disposition unavailable. READINESS correctly says unresolved/unverified; no evidence of resolution. No independent query repeated by this session., current_main_ci=At 2026-10-28 22:43 UTC, post-PR310 main CI 40781709732 is still in progress on exact cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e; Node22 cargo release build, Node24 CLI tests had started; CodeQL 40781709679 passed., pr308=Merged as 10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496. PR-head required checks (Node22, Node24, Linux, JS/TS, CodeQL) succeeded; Entire Gates neutral., pr310=At 2026-10-28 22:12Z, remote PR #310 head remains 1f54f2f7835e05b8470cb68156ec96362e99d8c7 on base 10c84df. JS/TS and CodeQL passed; Entire Gates in progress but neutral/not required on ruleset; Node22 and Node24 are running full CLI tests from 22:05:52Z and 22:06:02Z, no failures. Linux waits on test-matrix. Auto-merge remains enabled. The active owner worktree has one unpushed commit ba9d0cd correcting main CI completion time; exact cumulative independent review ACCEPT, SHA256 6c25ef45401a48dc56551c90741811b9a05c371698420dc9143924383040fadf. Owner claim is active; do not touch or push., current_main_gate=Verified in clean detached worktree /tmp/nexus-main-enforce-10c84df at exact source 10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496 with isolated HOME: check_requirements.mjs --enforce exit 0; sync-version.mjs --check exit 0. Ledger: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals., status=Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no accepted successor RC or public stable v1.0.0., ci_observation=Verified live handle 40770466028: main Linux test step finished successfully (job is now on package-linux.sh); Node22/24 succeeded. PR310 run 40775615742 on exact remote head 5afbae0e remains Node22/24 in progress; JS/TS, CodeQL passed; Entire pending., suite_claim=Still held by kimi-main. Latest observed scope updated package and installer smoke with isolated HOME and mock inference only. Do not run tests., review_policy=User confirms repository has one human user; do not require another human account. Distinct non-implementing agent review is available and has accepted the documentation changes. Keep formal release acceptance IN_PROGRESS until all mandatory external qualification and exact-RC gates are complete., pr310_review_hash=Resolved: plan05_readonly_review confirms ACCEPT covers cumulative PR content at b9a23d51, including b035e716 and b9a23d51. Initial 3f5e1f hash was a working-tree diff including later edits before b9 commit, not the pushed range. Correct base-to-head patch hash for exact pushed PR b9a23d51 is 54bfd6c4bc845df99088ad85f1eef1a8b7181a9e8c29914085972b0fec3839ec; reviewer confirms same content was reviewed., pr310_ci=Completed. PR #310 merged 2026-10-28T22:39:59Z as cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e. Exact PR head 1f54f2f passed Node22/24, Linux package/repro/SBOM/smoke, JS/TS, CodeQL; Entire Gates concluded NEUTRAL., readiness_worktree=Local readiness branch has additional unpushed commit bf3965543431061d4c119940edab29ab4ee9d473, updating readiness text with completed Node22/24 and remaining Linux test. It is one commit ahead of remote PR head b9a23d51. Preserve; do not force push; exact head requires owner-authorized push and fresh PR checks., pr310_checks=No missing Linux job defect: exact base workflow `.github/workflows/ci.yml` declares `linux-x86_64` with `needs: [test-matrix]`. PR #310’s Node22/24 jobs must finish before Linux is created. Current remote head b9a23d has Node22/24 still running; Linux absence is expected sequencing, not a skip. Ruleset 25340146 requires Node22, Node24 and Linux. Local owner head bf39655 is unpushed; independent reviewer says hosted checks at b9a23 do not cover it., entire_trail23=Independent read-only verification from authenticated `ubuntu-desktop` session over SSH at 2026-10-28 21:55 UTC: `entire trail show 23 --json` reports trail status open, Nexus Code change status merged, hasCodeChanges=false, isPossiblyPartial=true. `entire trail approvals 23` and `entire trail finding list --trail 23 --status any --include-dismissed --json` both report no open changes in selected repository, so the historic high-severity finding and approval details remain unavailable. No finding resolution is inferred. This supports the cautious wording in PR310; no credentials or protected corpus content read., rc_process=Verified from `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/sync-version.mjs` at exact current source 10c84df: root package.json is version source; sync-version updates CLI and Rust package/lock files. Tag workflow requires tag on main, tag/version match, and docs/releases/<tag>.md; it runs tests/security, deterministic double Linux package plus checksum/notices/SBOM/installer comparisons and smoke, attests archive/checksum, then publishes RC tags as prereleases. Stable tag must be a version-only child of matching RC; workflow creates stable GitHub release as draft, which is made public with `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after signed acceptance. Current version is 1.0.0-rc.10. Do not tag successor RC until PR310 integration and pre-RC gates are exact., remaining_blockers=Held-out Issue #1 remains open and unassigned with no response since 2026-10-28 20:25:33Z; custody qualification cannot start. Human terminal matrix remains 0/15, awaiting successor RC and actual interactive execution. Entire historical high-severity finding remains unresolved/unverified; authenticated remote query confirms trail23 open, change merged, no open change for approval/finding views., source_candidate=Candidate branch v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9 exact head 4c4df05a32889dae251750780880b6d4d61401eb. Focused batch_read mid-stream error test PASS 1/1; independent source review ACCEPT; requirements --enforce PASS (123 rows, 108 tested, 12 explicitly deferred exact-RC), sync-version check PASS and confirms package metadata is still rc.10. No PR or candidate artifact yet., heldout_evaluator=Issue #1 remains open and unassigned. Posted metadata-only follow-up comment 6482202709: evaluator intentionally requires isolated blackbox-v1 for qualification; legacy in-process validators cannot be enabled. Requested custodian conversion/replacement path and status. No private corpus accessed., next_action=Monitor exact PR311 checks. If all required checks pass and independent source review remains current, merge through the already granted authorization; then reconcile candidate branch claims, run exact-main post-merge CI/requirements, and begin successor-RC construction only after pre-RC prerequisites., source_pr311=PR #311 v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9 remains open against cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e at 4c4df05a32889dae251750780880b6d4d61401eb; required Node22/24 checks still running, JS/TS and CodeQL pass, Entire Gates in progress. No merge yet., terminal_screenshot_waiver=User explicitly wai