{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:15:25.127Z","ordinal":469098,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a184cc-0347-7011-8cc3-edb9ada9197b","call_id":"call_491274334c71485095d5095fea8e551b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 30.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f51885\",\"wall_time_seconds\":30.001128077,\"session_id\":20343,\"original_token_count\":690,\"output\":\"  ✔ recorded findings survive a restart and later compactions of the restored record (3586.24382ms)\\n  ✔ findings beyond the memory bound are condensed, oldest first, never lost: each keeps its sources, says it is condensed, and is returned in full by read_findings (16623.283617ms)\\n  ✔ in a small context window recorded findings are bounded to fit, so they never block the investigation (9505.868842ms)\\n[context_findings] step=6 observations=1 recorded=yes chars=18\\n[context_findings] step=6 observations=1 recorded=yes chars=18\\n[context_findings] step=6 observations=1 recorded=yes chars=18\\n[context_findings] step=6 observations=1 recorded=yes chars=18\\n  ✔ findings not shown in full to bound the memory are claimed only as recoverable: removal notes and a re-run say read_findings returns them in full (17005.976848ms)\\n  ✔ CTX-07: 30 findings on 5 subjects bounded to the 24K budget keep at least one full claim sentence per subject in view (118.988269ms)\\n  ✔ across compactions findings keep their order and stay distinct: only a condensed or shortened copy gives way to its full finding (101.605ms)\\n  ✔ while findings exceed their bound, the first output of each step says so with the step position; recording ignores it (436.864407ms)\\n  ✔ in the last fifth of the step budget the first output of each step says how many remain and asks to finish, leaving room for validation; recording ignores it (112.440727ms)\\n  ✔ a new request does not inherit the memory notice: it returns only once that request's own compaction finds findings over their bound (1315.595614ms)\\n  ✔ step notices speak only for the turn that issued them: a follow-up or retried turn does not see an earlier turn's (1680.25837ms)\\n  ✔ the whole memory is bounded: past its budget the oldest commands, then removal notes, give way, so the record stays flat (145.243092ms)\\n[context_findings] step=2 observations=12 recorded=yes chars=30\\n  ✔ a follow-up turn on a record whose removal notes were omitted cannot rest on the output they covered (573.984786ms)\\n  ✔ an observation's identity is bounded: a large write is named by its start and a hash, still distinct, and the record does not carry its content (113.967665ms)\\n  ✔ a finding holds exactly the observations it came from: past the header's cap, and not another tool's whose key contains it (412.86733ms)\\n  ✔ only labelled findings are lifted out of an untrusted record; anything else stays opaque (94.771672ms)\\n  ✔ re-running a call whose findings were recorded is answered in full, marked with when, whether it changed, and the step (8761.359889ms)\\n  ✔ findings from an output that has since changed, or was seen only in part, are recorded again; the comparison ignores the note (7982.715007ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","create_time":1793229325.1271977}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
