{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:17:37.950Z","ordinal":469123,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a184ce-0a1e-7031-96d2-5e1af8448dae","call_id":"call_92fcc9ed454a46e1a66c6536d0174ef3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 30.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c7a907\",\"wall_time_seconds\":30.001593692,\"session_id\":20343,\"original_token_count\":1657,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1657)\\nTotal output lines: 79\\n\\n  ✔ a durable operation over the workload blocks with the reason instead of completing (3813.555091ms)\\n✔ G: compaction never lets a recalled result satisfy completion (18214.31784ms)\\n▶ I6: only the operator environment and config.env decide where a stored credential goes\\n  ✔ the stored credential reaches its own gateway, and a foreign endpoint gets none (3407.878072ms)\\n  ✔ a working-directory .env cannot widen the credential origins (the reproduced I6 defect), even across a 401 (2387.740811ms)\\n  ✔ a working-directory .env cannot re-home the gateway either (817.737482ms)\\n  ✔ a config.env key is not re-bound to an endpoint a project .env selects (1665.004417ms)\\n  ✔ nested and workspace .env files have no authority (they are not loaded from elsewhere) (2042.966867ms)\\n  ✔ precedence: the operator's own environment keeps its authority; a project's own key goes only to the project's endpoint (1625.704613ms)\\n  ✔ an explicit credential works for its own provider; the gateway keeps its own (1694.17226ms)\\n  ✔ scheduler probes and catalog refresh: a spec's apiKeyEnv cannot send a stored credential to another origin (23.825443ms)\\n  ✔ a project .env that sets HOME cannot send the operator's key to a spec resource's apiKeyEnv origin (V3n) (2934.9408ms)\\n  ✔ a re-homed token file that links to the operator's token reaches no foreign endpoint (i6i), even one the project selects (2905.500981ms)\\n  ✔ positive control: under the same re-homing .env, the operator's gateway still receives the stored token (880.276378ms)\\n  ✔ no credential material in CLI output, logs or durable state from these runs (0.890339ms)\\n✔ I6: only the operator environment and config.env decide where a stored credential goes (20389.142937ms)\\n✔ generated acyclic operations schedule only after dependencies complete and converge (42.589178ms)\\n✔ scheduler event callback failures produce bounded debug diagnostics (1.99569ms)\\n▶ resource eligibility\\n  ✔ 1. a 429 marks the resource t…657 tokens truncated…ccount-scope limits cover exactly that provider or credential (0.653646ms)\\n  ✔ 29. a model-scope limit covers that model on every endpoint of the provider, and nothing else (0.335432ms)\\n  ✔ 30. no busy loop: repeated failures back off and are bounded (3.372071ms)\\n✔ replay safety and non-temporary conditions (13.351161ms)\\n▶ compatibility and convergence\\n  ✔ 31. unit agents are pinned to the resource and never admit more context than it serves (3.660756ms)\\n  ✔ 32. durable state survives park, wait and resume (398.45481ms)\\n  ✔ 33. completion still requires the original acceptance dependencies (4.679069ms)\\n  ✔ 34. a genuine no-safe-transition blocks with one concrete decision instead of looping (1.711009ms)\\n✔ compatibility and convergence (409.201948ms)\\n▶ provider catalog enrichment (optional)\\n  ✔ gateway /v1/models metadata adds capabilities, context and pool; no serving capacity parks the model (1.717197ms)\\n  ✔ an expired catalog condition is re-checked before work is sent, not rediscovered with a request (2.177808ms)\\n  ✔ one driver per operation: a live holder excludes a second driver; a dead holder's lock is taken over (5.174253ms)\\n  ✔ dependency cycles and unknown references are rejected up front (0.773407ms)\\n  ✔ scheduler decisions are pure over state (no executor needed) (0.532583ms)\\n✔ provider catalog enrichment (optional) (10.997031ms)\\n▶ provider credential boundary\\n  ✔ the stored gateway credential is still sent to its gateway (135.942347ms)\\n  ✔ a foreign provider configured as the endpoint receives no stored credential, even after a 401 (33.479976ms)\\n  ✔ a planner on a foreign provider does not inherit the primary gateway's key (188.222203ms)\\n  ✔ an explicit foreign credential is used only for its own provider; the gateway keeps its own (20.737211ms)\\n✔ provider credential boundary (381.272898ms)\\n✔ storedCredentialFor and mayBindCredential do not follow a HOME changed after the authority was recorded (12.372538ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","create_time":1793229457.95009}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
