n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"Diagnosed PR #311 exact-head terminal-safety test failures and corrected ANSI-aware assertions and PTY timing.\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Definition-first search located the terminal output path. CI evidence showed ANSI styling was incorrectly rejected and the elapsed assertion ran before the one-second status tick. Search results were useful, with some unrelated passages.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test.md -m \"docs(field-report): diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: Diagnosed PR #311 exact-head terminal-safety test failures and corrected ANSI-aware assertions and PTY timing.\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-diagnosed-pr-311-exact-head-terminal-safety-test.md.\"\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":19,"nanos":990690492}},"started_at_ms":1793230904415,"completed_at_ms":1793230924406}}
