{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:56:40.447Z","ordinal":469999,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae28bb647b881a0975391fd99e566b9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Understood. I won’t require another human account. A non-implementing agent can review the code changes; that review accepted the exact PR #311 follow-up diff. This does not replace independent acceptance of the exact release candidate.\n\nI committed the test fixes as `1b934287` and pushed PR #311 at [`8e3bd15`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/8e3bd15037f38517176b0ed057f95d73244dce8e). The focused operation-view and PTY tests passed **30/30** after building the required native artifact. Requirements enforcement also passes on the clean candidate. Node 22/24 CI is still running; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks have passed.\n\nThe broad local suite initially failed because the native artifact was missing and unrelated evaluator/terminal tests lacked prerequisites. After building it, the affected focused tests passed. I’m keeping those broad-suite failures distinct from the focused results.\n\nKimi Code has claimed the held-out corpus lane, but the private corpus store is inaccessible to this account. T2’s legacy validators also cannot be enabled under the current qualification security rules. Fresh custodian validation remains necessary.\n\n**Campaign remains active; acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS. No RC acceptance or release is claimed.**"}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793231798354,"completed_at_ms":1793231800447}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:56:40.457Z","ordinal":470000,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae28bb647b881a0975391fd99e566b9","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Understood. I won’t require another human account. A non-implementing agent can review the code changes; that review accepted the exact PR #311 follow-up diff. This does not replace independent acceptance of the exact release candidate.\n\nI committed the test fixes as `1b934287` and pushed PR #311 at [`8e3bd15`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/8e3bd15037f38517176b0ed057f95d73244dce8e). The focused operation-view and PTY tests passed **30/30** after building the required native artifact. Requirements enforcement also passes on the clean candidate. Node 22/24 CI is still running; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks have passed.\n\nThe broad local suite initially failed because the native artifact was missing and unrelated evaluator/terminal tests lacked prerequisites. After building it, the affected focused tests passed. I’m keeping those broad-suite failures distinct from the focused results.\n\nKimi Code has claimed the held-out corpus lane, but the private corpus store is inaccessible to this account. T2’s legacy validators also cannot be enabled under the current qualification security rules. Fresh custodian validation remains necessary.\n\n**Campaign remains active; acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS. No RC acceptance or release is claimed.**","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","create_time":1793231798.2830977,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae28bb647b881a0975391fd99e566b9","turn_id":"01a184b8-1382-7c51-b7ba-1106ed9497c7","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a184f1-c889-77a3-a6e3-116c8fd6da26","complet