e independent author/custodian is active, for the next checkpoint, or for the authorized custody handoff path. Comment 6479873007; no payloads/answers/private digests requested. Public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance; compatibility blocker remains legacy hidden command format vs blackbox-v1 evaluator. Qualification remains unstarted and protected.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [done] Refresh authoritative release state after Entire review (details=Current authoritative state refreshed 2026-10-28 20:06 UTC. origin/main=13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0; its CI run 40751988282 passed all required jobs. PR300 head f3957a67 and PR309 head aace981b are based on current main with Node22/24 still in progress at last check. PR308 head 2c1b2dfa remains on current base, Node24 succeeded, Node22 still running in run 40757432379. Main rules require Node22, Node24, Linux only and zero approving reviews; Entire Gates (including approval/finding signal) is not a required status check and must not be treated as a human reviewer blocker. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify Nexus host identity is independent of provider/model (details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: cli/src/agent.ts:232 injects explicit Nexus Code host identity and prohibits inferring host from provider/model; cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts covers it. Exact-main CI 40751988282 passed Node22, Node24 and Linux. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify sensitive-checkpoint failure offers operator choices (details=Confirmed on exact current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0: REPL offers read-only, continue without rollback checkpoint, create checkpoint despite sensitive persistence risk, cancel, or re-enter; sidecar reports same options. Tests cover REPL and sidecar; exact-main CI 40751988282 passed all jobs. This is source/CI evidence, not exact-RC qualification.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify upgrade accepts signed GitHub release asset redirect (details=The RC7 failure URL host is now explicitly allowlisted in current origin/main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 only for the expected release-asset path (cli/src/upgrade.ts:665-671). cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts:159 covers a synthetic signed GitHub release URL and unsafe cases remain rejected. Exact-main CI run 40751988282 passed all three jobs. This source check does not replace running `nexus upgrade` on the successor exact RC/package or validate backup-time UX.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [doing] Reconcile doctor D1-D3 report against current main (details=Entire recall plus exact committed origin/main source/test inspection at 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0. D1 appears source-remediated: async opendir/lstat in batches of 128, bounded newest-record parsing, 30s default integrity deadline; committed tests assert event-loop responsiveness, bounded concurrency and deadline. D2 appears source-remediated: index.json is excluded, schema-v2 requires messageLog and rejects messages; schema-v1 keeps messages. D3 has intended distinction: absent /models entry is advisory WARN; --deep performs one inference and upgrades model.available only on success; committed tests cover that exact case. These are committed-source/test evidence, not rerun tests or live reproduction. Next: inspect exact current commit CI/test coverage if needed and reproduce on mike-dev state without altering user data; acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [done] Verify RC7 download redirect rejection against current main (details=Verified main 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0 source/test and tag ancestry. Fix commit 64c22d3e6fc20c36432946abc8e237017d4b91be (2026-10-26 03:17 UTC) accepts the signed GitHub release-assets redirect only on /github-production-release-asset/. Regression coverage added