is not required. Await required checks and merge., updated 9 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] Prepare manual terminal matrix on ubuntu-desktop (details=Fresh SSH at 2026-10-28 21:00 UTC to mike@10.0.8.3 succeeded. loginctl confirms active local session 7, seat0, Remote=no, Type=wayland. xterm XTerm(407), kitty 0.45.0, tmux 3.6, VS Code 1.143.1, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0 are present. No matrix cells executed: exact successor RC is not built/installed. Screenshots remain waived by user; interactive behavior checks remain required.), updated about 3 hours ago\\n  - [doing] Close evaluation coverage gate with independent held-out qualification (details=Fresh Issue #1 check at 2026-10-28 20:24 UTC still OPEN/unassigned; no response to prior metadata-only request at 14:23. Sent a concise follow-up asking whether the independent author/custodian is active, for the next checkpoint, or for the authorized custody handoff path. Comment 6479873007; no payloads/answers/private digests requested. Public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance; compatibility blocker remains legacy hidden command format vs blackbox-v1 evaluator. Qualification remains unstarted and protected.), updated about 4 hours ago\\n  - [doing] Reconcile doctor D1-D3 report against current main (details=Entire recall plus exact committed origin/main source/test inspection at 13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0. D1 appears source-remediated: async opendir/lstat in batches of 128, bounded newest-record parsing, 30s default integrity deadline; committed tests assert event-loop responsiveness, bounded concurrency and deadline. D2 appears source-remediated: index.json is excluded, schema-v2 requires messageLog and rejects messages; schema-v1 keeps messages. D3 has intended distinction: absent /models entry is advisory WARN; --deep performs one inference and upgrades model.available only on success; committed tests cover that exact case. These are committed-source/test evidence, not rerun tests or live reproduction. Ne