{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:15:14.159Z","ordinal":470571,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18502-c6ee-7eb3-a86b-ad0a8ac894b7","author":"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\nPayload:\nAt exact `origin/main` revision `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, issue #1 remains open and unassigned. Its newest comment, #6483900189, says there has been no custodian update and T2/T3/T4 qualification has not started. The current Agent Mail directory has no active custodian identity, and there are no active project windows. I did not access the private store or contact anyone.\n\n**Next action:** the coordinator needs to identify the custodian’s reachable channel and obtain an acknowledged handoff and safe status checkpoint, or assign a named replacement custodian through the established process. Operator authorization for private validation does not identify a contact.\n\nT2 qualification still requires the custodian to convert or replace legacy tasks with isolated `blackbox-v1` validators, repeat custody checks, and record a new immutable manifest identity. Current evaluator code rejects legacy validators for qualification; PR #33’s hardened legacy path is limited to development and pilot use. The public manifest identities—T2: 40 tasks, `50895b84…`; T3: 8 tasks, `85fb9caf…`—do not prove private custody acceptance or qualification."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184ff-559b-7033-aa05-fd38360910ba","create_time":1793232914.1588738}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22373}}
