{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:16:21.705Z","ordinal":470607,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a184ff-559b-7033-aa05-fd38360910ba","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4867d7a1-306a-4578-a2bc-1e93644da27e","process_id":"5905","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --json comments --jq '[.comments[]|select((.body|test(\"custodian|custody\";\"i\")))|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body:(.body|gsub(\"\\\\n\";\" \")|.[0:1000])}]'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --json comments --jq '[.comments[]|select((.body|test(\"custodian|custody\";\"i\")))|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body:(.body|gsub(\"\\\\n\";\" \")|.[0:1000])}]'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.  **Done** - T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined. - T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`). - Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.  **Still open before this can close** 1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record. 2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository \\u0026 Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` \\u0026 `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**  1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**    - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):      - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks      - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks      - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks      - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task      - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task    - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).    - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table i\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity fr\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.  Custodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference so\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**  The public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.  The latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.  Custodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible immutable successor and repeat validation/custody checks, or whether an already-approved compatibility path exists; (3) expected completion/owner; and (\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the v1.0.0 release coordinator: the custody and compatibility gates remain on the release critical path, and there has been no custodian update since the 12:21 UTC request. Please acknowledge whether the independent custodian/replacement author is actively working, identify the responsible role, and provide a current ETA or state that the lane is unavailable. Status only: do not include task identifiers, repository URLs, objectives, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance and a compatible immutable T2 identity. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T15:06:44Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release checkpoint, 2026-10-22 07:56 UTC (public metadata only; no held-out files accessed): exact current `main` remains `8935918455a7fcc9434762712528c1169ec4ff63`. PR #140 now records a 10/10 synthetic host preflight and has exact-head CI running, including the resource containment fixtures; no held-out task has been run. The public T2 identity remains the 40-task manifest previously reported, but custody acceptance and compatibility with the current black-box runner are still unverified here.  Custodian/replacement author: please provide a safe status update only: (1) current assigned owner and whether authoring/validation is active; (2) whether any sealed content changed, and if so the new immutable identity/supersession; (3) whether independent private digest, exposure-history, setup/reference, effective-access, and task/evaluator separation checks are complete; (4) whether an approved runner-compatible immutable T2 successor is underway and its ETA; (5) T3 custody status. Do not \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T07:56:01Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custodian coordination update, current source `main@19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`. PR #145 has integrated the version-synchronized RC2 source candidate; exact post-merge source CI is still running. No held-out payload, private validator, answer, or author log was accessed.  Please reply with safe status metadata only: 1. Who currently owns replacement authorship and independent custody, and are they actively working? 2. Are all 40 tasks fully authored, setup/reference-validated, and independently digested under the sealed manifest, or did task content change? 3. Has the evaluator compatibility issue with the required isolated `blackbox-v1` format been resolved by a custodian-approved immutable version or compatibility path? 4. Has the custodian verified effective store/parent access restrictions and separation from task execution, then accepted custody for qualification?  Do not include payloads, solutions, private validator content, or credentials in this pub\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T14:54:39Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up: the latest T2/T3 custody attestations are from October 18, no current custodian claim or acknowledged handoff is visible, and the current qualification runner rejects T2's legacy `hidden.command` format. No held-out qualification has started.  Please have the current independent custodian confirm, without exposing private material:  - who currently owns authoring and custody, and the claim/handoff reference; - whether the public T2/T3 manifests remain the intended sealed identities or need a versioned successor; - the approved path to resolve T2 runner compatibility, including whether a custodian-led conversion/replacement is in progress and its next checkpoint; - whether fresh setup, reference-validation, access-boundary, and integrity checks can be attested against the accepted execution boundary.  Please do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validators, reference solutions, author logs, credentials, or private digests here. If no custodian is active, pl\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T16:19:34Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).  The current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.  Please answer only as safe status metadata:  1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior? 2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA? 3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaiting custodian-authored replacement?  No task identifiers, objectives, source URLs, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials are needed. Qualification remains closed until custodian \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).  The prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:  - Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane. - Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint. - Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for completeness/coverage, setup and reference validation, payload/validator digest derivation, access controls and author-session independence, without disclosing payloads or answers to implementers. - If t\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.  RC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.  Please provide only safe status metadata: - current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference; - whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA; - whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted; - if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.  Please do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains c\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.  Please reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the current release candidate path (public metadata only): the current evaluator requires the blackbox-v1 task contract, while prior custody records describe the sealed legacy hidden-command corpus. Please confirm the currently assigned custodian, whether the sealed 40-task corpus can be qualified losslessly under the current evaluator or requires a newly versioned corpus, and the expected timing for the required custody acceptance and frozen run metadata. Please do not post task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results, or credentials here. No held-out execution has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public metadata-only follow-up: current `origin/main` is `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; its source CI and CodeQL have passed, and PR #246 is in exact-head CI after rebasing onto that commit. Held-out qualification remains blocked because the latest custody status request has no response.  Please confirm, using metadata only:  1. Who currently owns independent authorship and custody, or whether a formal handoff is needed. 2. Whether the sealed T2 corpus and validators are compatible with the current `blackbox-v1` evaluator contract, or what custodian-led successor path is planned. 3. Whether the required coverage, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, private digest re-derivation, effective access restrictions, and immutable corpus identity have been rechecked for that path. 4. The next expected checkpoint or a concrete blocker requiring operator help.  Please do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validator contents, or private digests here. No held-\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T02:33:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator follow-up (public metadata only; current exact source: `7f52ed1b76e2fa69dee1416d1b13f1e1263ff52d`). PR #252 is integrated; post-merge Node 22/24 jobs pass and Linux package CI is still running.  Held-out qualification remains closed because independent custody has not been confirmed. Please reply with safe metadata only:  1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or confirmation that a formal handoff is needed. 2. Whether all 40 tasks are complete and whether coverage, setup, and reference validation are accepted. 3. Whether private digests, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and separation from task execution have been rechecked and accepted. 4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract or requires a custodian-approved successor version, plus the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.  Do not post prompts, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, cred\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T12:18:17Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator update: source revision `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` is now integrated. Exact-main requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals); version sync confirms all components at `1.0.0-rc.9`. Post-merge CodeQL `40363722565` passed, Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in CI `40363722642` passed, and Linux package/test checks are still running.  Held-out qualification remains closed until designated custody acceptance. Please reply with safe status metadata only:  1. Current independent author and custodian, or whether a formal handoff is needed. 2. Whether all 40 tasks, coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted. 3. Whether private payload/validator integrity, author-session independence and exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted. 4. Whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator, or needs a cu\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T17:37:52Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public metadata update only; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.  Current integration is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On this exact revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; Node 22/24 and CodeQL pass, while Linux CI is still running. The current public held-out manifest is not, by itself, evidence of private custody acceptance. The issue’s opening 4/20 count is historical and should not be read as current corpus progress.  The release remains blocked on an independent custodian confirming the active author/custodian separation, compatibility with the current evaluator contract (including any required replacement and new manifest identity), private payload/validator integrity and provenance, access boundaries, and final custody acceptance. Please identify the current custodian and provide a metadata-only status/next step. Please do not post task payloads, answers, or private validator contents here. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T16:37:30Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public metadata-only update; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.  Current integration is `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. On this exact source, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.  Custody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only: 1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed. 2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted. 3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted. 4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract, or requires a custodian-approved successor version, and the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.  Please do not post task \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.  Please provide safe status metadata only:  1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed. 2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance. 3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required. 4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.  Do not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Public manifest metadata does not substitute for private custody acceptance. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release-critical metadata follow-up (2026-10-28 20:24 UTC): the 14:23 status request remains unanswered and the issue is still unassigned. Please confirm whether the independent author/custodian is actively preparing the corpus and give the next checkpoint. If that owner is unavailable, identify the authorized custody handoff path so this lane can continue without exposing private material. No task payloads, validators, answers, or private digests are requested. Held-out qualification remains unstarted.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T20:25:33Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release qualification contract clarification (2026-10-28): the current exact-source evaluator intentionally rejects in-process legacy hidden validators for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs` qualification check and `eval/run.mjs` hidden-check path). The evaluator documentation explains that those validators share the candidate runtime/workspace and are not safe for independent qualification; the qualification format is the isolated `blackbox-v1` oracle. This is a security boundary, so coordinator changes will not enable legacy hidden commands to make the existing corpus run.  Please confirm the custodian-led path to convert the sealed public task manifest to `blackbox-v1` or produce a newly versioned replacement corpus, then perform private validator/reference checks and re-derive custody digests. Public metadata only is needed here: corpus version/manifest identity, compatibility status, owner/checkpoint, and whether this conversion requires new custody acceptance. No private payloads\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T22:23:50Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Following up on the public custody status only; no private corpus content or answers are requested. The issue remains open and unassigned, and there has been no custodian update since the previous clarification.  Please provide either (1) the independent author/custodian’s current status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus, or (2) the authorized handoff path if that owner is unavailable. Please do not attach task payloads, hidden solutions, or validator contents here.  T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted until the custodian confirms independent authorship, complete coverage, re-derived private integrity checks, isolated setup/reference validation, effective access boundaries, and sealed-manifest acceptance. The public manifest alone is not custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T23:57:25Z\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":532527185}},"started_at_ms":1793232980171,"completed_at_ms":1793232981704}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:16:22.808Z","ordinal":470608,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18503-d318-7741-b4d9-44fede1c43c2","call_id":"call_d2807701027e4cd4aefbc4447a64de12","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6998)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.  **Done** - T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined. - T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`). - Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.  **Still open before this can close** 1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record. 2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository \\u0026 Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` \\u0026 `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**  1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**    - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):      - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks      - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks      - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks      - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task      - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task    - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).    - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table i\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity fr\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.  Custodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference so\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**  The public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.  The latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.  Custodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible imm…3498 tokens truncated…s in CI `40363722642` passed, and Linux package/test checks are still running.  Held-out qualification remains closed until designated custody acceptance. Please reply with safe status metadata only:  1. Current independent author and custodian, or whether a formal handoff is needed. 2. Whether all 40 tasks, coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted. 3. Whether private payload/validator integrity, author-session independence and exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted. 4. Whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator, or needs a cu\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T17:37:52Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public metadata update only; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.  Current integration is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On this exact revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; Node 22/24 and CodeQL pass, while Linux CI is still running. The current public held-out manifest is not, by itself, evidence of private custody acceptance. The issue’s opening 4/20 count is historical and should not be read as current corpus progress.  The release remains blocked on an independent custodian confirming the active author/custodian separation, compatibility with the current evaluator contract (including any required replacement and new manifest identity), private payload/validator integrity and provenance, access boundaries, and final custody acceptance. Please identify the current custodian and provide a metadata-only status/next step. Please do not post task payloads, answers, or private validator contents here. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T16:37:30Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public metadata-only update; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.  Current integration is `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. On this exact source, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.  Custody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only: 1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed. 2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted. 3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted. 4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract, or requires a custodian-approved successor version, and the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.  Please do not post task \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.  Please provide safe status metadata only:  1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed. 2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance. 3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required. 4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.  Do not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Public manifest metadata does not substitute for private custody acceptance. \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release-critical metadata follow-up (2026-10-28 20:24 UTC): the 14:23 status request remains unanswered and the issue is still unassigned. Please confirm whether the independent author/custodian is actively preparing the corpus and give the next checkpoint. If that owner is unavailable, identify the authorized custody handoff path so this lane can continue without exposing private material. No task payloads, validators, answers, or private digests are requested. Held-out qualification remains unstarted.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T20:25:33Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release qualification contract clarification (2026-10-28): the current exact-source evaluator intentionally rejects in-process legacy hidden validators for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs` qualification check and `eval/run.mjs` hidden-check path). The evaluator documentation explains that those validators share the candidate runtime/workspace and are not safe for independent qualification; the qualification format is the isolated `blackbox-v1` oracle. This is a security boundary, so coordinator changes will not enable legacy hidden commands to make the existing corpus run.  Please confirm the custodian-led path to convert the sealed public task manifest to `blackbox-v1` or produce a newly versioned replacement corpus, then perform private validator/reference checks and re-derive custody digests. Public metadata only is needed here: corpus version/manifest identity, compatibility status, owner/checkpoint, and whether this conversion requires new custody acceptance. No private payloads\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T22:23:50Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Following up on the public custody status only; no private corpus content or answers are requested. The issue remains open and unassigned, and there has been no custodian update since the previous clarification.  Please provide either (1) the independent author/custodian’s current status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus, or (2) the authorized handoff path if that owner is unavailable. Please do not attach task payloads, hidden solutions, or validator contents here.  T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted until the custodian confirms independent authorship, complete coverage, re-derived private integrity checks, isolated setup/reference validation, effective access boundaries, and sealed-manifest acceptance. The public manifest alone is not custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T23:57:25Z\"}]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184ff-559b-7033-aa05-fd38360910ba","create_time":1793232982.808137}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
