{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:24:18.603Z","ordinal":470837,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1850b-15ab-7bc0-a1bb-7a367c908d6c","call_id":"call_76427af11bd844cd9b80ca520060b869","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At exact `origin/main` revision `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, issue #1 remains open and unassigned. Its newest comment, #6483900189, says there has been no custodian update and T2/T3/T4 qualification has not started. The current Agent Mail directory has no active custodian identity, and there are no active project windows. I did not access the private store or contact anyone.\\n\\n**Next action:** the coordinator needs to identify the custodian’s reachable channel and obtain an acknowledged handoff and safe status checkpoint, or assign a named replacement custodian through the established process. Operator authorization for private validation does not identify a contact.\\n\\nT2 qualification still requires the custodian to convert or replace legacy tasks with isolated `blackbox-v1` validators, repeat custody checks, and record a new immutable manifest identity. Current evaluator code rejects legacy validators for qualification; PR #33’s hardened legacy path is limited to development and pilot use. The public manifest identities—T2: 40 tasks, `50895b84…`; T3: 8 tasks, `85fb9caf…`—do not prove private custody acceptance or qualification.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1850a-3fe6-78d1-9f07-1fed60ff6ff6","create_time":1793233458.6032834}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
