{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:26:49.890Z","ordinal":470881,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1850d-6487-7543-a0f1-6d05bea053b1","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — exact base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, head `8e3bd15037f38517176b0ed057f95d73244dce8e`. Full diff SHA-256: `d4d6b9d7f85ab4b4b24171ef500e92a0fe30a1bddaf4fcd471708c394df354ee`.\n\n**Finding:** The new corrupt-state error path can inject terminal controls into `nexus run --resume` output. `listTasks` now builds `CorruptStateError` using the task filename and quarantined path at [state.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/cli/src/core/state.ts:1042) and [state.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/cli/src/core/state.ts:1062). The resume handler catches that error and prints `err.message` directly to stderr at [index.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9/cli/src/index.ts:513). A malformed task file with a control-character filename can therefore emit those controls. Sanitize this non-JSON error output, or ensure the error message cannot contain raw path or ID data, and add a regression.\n\nThe earlier acceptance of the `batch_read` fix still applies to that slice. I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1850d-3ac5-7c63-97bb-ed8b070a7d6e","create_time":1793233609.8630846}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22391}}
